#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "open gun safe"
msgstr "枪用保险箱（开）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "open gun safe"
#. ~ Description of furniture "closed gun safe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A large and heavy container with thick metal walls and a rotary combination "
"lock, this is designed to securely store firearms, weapon mods, and "
"ammunition."
msgstr "一个巨大而沉重的容器，有着厚厚的金属壁和旋转式组合锁，能够安全地储存枪械，武器模组和弹药。"

#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "open gun safe"
#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "closed gun safe"
#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "locked gun safe"
#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "jammed gun safe"
#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "electronic gun safe"
#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "safe"
#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "open safe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "screeching metal!"
msgstr "金属撕裂声！"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "closed gun safe"
msgstr "枪用保险箱（关）"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "locked gun safe"
msgstr "枪用保险箱（锁）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "locked gun safe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A large and heavy container with thick metal walls and a rotary combination "
"lock, this is designed to securely store firearms, weapon mods, and "
"ammunition.  If you had something to pick its lock with, you could probably "
"open it."
msgstr "一个巨大而沉重的容器，有着厚厚的金属壁和旋转式组合锁，能够安全地储存枪械，武器模组和弹药。如果有个可以撬开它的锁的工具，你也许可以打开它。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "jammed gun safe"
msgstr "枪用保险箱（已卡死）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "jammed gun safe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A heavy and durable metal safe for storing firearms and ammunition.  "
"Unfortunately, the lock is completely broken, and short of some pretty "
"serious machinery, you have no possible way of opening it."
msgstr "一个用于储存枪械和弹药的坚固耐用的金属保险箱。不幸的是，锁已经完全坏了，而且没有特制的机器，你没可能打开它。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "electronic gun safe"
msgstr "电子枪用保险箱"

#. ~ Description of furniture "electronic gun safe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A large and heavy container with thick metal walls and an electronic locking"
" system, this is designed to securely store firearms, weapon mods, and "
"ammunition.  If you had some way of hacking into it, you could probably "
"crack it open."
msgstr "一个巨大而沉重的容器，有着厚厚的金属壁和电子锁，能够安全地储存枪械，武器模组和弹药。如果有破解电子锁的办法的话，你也许能打开它。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "locker"
msgstr "锁柜"

#. ~ Description of furniture "locker"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A tall sheet metal cabinet, useful for storing just about anything that'll "
"fit."
msgstr "一个高大的金属柜，能储存任何能装下的物品。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "mailbox"
msgstr "邮箱"

#. ~ Description of furniture "mailbox"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A small metal box on top of a wooden post, designed to receive mail "
"deliveries.  Although considering the circumstances, it will likely never "
"see proper use again."
msgstr "一个安装在木桩上的金属小盒子，用来接收邮件。不过考虑到现在的情况，它很可能再也用不上了。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "clothing rail"
msgstr "挂衣杆"

#. ~ Description of furniture "clothing rail"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A metal frame on a set of wheels used for hanging large amounts of clothes."
"  Usually used in theater or retail environments, it's easy to use and quick"
" to access."
msgstr "一个底下带有滚轮的金属框架，能挂上大量衣物。通常用于剧院或购物场所，它易于使用而且很方便。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "display rack"
msgstr "展架"

#. ~ Description of furniture "display rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A sheet metal shelving unit, with the storage surfaces angled in such a way "
"as to show off the items stored."
msgstr "一个由金属板制成的货架，上面放货品的金属板略微向外倾斜，能更好地展示所放置的商品。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "locked display rack"
msgstr "展架（锁）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "locked display rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A sheet metal shelving unit, with the storage surfaces angled in such a way "
"as to show off the items stored.  Metal fasteners with a lock hold the items"
" securely to the rack."
msgstr "一个由金属板制成的货架，上面放货品的金属板略微向外倾斜，能更好地展示所放置的商品。带锁的金属闩将物品牢牢固定在展示架中。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "wooden rack"
msgstr "木架"

#. ~ Description of furniture "wooden rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A wooden shelving unit with angled storage surfaces designed to show off "
"whatever is stored on it."
msgstr "一个由木板制成的货架，上面放货品的木板略微向外倾斜，能更好地展示所放置的商品。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "coat rack"
msgstr "衣帽架"

#. ~ Description of furniture "coat rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A tall wooden pole with a set of hooks used to store outdoor jackets and "
"hats to allow easy access."
msgstr "一根高高的木杆，上面有许多钩子，用来存放户外夹克和帽子，以便随时取用。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "recycle bin"
msgstr "可回收垃圾箱"

#. ~ Description of furniture "recycle bin"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A large plastic bin painted green with a 'recycle' symbol emblazoned on it."
"  While intended to store discarded things to be processed back into a "
"factory, the drastic change in priorities as of late means that these may "
"hold valuable materials."
msgstr ""
"一个被漆成绿色的大塑料桶，上面印有“可回收”的符号。虽然它是用来存放准备被送回工厂处理的废弃物的，但最近发生的剧变意味着它可能存放着对你很有价值的材料。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "safe"
msgstr "保险箱"

#. ~ Description of furniture "safe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A small, heavy, and near-unbreachable metal box with a rotary combination "
"lock.  Although, this isn't actually locked, just closed."
msgstr "一个笨重的完全无法被强行打开的小型金属箱子，上面有个旋转式组合锁。不过，它并不是真的被锁上了，只是关上了。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "safe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A small, heavy, and near-unbreachable metal box with a rotary combination "
"lock.  With something to listen really closely and a hell of a lot of time, "
"you might be able to crack it."
msgstr "一个笨重的完全无法被强行打开的小型金属箱子，上面有个旋转式组合锁。如果找来能仔细听它声音的工具，并花上很多时间，你也许能打开它。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "open safe"
msgstr "保险箱（开）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "open safe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A small, heavy, and near-unbreachable metal box with a rotary combination "
"lock, albeit significantly less secure with the door open."
msgstr "一个笨重的完全无法被强行打开的小型金属箱子，上面有个旋转式组合锁。它的门现在开着，里面的东西可不保险了。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "trash can"
msgstr "垃圾桶"

#. ~ Description of furniture "trash can"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A plastic bin for storing discarded waste as to be disposed of later.  "
"Although, considering the circumstances, it might be worth seeing what's "
"inside."
msgstr "一个塑料垃圾桶，用于储存垃圾，以便后续丢弃处理。不过，考虑到现在的情况，也许值得看看里面装着什么。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "metal trash can"
msgstr "金属垃圾桶"

#. ~ Description of furniture "metal trash can"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "A crude metal bin typically used to dispose of waste."
msgstr "一个粗糙的金属桶，通常用于垃圾处理。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "wardrobe"
msgstr "大衣柜"

#. ~ Description of furniture "wardrobe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A very large wooden cabinet for storing clothes, effectively an upright "
"closet.  Could technically be used to store anything else that would fit, "
"though."
msgstr "一个非常大的存放衣物的木制柜子，实际上是一个直立的壁橱。当然理论上也可以用来存储其他任何能装下的物品。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "filing cabinet"
msgstr "档案柜"

#. ~ Description of furniture "filing cabinet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A rack of metal drawers designed to hold various files and paperwork.  "
"Paperwork that has more than likely lost all worth or value by now."
msgstr "一个用来存放各种文件档案的金属抽屉架。现在看，里面的文档应该早就没有了任何价值。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "utility shelf"
msgstr "实用货架"

#. ~ Description of furniture "utility shelf"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A simple heavy-duty plastic and metal shelving unit, intended to store tools"
" and materials for easy access to workers."
msgstr "一个简单耐用的由塑料和金属制成的货架，用来存储工具和材料，便于工人们使用。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "warehouse shelf"
msgstr "仓库货架"

#. ~ Description of furniture "warehouse shelf"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A huge, sturdy steel shelf for storing pallets of crates in warehouses."
msgstr "一个由钢材制成的巨大而坚固的货架，用于在仓库中存放货盘和板条箱。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "wooden keg"
msgstr "大木桶"

#. ~ Description of furniture "wooden keg"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A large standing wooden barrel, completely watertight.  Good for storing "
"liquids of all kinds."
msgstr "一个立起来的大木桶，完全水密。适合贮存各种液体。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "display case"
msgstr "展柜"

#. ~ Description of furniture "display case"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A secure wooden case at about waist-height, with glass panelling on the top."
"  Useful for storing valuable things while still showing them off.  Not "
"actually as secure as it looks, as the display windows are easily broken."
msgstr "一个稳固的木柜，约与腰部同高，顶部镶嵌着一片玻璃板。用来存放贵重的物品，同时展示它们。实际上并不像看上去那么安全，因为展示窗很容易被打碎。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "open display case"
msgstr "展柜（开）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "open display case"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A secure wooden case at about waist-height, with glass panelling on the top."
"  Useful for storing valuable things while still showing them off.  Not "
"actually as secure as it looks, as the display windows are easily broken.  "
"This one has had its lock picked and is open."
msgstr ""
"一个稳固的木柜，约与腰部同高，顶部镶嵌着一片玻璃板。用来存放贵重的物品，同时展示它们。实际上并不像看上去那么安全，因为展示窗很容易被打碎。它的锁被撬开了，已经打开了。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "broken display case"
msgstr "展柜（损坏）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "broken display case"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A secure wooden case at about waist-height, with glass panelling on the top."
"  Would be useful for storing valuable things while still showing them off, "
"if the glass hadn't been shattered.  Careful not to cut yourself when "
"looting."
msgstr ""
"一个稳固的木柜，约与腰部同高，顶部镶嵌着一片玻璃板。原本用来存放贵重的物品，同时展示它们，不过玻璃已经被人砸碎了。在洗劫的时候小心不要割伤自己。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "fireman's cabinet"
msgstr "消防柜"

#. ~ Description of furniture "fireman's cabinet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A metallic cabinet painted to stand out, visibly holding tools behind a thin"
" panel of tempered glass."
msgstr "一个漆成鲜亮颜色的金属柜子，在一块薄薄的钢化玻璃板后面放着显眼的消防工具。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "unlocked fireman's cabinet"
msgstr "消防柜（解锁）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "unlocked fireman's cabinet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A metallic cabinet painted to stand out.  Its glass panel door was left "
"unlocked and slightly ajar."
msgstr "一个漆成鲜亮颜色的金属柜子。它的玻璃门没有上锁，略微敞开。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "open fireman's cabinet"
msgstr "消防柜（开）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "open fireman's cabinet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A metallic cabinet painted to stand out.  Its protective glass panel lies "
"broken from some past emergency or looting attempt."
msgstr "一个漆成鲜亮颜色的金属柜子。它用于防护的玻璃门因过去所发生的紧急情况或抢劫企图而碎裂开来。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "standing tank"
msgstr "储存罐"

#. ~ Description of furniture "standing tank"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A huge metal tank that can be used to safely store large amounts of liquid."
msgstr "一个巨大的金属容器，可以用来安全地储存大量液体。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "fuel tank"
msgstr "油罐"

#. ~ Description of furniture "fuel tank"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "A tank filled with gasoline."
msgstr "一个装满汽油的油箱。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "broken fuel tank"
msgstr "油罐（损坏）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "broken fuel tank"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "A broken tank which was filled with gasoline."
msgstr "一个曾经装满汽油的坏油箱。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "fuel tank"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "A tank filled with diesel."
msgstr "一个装满柴油的油箱。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "broken fuel tank"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "A broken tank which was filled with diesel."
msgstr "一个曾经装满柴油的坏油箱。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Snippet in category "<name_b>"
#. ~ generic negative/hostile pronouns
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/json/npcs/talk_tags.json
msgid "dumpster"
msgstr "垃圾箱"

#. ~ Description of furniture "dumpster"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A large metal dumpster that will likely not be getting picked up by the "
"city's waste management any time soon.  Despite the unpleasant nature of "
"climbing inside, it could make for a viable hiding spot."
msgstr "一个大型金属垃圾箱，再也不会被城市的垃圾处理部门回收了。尽管一想到爬进它就会让你不舒服，但它还是可以勉强成为一处藏身之地。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "butter churn"
msgstr "黄油搅拌机"

#. ~ Description of furniture "butter churn"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A metal tube with a built-in mixer for making butter.  Rather than needing "
"electricity, it is pedal-driven, allowing use without power."
msgstr "一根用来制造黄油的内置搅拌器的金属罐子。它不需要电，而是靠踏板驱动，让你能在停电时使用。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "riveted metal crate"
msgstr "铆接金属板条箱"

#. ~ Description of furniture "riveted metal crate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"This huge box is made of a dull metal, riveted together.  There is no "
"obvious opening mechanism, and the rivets don't match any of your tools.  "
"The only way in would be to smash it."
msgstr "这个大箱子是用某种光泽暗淡的金属板铆接在一起的。没有明显的开启机制，它所使用的铆钉与你的任何工具都不匹配。开启它的唯一办法就是把它砸碎。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "sealed metal crate"
msgstr "金属板条箱（密封）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "sealed metal crate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"This is a huge, tightly sealed storage crate made from welded and riveted "
"sheet metal.  The sealing mechanism is too tight to open bare-handed and "
"would need some kind of prying instrument to release."
msgstr "这是一个巨大的密封储存板条箱，由某种金属板焊接铆接制成。它的密封机构结合非常紧密，无法徒手打开，需要某种撬棍工具才能打开。"

#. ~ Prying action message of furniture "sealed metal crate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "You wrench open the metal crate."
msgstr "你撬开了金属板条箱。"

#. ~ Prying failure message of furniture "sealed metal crate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "The lid is sealed more tightly than you thought."
msgstr "它的盖子比你想象的要密封得更紧。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "open metal crate"
msgstr "金属板条箱（开）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "open metal crate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"This large metal crate’s lid is unsealed, and hinges open easily to reveal a"
" number of storage shelves inside.  Once open, the side panels also swing "
"wider for easy access."
msgstr "这个大的金属板条箱的盖子已经打开了，盖子上的铰链打开后，显露出内部的许多储藏架。一旦打开，它的侧面板也会旋转变得更宽，以便于存取物品。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "wooden chest"
msgstr "木箱"

#. ~ Description of furniture "wooden chest"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A sealed wooden storage container.  Lacking any labels, it could hold just "
"about anything inside.  It has a simple metal latch."
msgstr "一个密封的木箱。没有任何标签，任何东西都可能被存在它里面。它正面有个简单的闩锁。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "metal foot locker"
msgstr "金属床脚柜"

#. ~ Description of furniture "metal foot locker"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A metal storage box, capable of holding any number of things.  The lid has a"
" small lock."
msgstr "一种能下装很多东西的金属箱子。它的盖子上有一把小锁。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "counter"
msgstr "柜台"

#. ~ Description of furniture "counter"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "Affixed to the wall or found in kitchens or stores."
msgstr "一个装在墙上、厨房里或是商店中的常见柜子。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "cupboard"
msgstr "橱柜"

#. ~ Description of furniture "cupboard"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "Store your cups."
msgstr "一个用于储存餐具的柜子。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "closed counter gate"
msgstr "柜台门（关）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "closed counter gate"
#. ~ Description of furniture "open counter gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid ""
"A commercial quality swinging door made of wood that allows passage behind "
"counters."
msgstr "一扇商用等级的弹簧门，用木头制成，让人能进出柜台后面。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "open counter gate"
msgstr "柜台门（开）"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "desk"
msgstr "书桌"

#. ~ Description of furniture "desk"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "Sit down at it or work on it."
msgstr "一个供书写或阅读用的桌子。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#: data/json/items/vehicle/tables.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "workbench"
msgid_plural "workbenches"
msgstr[0] "工作台"

#. ~ Description of furniture "workbench"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid ""
"A sturdy workbench built out of metal.  It is perfect for crafting large and"
" heavy things."
msgstr "一个用金属制成的坚固的工作台。它非常适合用来制造巨大而沉重的物品。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "leather tarp"
msgid_plural "leather tarps"
msgstr[0] "防水皮革"

#. ~ Description of furniture "leather tarp"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid ""
"A large sheet of sewn leather that can be used instead of a picnic blanket, "
"but it's more valuable as a butchery appliance as it does not soak in blood."
msgstr "一大块缝制的皮革，可以用来代替野餐毯子，但用作屠宰工具更有价值，因为它不会渗血。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "plastic groundsheet"
msgstr "塑料防潮布"

#. ~ Description of furniture "plastic groundsheet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid ""
"A large sheet of thick plastic has been tossed on the ground here.  It would"
" be a useful place to do some butchery, perhaps."
msgstr "地上铺着一大块厚塑料防潮垫，也许这是一个屠宰的好地方。"

#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "plastic groundsheet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "whuff!"
msgstr "沙咔！"

#. ~ Bashing failed sound of furniture "plastic groundsheet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "crinkle."
msgstr "沙沙。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "fiber mat"
msgid_plural "fiber mats"
msgstr[0] "纤维垫"

#. ~ Description of furniture "fiber mat"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid ""
"A large mat woven from fibrous material that can be used instead of a picnic"
" blanket, but it's more valuable as a butchery appliance.  Too thin to be a "
"comfortable sleeping place."
msgstr "一种由纤维材料编织而成的大垫子，可代替野餐毯，但用作屠宰工具更有价值。因为太薄不能作为舒适的睡眠场所。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ values based on real world collapsible camping table
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "folding table"
msgid_plural "folding tables"
msgstr[0] "折叠桌"

#. ~ Description of furniture "folding table"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid ""
"Small metal folding table, ideal for off-road trips into the wild.  Can be "
"used as a workbench in a pinch."
msgstr "一个小型金属可折叠餐桌，适合野外郊游时使用。紧急情况下可以当作工作台。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "table"
msgstr "桌子"

#. ~ Description of furniture "table"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "Sit down when you eat!"
msgstr "一个可以在上面放东西、做事情、吃饭、写字、工作等的常用家具。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "table"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "a low table for livingrooms."
msgstr "客厅用的矮桌。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "metal table"
msgstr "金属桌"

#. ~ Description of furniture "metal table"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "A serviceable but simple table made of scrap metal."
msgstr "一张用金属废料制成的既实用又简单的桌子。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "tatami mat"
msgstr "榻榻米"

#. ~ Description of furniture "tatami mat"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A tatami is a type of mat used as a flooring material in traditional "
"Japanese-style rooms."
msgstr "榻榻米，传统日式房间中铺在地板上的垫子。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "pillow fort"
msgstr "枕头堡垒"

#. ~ Description of furniture "pillow fort"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A comfy place to hide from the world.  Not very defensible, though."
msgstr "一处能让你暂时逃避残酷现实的舒适空间。但不是很坚固。"

#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "pillow fort"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "paf!"
msgstr "噗！"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "cardboard fort"
msgstr "纸箱城堡"

#. ~ Description of furniture "cardboard fort"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A fort built by tipping a cardboard box on its side, lining it with "
"blankets, and partly weather sealing it with a plastic sheet."
msgstr "纸盒子堆叠成的“堡垒”，以毛毯衬里，部分屋顶被塑料薄膜盖住。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "cardboard wall"
msgstr "纸板墙"

#. ~ Description of furniture "cardboard wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"This is a pile of cardboard boxes that have been filled with rags and junk "
"and stacked together like bricks to form a wall."
msgstr "这是一堆纸板盒，装满了破布和垃圾，像砖块一样堆放在一起，形成了一堵墙。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "cardboard floor"
msgstr "纸箱地板"

#. ~ Description of furniture "cardboard floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A flat floor made of sheets of cardboard duct-taped together overtop a "
"plastic sheet."
msgstr "一块平坦的地板，由粘在塑料板上的纸板箱制成。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "cardboard roof"
msgstr "纸箱屋顶"

#. ~ Description of furniture "cardboard roof"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A sloped roof made of cardboard boxes, stuffed with scrap cardboard and "
"paper and layered atop each other.  Sheets of plastic are carefully arrayed "
"on top to shed water.  It looks like it could last a season or two at least "
"before crumbling."
msgstr ""
"一块倾斜的屋顶，由纸板箱制成，里面塞满了叠在一起的废纸板和纸屑。一块块塑料板被小心地排列在顶部来排水。看起来它在彻底倒塌前至少可以撑过一两个季节。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "cardboard door"
msgstr "纸箱门"

#. ~ Description of furniture "cardboard door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"This is a pile of cardboard boxes that have been filled with rags and junk "
"and stacked together like bricks to form a wall.  The largest box has been "
"cut open and folded to form a makeshift door, which is open."
msgstr "一堆里面塞满了破布和垃圾的纸板箱，像砖块一样堆在一起形成了一堵墙。最大的箱子被切开并折叠起来，形成一扇打开的简易门。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "cardboard door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"This is a pile of cardboard boxes that have been filled with rags and junk "
"and stacked together like bricks to form a wall.  The largest box has been "
"cut open and folded to form a makeshift door, which is closed."
msgstr "一堆里面塞满了破布和垃圾的纸板箱，像砖块一样堆在一起形成了一堵墙。最大的箱子被切开并折叠起来，形成一扇关闭的简易门。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "beaded curtain"
msgstr "珠帘"

#. ~ Description of furniture "beaded curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "This beaded curtain could be pulled aside."
msgstr "这珠子门帘可以拉到一边。"

#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "beaded curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "clickity clack… clack… clack"
msgstr "咔嗒…咔嗒…咔嗒…"

#. ~ Bashing failed sound of furniture "beaded curtain"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of furniture "open beaded curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "clickity clack… clack"
msgstr "咔嗒…咔嗒…"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "open beaded curtain"
msgstr "珠帘（开）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "open beaded curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "This beaded curtain has been pulled aside."
msgstr "这珠子门帘已经拉到一边了。"

#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "open beaded curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "clickity clack… clack… clack!"
msgstr "咔嗒…咔嗒…咔嗒！"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "canvas floor"
msgstr "帆布地板"

#. ~ Description of furniture "canvas floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"Flooring made out of stretched, waterproof cloth.  Helps keep the dirt out "
"of the tent."
msgstr "地板由拉伸的防水布制成。有助于防止灰尘进入帐篷。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "canvas wall"
msgstr "帆布墙"

#. ~ Description of furniture "canvas wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A wall made of stretched, waterproof cloth."
msgstr "一种由拉伸的防水布制成的墙。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "canvas wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A wall made of stretched, heavy-duty, waterproof cloth."
msgstr "由拉伸的重型防水布制成的墙。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "canvas flap"
msgstr "帆布门帘"

#. ~ Description of furniture "canvas flap"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "This canvas flap door could be pulled aside."
msgstr "这扇帆布门帘可以拉到一边。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "open canvas flap"
msgstr "帆布门帘（开）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "open canvas flap"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "This canvas flap door has been pulled aside."
msgstr "这扇帆布门帘已被拉开。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "canvas flap"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "This heavy canvas flap door could be pulled aside."
msgstr "这扇厚重的帆布门帘可以拉到一边。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "open canvas flap"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "This heavy canvas flap door has been pulled aside."
msgstr "这扇厚重的帆布门帘已被拉开。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "groundsheet"
msgstr "防潮布"

#. ~ Description of furniture "groundsheet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "This plastic groundsheet could keep you dry."
msgstr "这个塑料防潮布能让你保持干燥。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "groundsheet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "This large plastic groundsheet could keep you dry."
msgstr "这个大塑料防潮布能让你保持干燥。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "groundsheet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"This plastic government-issue groundsheet could keep you dry, but was made "
"by the lowest bidder."
msgstr "这个塑料政府发行的防潮布可以让你保持干燥，但它是由出价最低的投标者制造的。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "animalskin wall"
msgstr "兽皮墙"

#. ~ Description of furniture "animalskin wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "Wall made out of animal skin.  Either an amazing or horrifying sight."
msgstr "用兽皮制成的墙面。不知该称它为惊奇还是惊吓。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "animalskin flap"
msgstr "兽皮门帘"

#. ~ Description of furniture "animalskin flap"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "This animal skin flap could be pulled aside."
msgstr "这扇兽皮门帘可以拉到一边。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "open animalskin flap"
msgstr "兽皮门帘（开）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "open animalskin flap"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "This animal skin flap has been pulled aside."
msgstr "这扇兽皮门帘已被拉开。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "animalskin floor"
msgstr "兽皮地板"

#. ~ Description of furniture "animalskin floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "This animal skin groundsheet could keep you dry."
msgstr "这个动物皮防潮布可以让你保持干燥。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "pile of rubble"
msgstr "瓦砾"

#. ~ Description of furniture "pile of rubble"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"Pile of various metals, bricks, and other building materials.  You could "
"clear it with a shovel."
msgstr "一堆各式废金属、砖块和其他建筑材料。你可以用铲子把它清理干净。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "pile of rocky rubble"
msgstr "石砾"

#. ~ Description of furniture "pile of rocky rubble"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "Pile of rocks.  Useless?"
msgstr "一堆石头。没什么用？"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "pile of trashy rubble"
msgstr "垃圾碎砾"

#. ~ Description of furniture "pile of trashy rubble"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"Trash topped with dirt and grass, it smells gross, but another man's trash…"
msgstr "一堆垃圾和泥土青草混在一起，味道很让人恶心，不过常言道：\"一个人的垃圾是……\""

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "metal wreckage"
msgstr "金属残骸"

#. ~ Description of furniture "metal wreckage"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "Pile of various bent and twisted metals."
msgstr "一堆各种各样的弯曲变形的废金属。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "radioactive slag"
msgstr "放射性炉渣"

#. ~ Description of furniture "radioactive slag"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A pile of melted slag from a destroyed nuclear reactor.  What are you doing "
"looking at this?  Get the hell out of here, you nutcase!"
msgstr "一堆被摧毁的核反应堆的熔渣。你还盯着这个看什么？赶紧跑啊，你这个疯子！"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "pile of ash"
msgstr "灰烬"

#. ~ Description of furniture "pile of ash"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "Some ash, from wood or possibly bodies."
msgstr "一堆木头或尸体焚烧后留下的灰烬。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "small boulder"
msgstr "小圆石"

#. ~ Description of furniture "small boulder"
#. ~ Description of furniture "small rock candy boulder"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#: data/mods/My_Sweet_Cataclysm/sweet_furniture.json
msgid ""
"Blocking your path.  Should be easy to move.  It can be used as a primitive "
"anvil."
msgstr "一块小圆石，重量一般。可以当作简易铁砧使用。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "medium boulder"
msgstr "中圆石"

#. ~ Description of furniture "medium boulder"
#. ~ Description of furniture "medium rock candy boulder"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#: data/mods/My_Sweet_Cataclysm/sweet_furniture.json
msgid ""
"Blocking your path.  It'll be a struggle to move.  It can be used as a "
"primitive anvil."
msgstr "一块比小圆石大很多的砾石，重量较大。可以当作简易铁砧使用。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "large boulder"
msgstr "大圆石"

#. ~ Description of furniture "large boulder"
#. ~ Description of furniture "large rock candy boulder"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#: data/mods/My_Sweet_Cataclysm/sweet_furniture.json
msgid "Now how are you going to move this?"
msgstr "一块巨大的砾石，重量同样巨大。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "street light"
msgstr "路灯"

#. ~ Description of furniture "street light"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"Raised source of light which used to illuminate streets and their "
"surrounding area, but it's useless without electricity."
msgstr "曾经被高高架起用来照亮街道四周的路灯，但是没有供电后它毫无用途。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "traffic light"
msgstr "交通信号灯"

#. ~ Description of furniture "traffic light"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"Signaling device positioned at road intersections and pedestrian crossings "
"to control flows of traffic, but it's useless without electricity."
msgstr "设置在道路交叉口和人行横道的用来指挥交通的信号装置，但是没有供电后它毫无用途。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "flagpole"
msgstr "旗杆"

#. ~ Description of furniture "flagpole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A 6m high metal flagpole.  You could hoist up a flag here."
msgstr "一根6米高的金属旗杆。你可以在这里升旗。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "flagpole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A 5m high wooden flagpole.  You could hoist up a flag here."
msgstr "一根5米高的木质旗杆。你可以在这里升旗。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "utility pole"
msgstr "电线杆"

#. ~ Description of furniture "utility pole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A long wooden post which used to support overhead power lines and other "
"public utilities, but it doesn't work anymore."
msgstr "一根用来支撑架空输电线和其他公共设施的长木桩，但是没有供电后它毫无用途。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "scrap metal bridge"
msgstr "金属废料桥"

#. ~ Description of furniture "scrap metal bridge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A simple bridge made of riveted sheet metal."
msgstr "一座由铆接金属板制成的简易桥梁。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting "fbmw_2_common_1"
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting "fbmw_2_common_smithy_2"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/recipes/basecamps/expansion/recipe_modular_workshop/version_2/recipe_modular_workshop_common.json
msgid "forge"
msgstr "锻炉"

#. ~ Description of furniture "forge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "Metalworking station typically used in combination with an anvil."
msgstr "一个一般和铁砧搭配使用的金属加工装置。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "Cody's forge"
msgstr "科迪的锻炉"

#. ~ Description of furniture "Cody's forge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"Metalworking station typically used in combination with an anvil.  You can "
"see pipes running into the walls."
msgstr "一个常同铁砧搭配使用的金属加工装置。你可以看到各种管道穿墙而过。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "anvil"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "Used in metalworking."
msgstr "用于金属锻造。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "still"
msgid_plural "stills"
msgstr[0] "蒸馏器"

#. ~ Description of furniture "still"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"An essential component for brewing and chemistry that allows for refining "
"liquid mixtures."
msgstr "一个酿造业和化工业所必不可少的能够精炼液体混合物的重要设备。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "screw press"
msgid_plural "screw presses"
msgstr[0] "螺旋压榨机"

#. ~ Description of furniture "screw press"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A large screw press for the purpose of manually pressing oil out of fruit or"
" seed paste.  The paste gets placed in wetted bags and gets pressed down by "
"the force of the screw mechanism."
msgstr "一种大型螺旋压榨机，用于手动从果实或种子糊中榨油。糊状物料被放入湿袋子中，并通过螺旋机构的力量向下挤压。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "charcoal kiln"
msgid_plural "charcoal kilns"
msgstr[0] "炭窑（空）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "charcoal kiln"
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled charcoal kiln"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A rock kiln designed to burn wood and organic material into charcoal in "
"absence of oxygen."
msgstr "一个用于制造木炭的石头炉子，将木头材质或其他有机材料在缺氧环境下燃烧制成木炭。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "filled charcoal kiln"
msgid_plural "filled charcoal kilns"
msgstr[0] "炭窑（满）"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "metal charcoal kiln"
msgstr "金属炭窑（空）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "metal charcoal kiln"
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled metal charcoal kiln"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A metal kiln designed to burn wood and organic material into charcoal in "
"absence of oxygen."
msgstr "一个用于制造木炭的金属炉子，将木头材质或其他有机材料在缺氧环境下燃烧制成木炭。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "filled metal charcoal kiln"
msgstr "金属炭窑（满）"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json data/json/obsoletion/obsolete_fake.json
msgid "arc furnace"
msgid_plural "arc furnaces"
msgstr[0] "电弧炉"

#. ~ Description of furniture "arc furnace"
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled arc furnace"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"An arc furnace designed to burn a powdery mix of coke and limestone to "
"create calcium carbide."
msgstr "一个用于煅烧粉末状焦炭石灰混合物来制取电石的电弧炉。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "filled arc furnace"
msgstr "电弧炉（满）"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/obsoletion/obsolete_fake.json
msgid "smoking rack"
msgid_plural "smoking racks"
msgstr[0] "烟熏架"

#. ~ Description of furniture "smoking rack"
#. ~ Description of furniture "metal smoking rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A special rack designed to smoke food for better preservation and taste.  "
"Works as a charcoal smoker in crafting recipes."
msgstr "一个特制的用来熏制食物的架子，熏制食物能够长期保存，而且风味更佳。在制作物品时可当作木炭烤架的替代品使用。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json
msgid "spinning wheel"
msgid_plural "spinning wheels"
msgstr[0] "纺车"

#. ~ Description of furniture "spinning wheel"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"Large wooden device with a mechanical wheel used to combine fibers together "
"into a stronger material."
msgstr "一个带有机械滚轮的大型木制装置，用于将纤维纺织在一起形成更坚固的材料。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json
msgid "stationary scutcher"
msgid_plural "stationary scutchers"
msgstr[0] "打麻机"

#. ~ Description of furniture "stationary scutcher"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"Bulky simple-hinged wooden device to break up the hard parts of fibre "
"plants, with nail combs on the back for separating them out."
msgstr "一台笨重的简易铰链木制装置，用于分解植物纤维中坚硬部分，背部有个钉梳，用来将纤维分开。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "active smoking rack"
msgstr "烟熏架（点燃）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "active smoking rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A special rack designed to smoke food for better preservation and taste.  It"
" is lit and smoking."
msgstr "一个特制的用来熏制食物的架子，熏制食物能够长期保存，而且风味更佳。它已经被点燃，正在熏制食物。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "metal smoking rack"
msgid_plural "metal smoking racks"
msgstr[0] "金属烟熏架"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "active metal smoking rack"
msgstr "金属烟熏架（点燃）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "active metal smoking rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A special rack designed to smoke food for better preservation and taste."
msgstr "一个特制的用来熏制食物的架子，熏制食物能够长期保存，而且风味更佳。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ All these fake objects may be referenced by preexisting base camps and
#. expansions, and so may have to remain for quite some time after their
#. obsolescence during the 0.E cycle
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/obsoletion/obsolete_fake.json
msgid "rock forge"
msgid_plural "rock forges"
msgstr[0] "石头锻炉"

#. ~ Description of furniture "rock forge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"Metalworking station made of rock, typically used in combination with an "
"anvil.  Works as a charcoal forge in crafting recipes."
msgstr "一个石头搭建的一般和铁砧搭配使用的金属加工装置。在制作物品时可当作木炭锻炉的替代品使用。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/obsoletion/obsolete_fake.json
msgid "clay kiln"
msgid_plural "clay kilns"
msgstr[0] "砖窑"

#. ~ Description of furniture "clay kiln"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "A kiln designed to bake clay pottery and bricks."
msgstr "一个用来烧制各类陶制器具和砖块的炉子。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "wooden stepladder"
msgid_plural "wooden stepladders"
msgstr[0] "木梯"

#. ~ Description of furniture "wooden stepladder"
#. ~ Description of furniture "aluminum stepladder"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A short, foldable ladder.  Can help you climb to a rooftop, or maybe slow "
"something down."
msgstr "一种可折叠的短梯子。可以帮助你爬到屋顶，或者作为障碍物减慢他人的速度。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "aluminum stepladder"
msgid_plural "aluminum stepladders"
msgstr[0] "铝梯"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json
msgid "electric arc furnace"
msgid_plural "electric arc furnaces"
msgstr[0] "电弧炉"

#. ~ Description of furniture "electric arc furnace"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"Not the kind of furnace you'd heat your house with, this is a device for "
"heating things to extreme temperatures as part of industrial fabrication "
"processes.  Can be used in recipes instead of forge, when supplied with "
"power from UPS."
msgstr "这不是你用来为房间供暖的那种炉子，这是一种把东西加热到极高温度的设备，是工业制造过程的其中一环。当使用UPS供电时，可用来替代锻铁炉。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Based on the Beverly B-2 Throatless Shear, 10 gauge capacity - as was
#. furniture - values based on real world Beverly B-2 Throatless Shear
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "Beverly shear"
msgid_plural "Beverly shears"
msgstr[0] "旋剪机"

#. ~ Description of furniture "Beverly shear"
#. ~ Based on the Beverly B-2 Throatless Shear, 10 gauge capacity - as was
#. furniture - values based on real world Beverly B-2 Throatless Shear
#. ~ Description of "Beverly shear"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid ""
"A massive bench-mounted device with a short guillotine blade mounted to a "
"long lever.  Designed for making straight or curved cuts through sheet metal"
" up to 3 millimeters thick."
msgstr "一台巨大的安装在长凳上的机器，较短的旋转铡刀安装在一根长杠杆上。设计用来对最高厚度达3毫米的金属板进行直线或曲线切割。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "drill press"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A powerful drill mounted on a slide that lets it drop precisely down.  "
"Useful in all kinds of projects from industrial fabrication to home "
"woodworking.  You can take this down and plug it into your own power grid to"
" use it."
msgstr "一台安装在滑轨上的强力钻机，可以用它精确钻孔。可用于从工业制造到家庭木工的各种工作。可以拆卸下来接入电源使用。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "firefly terrarium"
msgstr "萤火虫玻璃盆栽"

#. ~ Description of furniture "firefly terrarium"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"While many survivors would have focused on trying to bring back electric "
"lights, whomever lives here has apparently decided to make use of the "
"changes wrought by the Cataclysm to provide light.  This vivarium contains "
"soil, strange plants you don't recognize immediately, and most strikingly, a"
" giant mutant firefly."
msgstr ""
"虽然许多幸存者专注于尝试恢复电力照明，但住在这里的，不管是谁，显然都决定利用大灾变带来的变化提供光源。这个生态箱里包含了土壤、难以辨认的陌生植物，还有最引人注目的，一只巨大的变异萤火虫。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "table saw"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A rotating sawblade set into a large flat table, for making straight "
"measured cuts, a key tool in any carpenter's arsenal.  You can take this "
"down and plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr "一台安装在大平台上的旋锯，能够笔直切割出精确的直线，各类木工设备中的关键利器之一。可以拆卸下来接入电源使用。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "mitre saw"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A circular sawblade on an arm that can slide and rotate in several "
"directions, this is a staple tool for nearly any carpentry.  You can take "
"this down and plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr "一台安装在机械臂上的圆锯，可以在多个方向上滑动旋转，是木匠的标配工具。可以拆卸下来接入电源使用。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "band saw"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A ribbonlike sawblade runs in a single direction in this tool, allowing "
"precise cuts at almost any angle.  You can take this down and plug it into "
"your own power grid to use it."
msgstr "一台朝一个方向运行的带型链锯。它可以按任意角度进行精确切割。可以拆卸下来接入电源使用。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/obsoletion/obsolete_fake.json
msgid "router table"
msgid_plural "router tables"
msgstr[0] "雕刻机"

#. ~ Description of furniture "router table"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"This table has an inset router, a rotating motor with an exchangeable blade "
"head for cutting specific profiles and grooves and stuff.  You can take this"
" down and plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr "这张桌子上安装着一台嵌入式刳刨机、一台旋转电机和一个可更换的刀头，能够切割出特殊轮廓、凹槽和其他形状。可以拆卸下来接入电源使用。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "planer"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A hefty tool that will take in a board and cut it smooth and flat to a "
"specific width, particularly great if working with raw lumber stock, but "
"also good just for shaving wood down to size.  You can take this down and "
"plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr "一台笨重机器，能把木板切割成特定厚度并抛光。特别适合用来处理原木，但也能用来把木块切削加工成合适的尺寸。可以拆卸下来接入电源使用。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "jointer"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A table-shaped tool with a rotating blade that will cut down, smooth out, "
"and square off a board to make it very smooth and nice indeed.  You can take"
" this down and plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr "一张安装有旋转刀刃工具的桌子，能把木板切割成形、抛光，使之变得非常光滑、美观。可以拆卸下来接入电源使用。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/science.json
msgid "catalytic cracking reactor"
msgid_plural "catalytic cracking reactors"
msgstr[0] "催化裂解反应堆"

#. ~ Description of furniture "catalytic cracking reactor"
#. ~ Description of furniture "hydraulic press"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"If you really want to squash something a lot, this would be exactly the "
"right industrial tool for you.  You can take this down and plug it into your"
" own power grid to use it."
msgstr "如果你真的很想挤压一些东西，这对你来说就是一个很好的工业工具。可以拆卸下来接入电源使用。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json data/json/obsoletion/obsolete_fake.json
msgid "power lathe"
msgid_plural "power lathes"
msgstr[0] "动力车床"

#. ~ Description of furniture "power lathe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"An industrial-grade lathe, for turning chunks of metal and other hard things"
" into round chunks of metal and other hard things."
msgstr "一种工业级车床，用于把大块金属变成圆形大块金属，把坚硬的东西变成其它坚硬的东西。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "air compressor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"This durable tank is topped with a motor that will cram as much air into the"
" tank as possible.  You can take this down and plug it into your own power "
"grid to use it."
msgstr "这个坚固的气罐顶部安装着一台压缩机，能将尽可能多的空气抽进罐中。可以拆卸下来接入电源使用。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Based on the Redline TC500M Manual Tire Changer
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "manual tire changer"
msgid_plural "manual tire changers"
msgstr[0] "手动换胎器"

#. ~ Description of furniture "manual tire changer"
#. ~ Based on the Redline TC500M Manual Tire Changer
#. ~ Description of "manual tire changer"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid ""
"This floor mounted machine contains all the levers, clamps and mounts "
"required to remove or fit a tire, plus an integrated foot pump to inflate "
"it."
msgstr "一台落地式机器，包含拆卸或安装轮胎所需的各类杠杆、夹具和安装件，以及一个内置脚压式充气泵。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "fermenting vat"
msgstr "发酵桶"

#. ~ Description of furniture "fermenting vat"
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled fermenting vat"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A sealable 50-liter vat for fermenting vinegar and various alcoholic brews."
msgstr "一个可以被密封的50升发酵罐，可用于食醋或者各种酒类的发酵。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "filled fermenting vat"
msgstr "满发酵桶"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "butchering rack"
msgstr "屠宰架"

#. ~ Description of furniture "butchering rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "Butchering rack designed to hang a carcass in the air."
msgstr "一个屠宰架子，可以将清理内脏后的胴体悬挂在半空中。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "metal butchering rack"
msgid_plural "metal butchering racks"
msgstr[0] "金属屠宰架"

#. ~ Description of furniture "metal butchering rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"Metal butchering rack designed to hang a carcass in the air.  It can be "
"deconstructed and folded for easy transportation."
msgstr "一个金属屠宰架子，可以将清理内脏后的胴体悬挂在半空中。它能够被拆除并折叠起来便于携带。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "hanging meathook"
msgstr "挂肉钩"

#. ~ Description of furniture "hanging meathook"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "A hefty hook suspended from a chain for stringing up corpses."
msgstr "一个沉重的钩子悬挂在链子上，用于把尸体串起来。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "wind mill"
msgid_plural "wind mills"
msgstr[0] "风力碾磨机"

#. ~ Description of furniture "wind mill"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A small wind-powered mill that can convert starchy products into flour."
msgstr "小型风动力磨，可以把含淀粉的物品加工成面粉。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "active wind mill"
msgstr "风力碾磨机（开）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "active wind mill"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A small wind-powered mill that can convert starchy products into flour.  Its"
" brake has been removed and it is turning."
msgstr "小型风动力磨，可将含淀粉的物品加工成面粉。它的制动装置已经移除，正在转动。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "water mill"
msgid_plural "water mills"
msgstr[0] "水力碾磨机"

#. ~ Description of furniture "water mill"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A small water-powered mill that can convert starchy products into flour."
msgstr "小型水动力磨，可以把含淀粉的物品加工成面粉。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "active water mill"
msgstr "水力碾磨机（开）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "active water mill"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A small water-powered mill that can convert starchy products into flour.  "
"Its brake has been removed and it is turning."
msgstr "小型水动力磨，可将含淀粉的物品加工成面粉。它的制动装置已经移除，正在转动。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "automated gas console"
msgstr "自助加油机"

#. ~ Description of furniture "automated gas console"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "Automated gas flow control console."
msgstr "自助加油机控制台。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "broken automated gas console"
msgstr "自助加油机（损坏）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "broken automated gas console"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"Automated gas flow control console.  Broken.  This is not a good thing."
msgstr "自助加油机控制台。坏了，这不是一件好事。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "reinforced vending machine"
msgstr "自动售货机（加固）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "reinforced vending machine"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A bit tougher to crack open than regular vending machines.  That just makes "
"it all the sweeter a target, doesn't it?"
msgstr "比普通的自动售货机更难打开。这只会使它成为一个更甜蜜的目标，不是吗？"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "vending machine"
msgstr "自动售货机"

#. ~ Description of furniture "vending machine"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "Buy stuff with a cash card."
msgstr "一个使用现金卡来购买物品的售货机，装有自动报警系统。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "broken vending machine"
msgstr "自动售货机（损坏）"

#. ~ Description of furniture "broken vending machine"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"Ponder if you could buy stuff, as it's broken.  Maybe if you broke it more, "
"you wouldn't need to pay at all!"
msgstr "它已经坏了，这不由得让你沉思如何从里面买东西。也许你可以再把它弄坏一点，这样你连钱都不用给了！"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-zlevel-transitions.json
msgid "rope leading up"
msgstr "向上绳索"

#. ~ Description of furniture "rope leading up"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "A rope.  You could use it to climb up."
msgstr "一根绳子。你可以爬上去。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "web leading up"
msgstr "向上蛛丝"

#. ~ Description of furniture "web leading up"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A long, thick strand of slightly sticky web.  You could use it to climb up."
msgstr "一根又长又厚的有点粘手的蛛丝。你可以爬上去。"

#. ~ Bashing failed sound of furniture "web leading up"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "twang."
msgstr "嘣。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "rope hoist"
msgstr "绳索起重器"

#. ~ Description of furniture "rope hoist"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A loop of rope hangs here, using a sturdy horizontal support as a basic "
"pulley.  While crude, it gives you some mechanical advantage for lifting "
"things."
msgstr "一圈绳索绕在坚固的水平支撑上，作为基本的滑轮。虽然很粗糙，但也能方便地起重一些物品。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "rope and tackle hoist"
msgstr "绳索滑轮起重器"

#. ~ Description of furniture "rope and tackle hoist"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A loop of rope hangs here, looped through a quality tackle to give a "
"significant mechanical advantage while lifting heavy objects."
msgstr "一圈绳索穿过坚固的滑轮组悬挂住，在起重时提供显著的省力效果。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "chain hoist"
msgstr "钢链起重器"

#. ~ Description of furniture "chain hoist"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A sturdy chain and heavy tackle hang well-supported from the ceiling here, "
"ready to lift most heavy items you could think of using mechanical "
"advantage."
msgstr "一条结实的钢链和固定在稳固的天花板上，可以用来举起你能想到的大多数重物。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
msgid "illuminating plant bulb"
msgstr "发光的植物根茎"

#. ~ Description of furniture "illuminating plant bulb"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
msgid ""
"A small plant grows among the roots here, its green onion-like bulb "
"illuminating the area around it."
msgstr "这里的根茎中长出了一株小植物，它顶端绿色葱状的鳞茎照亮了周围的地区。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
msgid "brambles"
msgstr "荆棘"

#. ~ Description of furniture "brambles"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
msgid ""
"A wall of tangled roots blocks the path here, you'd have destroy it to get "
"past."
msgstr "一堵纠缠在一起的根茎组成的墙挡住了这条路，你必须摧毁它才能通过。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
msgid "composting midden"
msgstr "堆肥坑"

#. ~ Description of furniture "composting midden"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
msgid ""
"A hole that has been dug into the roots here, and a pretty unpleasant smell "
"emits from it."
msgstr "这里的根茎中被挖出了一个深坑，一股难闻的气味从里面散发出来。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid "walkway"
msgstr "栈道"

#. ~ Description of terrain "walkway"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid ""
"A metallic bridge commonly used in industrial settings to meet specified "
"safety standards."
msgstr "金属材质的桥梁，用于需要特殊安全标准的工业建筑中。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_recreational.json
msgid "dock"
msgstr "码头"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dock"
#. ~ Description of terrain "shallow bridge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid "A wooden platform held by a support made of logs dug into the ground."
msgstr "一个由许多深深插入地底的原木支撑起的木制平台。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid "deep dock pile"
msgstr "深水码头木桩"

#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock pile"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid ""
"A sturdy pile made of wood extending all the way to the riverbed.  A frame "
"will be required to support a surface."
msgstr "一片固定在河床上的结实的木桩。它还需要一个框架才能支撑地板。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid "deep dock frame"
msgstr "深水码头框架"

#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock frame"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid ""
"A log frame secured atop a wooden pile.  Adding a wood surface will make "
"this into a proper dock section."
msgstr "安装于木桩上的原木框架。再铺上木质的地板，这就是一个完整的码头了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid "deep dock"
msgstr "深水码头"

#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid ""
"A wooden platform held by a tall wooden pile that extend to the riverbed.  "
"Very sturdy, and likely to outlast you."
msgstr "固定在河床上的木桩所支撑的木质平台。它非常牢固，预期寿命可能比你还长。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid "shallow bridge"
msgstr "浅水桥"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid "pontoon bridge"
msgstr "浮桥"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pontoon bridge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid ""
"A floating temporary bridge over still water, like the ones armies used to "
"make to cross lakes."
msgstr "一座漂浮在静水上的临时浮桥，就像那些军队用来穿过湖泊时使用的一样。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid "river bridge"
msgstr "河桥"

#. ~ Description of terrain "river bridge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid ""
"A floating temporary bridge over flowing water, like the ones armies used to"
" make to cross rivers."
msgstr "一座漂浮在流水上的临时浮桥，就像那些军队用来穿过河流时使用的一样。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
msgid "bridge pavement"
msgstr "桥面"

#. ~ Description of terrain "bridge pavement"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
msgid "A bridge section made out of concrete and metal."
msgstr "由混凝土和金属制成的桥梁部分。"

#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "bridge pavement"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "bridge yellow pavement"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "bridge sidewalk"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
msgid "concrete cracking and metal screeching!"
msgstr "混凝土破裂和金属扭曲声！"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
msgid "bridge yellow pavement"
msgstr "黄线桥面"

#. ~ Description of terrain "bridge yellow pavement"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
msgid "A bridge section made out of concrete and metal.  It's painted yellow."
msgstr "由混凝土和金属制成的桥梁部分。它被漆成了黄色。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
msgid "bridge sidewalk"
msgstr "桥面人行道"

#. ~ Description of terrain "bridge sidewalk"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
msgid "The sidewalk section of a concrete bridge."
msgstr "混凝土桥的人行道。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dock"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid ""
"A metal platform held by a support made of concrete set into the ground."
msgstr "一个由许多深深插入地底的混凝土梁支撑起的金属平台。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock pile"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid ""
"A sturdy pile made of poured concrete extending all the way to the riverbed."
"  A metal frame will be required to support a surface."
msgstr "一片固定在河床上的结实的混凝土桩。它还需要一个金属框架才能支撑地板。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock frame"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid ""
"A metal frame secured atop a concrete pile.  Adding a metal surface will "
"make this into a proper dock section."
msgstr "安装于混凝土桩上的金属框架。再铺上金属地板，这就是一个完整的码头了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid ""
"A metal platform held by a tall metal pile that extends to the riverbed.  "
"Very sturdy, and likely to outlast you."
msgstr "固定在河床上的混凝土桩所支撑的金属平台。它非常牢固，预期寿命可能比你还长。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid "metal floating dock"
msgstr "金属浮船坞"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal floating dock"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid "A floating temporary dock, anchored to keep it from drifting away."
msgstr "一座临时浮船坞，已经被锚定以防止它漂走。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed laminated glass door"
msgstr "夹层玻璃门（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed laminated glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A closed laminated glass door is composed layers of glass and plastic held "
"together by an interlayer."
msgstr "由夹层粘合多层玻璃和塑料制成的夹层玻璃门。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open laminated glass door"
msgstr "夹层玻璃门（开）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open laminated glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Laminated glass door is composed layers of glass and plastic held together "
"by an interlayer.  Yep, it's open."
msgstr "由夹层粘合多层玻璃和塑料制成的夹层玻璃门。没错，这个是开着的。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed ballistic glass door"
msgstr "防弹玻璃门（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed ballistic glass door"
#. ~ Description of terrain "ballistic glass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "Ballistic glass consists of layers of laminated glass."
msgstr "由多层玻璃制成的防弹玻璃门。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open ballistic glass door"
msgstr "防弹玻璃门（开）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open ballistic glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Ballistic glass consists of layers of laminated glass.  Yep, it's open."
msgstr "由多层玻璃制成的防弹玻璃门。没错，这个是开着的。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed reinforced glass door"
msgstr "强化玻璃门（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed reinforced glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A closed glass door reinforced with woven steel wires in a stylish, but "
"practical pattern."
msgstr "封闭的玻璃门，用于强化的钢丝编织成优雅而实用的图案。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open reinforced glass door"
msgstr "强化玻璃门（开）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open reinforced glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A glass door reinforced with woven steel wires in a stylish, but practical "
"pattern.  Yep, it's open."
msgstr "一扇玻璃门，用于强化的钢丝编织成优雅而实用的图案。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed wood door"
msgstr "木门（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn"
" easily, too."
msgstr "标准的木门，看起来不太坚固。多半也很易燃。"

#. ~ Prying message of terrain "closed wood door"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "closed wood door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "You notice the door is unlocked, so you simply open it."
msgstr "你发现这个门并没有上锁，于是你直接打开了门。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open wood door"
msgstr "木门（开）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn"
" easily, too.  This one is wide open."
msgstr "标准的木门，看起来不太坚固。多半也很易燃。这是敞开的。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "damaged wood door"
msgstr "木门（损坏）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "damaged wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A trashed wooden door, that is more of an obstacle than a door.  Also, you "
"can see right through it.  It could be boarded up with a few planks."
msgstr "一扇破烂的木门，与其说是门更像是障碍。而且，你能看穿它。可以用木板封上。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "empty door frame"
msgstr "空门框"

#. ~ Description of terrain "empty door frame"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An empty door frame made from planks and nails.  A variety of doors could be"
" constructed here."
msgstr "一个用木板和钉子打造的空门框。各式各样的门都可以安装在上面。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed glass door"
msgstr "玻璃门（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A sliding glass door, the kind that was on social media with people and "
"animals running into.  This one is closed, so don't hurt yourself."
msgstr "一扇可滑动的玻璃门，看上去就和网络视频里那些人和动物经常撞上的一模一样。这扇门已经关上了，所以小心点别伤到自己。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open glass door"
msgstr "玻璃门（开）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open glass door"
#. ~ Description of terrain "open frosted glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A sliding glass door that has been left open for all manner of things to "
"travel through."
msgstr "一扇可滑动的玻璃门，看上去就和网络视频里那些人和动物经常撞上的一模一样。这扇门已经打开了，你可以随意进出。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed wood door with peephole"
msgstr "猫眼木门（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If "
"you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole."
msgstr "由普通木头制成的常规木门，差在多了个窥视孔。如果你仔细检查，就可以透过孔窥视。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "damaged wood door with peephole"
msgstr "猫眼木门（损坏）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "damaged wood door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Bad news is the peephole is broken and you can't look outside the door.  "
"Good news is the door is nearly broken down, so there's nothing blocking the"
" view.  A few planks, nails and the right tools could patch up all the "
"damage."
msgstr "坏消息是，窥视孔被打坏，你无法往门外看。好消息是，门几乎被打破了，所以没有任何东西挡住视线。一些木板，钉子和正确的工具可以修补所有伤害。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open wood door with peephole"
msgstr "猫眼木门（开）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open wood door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If "
"you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole.  "
"Although, you don't need to peek through it since the door is open anyway."
msgstr "由普通木头制成的常规木门，差在多了个窥视孔。如果你仔细检查，就可以透过孔窥视。现在门已经打开，不需要窥视了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed reinforced wood door"
msgstr "强化木门（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed reinforced wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Just like other wooden doors, except this one has layers of nailed in planks"
" and additional hinge for reinforcement.  It might be barricaded, but still "
"susceptible to fire."
msgstr "与普通木门有所不同，这扇门用木板和额外的铰链加固过，它的防护性更强，但仍然容易起火。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "damaged reinforced wood door"
msgstr "强化木门（损坏）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "damaged reinforced wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"There are splintering planks and visible holes in the wood, it looks like it"
" could be smashed apart if not repaired."
msgstr "木头上有碎裂的木板和明显的开口，看来若不修复它可能会被砸碎。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open reinforced wood door"
msgstr "强化木门（开）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open reinforced wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Just like other wooden doors, except this one has layers of nailed in planks"
" for reinforcement.  It might be fortified, but still susceptible to fire.  "
"It's open so it's not stopping anything right now."
msgstr "除了一层钉牢加固的木板，这扇木门跟其他的没啥区别。它也许经过强化，但仍然容易着火。现在是敞开的，阻挡不了任何东西。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn"
" easily, too.  This one has an extra keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You "
"could pry it open or pick the lock."
msgstr "标准的木门，看起来不太坚固。多半也很易燃。这一扇门上有个锁孔，应该是被锁上了。你可以用撬棍撬开这扇门，或者使用开锁工具尝试开锁。"

#. ~ Prying message of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "You pry open the door."
msgstr "你撬开了门。"

#. ~ Prying failure of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "You pry, but can't pry open the door."
msgstr "你试图撬开门，但是没能成功。"

#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "closed wood door"
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "t_door_metal_interior_locked"
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "With a satisfying click, the lock on the door opens."
msgstr "随着一声令人满意的咔嗒声，门上的锁被打开了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn"
" easily, too.  This one has a deadbolt keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You "
"could pry it open or pick the lock, or unlock the deadbolt from the inside."
msgstr ""
"标准的木门，看起来不太坚固。多半也很易燃。这一扇门上有个门栓，应该是被锁上了。你可以用撬棍撬开这扇门，或者使用开锁工具尝试开锁，也可以从内侧将门栓打开。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If "
"you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole.  This "
"one has a deadbolt keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You could pry it open or"
" pick the lock, or unlock the deadbolt from the inside."
msgstr ""
"由普通木头制成的常规木门，差在多了个窥视孔。如果你仔细检查，就可以透过孔窥视。这一扇门上有个门栓，应该是被锁上了。你可以用撬棍撬开这扇门，或者使用开锁工具尝试开锁，也可以从内侧将门栓打开。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed door curtain"
msgstr "门帘（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed door curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Repurposed curtains from a window acting as a door.  Could be easily taken "
"down for supplies or placed somewhere else."
msgstr "将窗帘直接吊在门框上，就成了一扇门帘。可以很轻松地将它拆除获得材料，或者拆下来安装在别处。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed makeshift door"
msgstr "简易门（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed makeshift door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A makeshift screen consisting of planks bound together with vertical rope "
"hanging from the top of the doorway.  Could be easily taken down and re-"
"purposed."
msgstr "一扇用绳索将木板捆绑拼凑而成的简易门，有着几条垂直绳索将其固定在门框顶部。可以很轻松地将它拆除获得材料，或者拆下来安装在别处。"

#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "closed makeshift door"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "open makeshift door"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "closed wooden gate"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "picket fence"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "woven wattle fence"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "narrow fence posts"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "closed wooden split rail gate"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "open wooden split rail gate"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "closed metal gate"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "open metal gate"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "closed wooden privacy gate"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "open wooden privacy gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "wham."
msgstr "砰。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open door curtain"
msgstr "门帘（开）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open door curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Repurposed curtains from a window acting as a door.  Could be easily taken "
"down for supplies or placed somewhere else.  These curtains are open, "
"bundled and tied next to the doorway."
msgstr "将窗帘直接吊在门框上，就成了一扇门帘。可以很轻松地将它拆除获得材料，或者拆下来安装在别处。这扇门帘被卷成一团用绳子吊在门框上。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed grass curtain"
msgstr "草门帘（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed grass curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Grass yarn sheets acting as a door.  Could be easily taken down for supplies"
" or placed somewhere else."
msgstr "将草绳吊在门框上，就成了一扇门帘。可以很轻松地将它拆除获得材料，或者拆下来安装在别处。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open grass curtain"
msgstr "草门帘（开）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open grass curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Grass yarn sheets acting as a door.  Could be easily taken down for supplies"
" or placed somewhere else.  These curtains are open, bundled and tied next "
"to the doorway."
msgstr "将草绳吊在门框上，就成了一扇门帘。可以很轻松地将它拆除获得材料，或者拆下来安装在别处。这扇门帘被卷成一团用绳子吊在门框上。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open makeshift door"
msgstr "简易门（开）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open makeshift door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A makeshift screen consisting of planks bound together with rope hanging "
"from the top of the doorway.  Could be easily taken down and re-purposed.  "
"The planks have been rolled up and attached to the top of the doorway, "
"allowing free movement through."
msgstr ""
"一扇用绳索将木板捆绑拼凑而成的简易门，有着几条垂直绳索将其固定在门框顶部。可以很轻松地将它拆除获得材料，或者拆下来安装在别处。这扇简易门的木板卷成一团用绳子吊在门框上。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "empty metal door frame"
msgstr "空金属门框"

#. ~ Description of terrain "empty metal door frame"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An empty door frame made of steel and assorted metal.  A variety of doors "
"could be constructed here."
msgstr "一个用钢铁和各式金属打造的空门框。各式各样的门都可以安装在上面。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "empty metal window frame"
msgstr "空金属窗框"

#. ~ Description of terrain "empty metal window frame"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An empty window frame constructed from assembled metal and carefully braced "
"with various hardware."
msgstr "一个由装配好的金属条构成的空窗框，四周仔细地用了各种五金件支撑。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "boarded up door"
msgstr "门（木板封死）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that has several planks across it, nailed down to "
"board it up and increase its durability.  Still flammable though."
msgstr "一扇标准的木门，有几块木板横穿而过，并钉牢在门框上，以增加其耐久。不过这门还是可燃的。"

#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up door"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up damaged door"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up door with peephole"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up reinforced door"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up damaged reinforced door"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up damaged door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "You pry the boards from the door."
msgstr "你撬开了门上的加固板。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "boarded up damaged door"
msgstr "门（木板封死）（损坏）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up damaged door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A boarded up wooden door, except that some of the planks are fractured or "
"coming loose.  Without repairs, it could be broken down easily."
msgstr "一扇标准的木门，有几块木板横穿而过，并钉牢在门框上，以增加其耐久。这扇门上的木板已经大部分折断或松动了，如果不修理的话，会很快损坏。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "boarded up door with peephole"
msgstr "猫眼门（木板封死）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A boarded up door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  "
"Although it's been covered up in planks, you could still examine the "
"peephole."
msgstr ""
"由普通木头制成的常规木门，差在多了个窥视孔，几块木板横穿而过，并钉牢在门框上，以增加其耐久。虽然安上了许多木板，如果你仔细检查，仍然可以透过孔窥视。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "boarded up reinforced door"
msgstr "强化门（木板封死）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up reinforced door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An additionally reinforced door of layered planks that has been boarded up "
"with more wood to prevent it from opening.  Still susceptible to fire."
msgstr "一扇强化门，有几块木板横穿而过，并钉牢在门框上，以增加其耐久。不过这门还是可燃的。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "boarded up damaged reinforced door"
msgstr "强化门（木板封死）（损坏）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up damaged reinforced door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A battered and torn reinforced door with planks bursting from the joints.  "
"The boarded up planks are fragmented and in pieces, this doesn't look like "
"an easy repair."
msgstr "一扇强化门，有几块木板横穿而过，并钉牢在门框上，以增加其耐久。门上的木板已经破旧不堪，四散成渣，看起来很难修理。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "boarded up damaged door with peephole"
msgstr "猫眼门（木板封死）（损坏）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up damaged door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A wrecked door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  "
"Although it's been covered up in planks, the peephole was damaged and can't "
"be used to see through."
msgstr ""
"由普通木头制成的常规木门，差在多了个窥视孔，几块木板横穿而过，并钉牢在门框上，以增加其耐久。门上的木板已经大部分损坏了，因此上面的窥视孔也无法使用了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed metal door"
msgstr "金属门（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape."
msgstr "一个十分坚固的金属门，由合金钢制成，一体冲压成型。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed corrugated metal door"
msgstr "金属卷帘门（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed corrugated metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A thin door made of corrugated steel held in a frame."
msgstr "一扇用波纹钢板制成的薄门，固定在门框内。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "metal wall"
msgstr "金属墙"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"An industrially fabricated thick sheet carefully positioned and joined "
"seamlessly with perimeter sealant, this wall is capable of resisting extreme"
" elements as well as hostile forces.  Blast load rated and extremely fire-"
"retardant, breaching will require specialized tools or industrial vehicles."
msgstr "经过精心定位并以边缘密封胶无缝连接的工业制厚板材，能抵抗极端气候与敌对力量。具备极优的爆炸负荷和抗燃性，想突破它需要专用工具或工业用载具。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open secret door"
msgstr "秘门（开）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open secret door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"This apparently normal segment of metal wall has opened to reveal a secret "
"passage."
msgstr "这显然是正常的金属墙的一部分打开了，露出了一条秘密通道。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "concrete wall"
msgstr "混凝土墙"

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A faux concrete wall positioned and joined seamlessly with the wall, this "
"wall is capable of resisting extreme elements as well as hostile forces.  "
"Blast load rated and extremely fire-retardant, breaching will require "
"specialized tools or industrial vehicles."
msgstr "经过精心定位并以边缘密封胶无缝连接的人造混凝土墙，能抵抗极端气候与敌对力量。具备极优的爆炸负荷和抗燃性，想突破它需要专用工具或工业用载具。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open secret door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"This apparently normal segment of concrete wall has opened to reveal a "
"secret passage."
msgstr "看上去十分正常的混凝土墙中一段被打开了，露出了一条秘密通道。"

#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "open secret door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "thwack!"
msgstr "哐！"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open metal door"
msgstr "金属门（开）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  It's open, so no tools are needed to break in."
msgstr "一个十分坚固的金属门，由合金钢制成，一体冲压成型。这扇门开着，可以自由出入。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open corrugated metal door"
msgstr "金属卷帘门（开）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open corrugated metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A thin door made of corrugated steel held in a frame.  It's open, so no "
"tools are needed to break in."
msgstr "一扇用波纹钢板制成的薄门，固定在门框内。这扇门开着，可以自由出入。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed metal door with peephole"
msgstr "猫眼金属门（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  If you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the "
"hole."
msgstr "一个十分坚固的金属门，由合金钢制成，一体冲压成型，差在多了个窥视孔。如果你仔细检查，就可以透过孔窥视。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open metal door with peephole"
msgstr "猫眼金属门（开）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open metal door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  If you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the "
"hole.  Although, you don't need to peek through it since the door is open "
"anyway."
msgstr "一个十分坚固的金属门，由合金钢制成，一体冲压成型，差在多了个窥视孔。如果你仔细检查，就可以透过孔窥视。现在门已经打开，不需要窥视了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A galvanized steel door, forged to withstand punishment and impede anyone or"
" anything.  Typically used in conjunction with automated electronic locking "
"mechanisms that require an external source to unlock."
msgstr "一扇镀锌钢门，锻造精良，能够经得起任何物品的捶打，能阻挡住任何人。通常会与可远程控制的各类自动电子锁定装置一起安装。"

#. ~ Prying message of terrain "t_door_metal_interior_locked"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "You pry open the metal door."
msgstr "你撬开了金属门。"

#. ~ Prying failure of terrain "t_door_metal_interior_locked"
#. ~ Prying failure of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "The metal door is too thick."
msgstr "金属门太厚了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  This one has an extra keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You could "
"probably pick the lock."
msgstr "一个十分坚固的金属门，由合金钢制成，一体冲压成型。这一扇门上有个锁孔，应该是被锁上了。你可以使用开锁工具尝试开锁。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed bar door"
msgstr "栏杆门（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed bar door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  The locking "
"mechanism doesn't appear to be engaged."
msgstr "由相互交叉的不锈钢棒所组成的牢房门。看上去似乎并没有上锁。"

#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "closed bar door"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "locked wire gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "closed wire gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "open wire gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "locked retractable gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "closed retractable gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "chain link fence"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "metal post"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "rebar cage"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "metal bars"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "armored boarded up window"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "window with metal bars"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "window frame with metal bars"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "window with metal bars and curtains"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "window with metal grate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid "You finish cutting the metal."
msgstr "你完成了金属切割工作。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open bar door"
msgstr "栏杆门（开）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open bar door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  It's swung "
"wide open.  Freedom!"
msgstr "由相互交叉的不锈钢棒所组成的牢房门。这扇门现在敞开着。终于自由了！"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed bar door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  The locking "
"mechanism appears to be engaged.  The mechanism could be picked open with "
"enough skill."
msgstr "由相互交叉的不锈钢棒所组成的牢房门。看上去似乎已经锁上了。你可以使用开锁工具尝试开锁。"

#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "closed bar door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "The door swings open…"
msgstr "门开了……"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed frosted glass door"
msgstr "毛玻璃门（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed frosted glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A sliding door of frosted white glass."
msgstr "一扇乳白色的毛玻璃推拉门。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open frosted glass door"
msgstr "毛玻璃门（开）"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed bulkhead door"
msgstr "舱壁门（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed bulkhead door"
#. ~ Description of terrain "open bulkhead door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door of cast metal, it is watertight and opened using"
" the fly wheel."
msgstr "一个十分坚固的金属门，由铸铁制成，完全水密，需要用转轮开启。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open bulkhead door"
msgstr "舱壁门（开）"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid "brick wall with embrasure"
msgstr "砖墙射击孔"

#. ~ Description of terrain "brick wall with embrasure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid ""
"This brick wall has an embrasure that lets you shoot and use reach weapons "
"against enemies on the outside, while also protecting you."
msgstr "这堵砖墙有一个射击孔，可以让你对外面的敌人射击和使用长距武器，同时能保护你。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid "adobe wall with embrasure"
msgstr "土坯墙射击孔"

#. ~ Description of terrain "adobe wall with embrasure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid ""
"This adobe brick wall has an embrasure that lets you shoot and use reach "
"weapons against enemies on the outside, while also protecting you."
msgstr "这堵土坯墙有一个射击孔，可以让你对外面的敌人射击和使用长距武器，同时能保护你。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid "stone wall with embrasure"
msgstr "石墙射击孔"

#. ~ Description of terrain "stone wall with embrasure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid ""
"The small opening on this stone wall allows you to shoot and use reach "
"weapons, while also granting you a good cover."
msgstr "这堵石墙有一个射击孔，可以让你对外面的敌人射击和使用长距武器，同时能保护你。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid "wooden wall with embrasure"
msgstr "木板墙射击孔"

#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden wall with embrasure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid ""
"This wooden wall has a hole that lets you shoot and use reach weapons.  "
"Highly flammable."
msgstr "这堵木板墙有一个射击孔，可以让你对外面的敌人射击和使用长距武器，同时能保护你。十分易燃。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid "wooden wall with a wide opening"
msgstr "木板墙缺口"

#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden wall with a wide opening"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid ""
"This wooden wall previously had an embrasure, but now the hole is so big you"
" could even pass through it.  Highly flammable."
msgstr "这堵木板墙之前有一个射击孔，但现在这个洞太大了，你甚至可以穿过它。十分易燃。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid "log wall with embrasure"
msgstr "原木墙射击孔"

#. ~ Description of terrain "log wall with embrasure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid ""
"This timber wall has a hole that lets you shoot through and use reach "
"weapons, while also protecting you.  Quite flammable."
msgstr "这堵原木墙有一个射击孔，可以让你对外面的敌人射击和使用长距武器，同时能保护你。十分易燃。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid "log wall with a wide opening"
msgstr "原木墙缺口"

#. ~ Description of terrain "log wall with a wide opening"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid ""
"This timber wall previously had an embrasure, but now the hole is so big you"
" could even pass through it.  Quite flammable."
msgstr "这堵原木墙之前有一个射击孔，但现在这个洞太大了，你甚至可以穿过它。十分易燃。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid "palisade wall with embrasure"
msgstr "篱笆墙射击孔"

#. ~ Description of terrain "palisade wall with embrasure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid ""
"An age-old type of fortification consisting of hefty lumber staked into the "
"ground and cabled together.  This section in particular has an embrasure."
msgstr "一种历史悠久的防御工程，由沉重的木材深深插入地下并紧密连接在一起。这段墙上有个射击孔。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid "simple concrete wall with embrasure"
msgstr "简易混凝土墙射击孔"

#. ~ Description of terrain "simple concrete wall with embrasure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid "A durable and uniform concrete wall.  This one has an embrasure."
msgstr "一面耐久很高且强度均匀的混凝土墙，没有装饰显得很单调。这段墙上有个射击孔。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid "reinforced concrete wall with embrasure"
msgstr "强化混凝土墙射击孔"

#. ~ Description of terrain "reinforced concrete wall with embrasure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid ""
"This nice hole lets you shoot your machine gun from the safety of your "
"reinforced bunker."
msgstr "这堵墙上的洞可以让你在加固掩体内用机枪安全地射击敌人。"

#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "reinforced concrete wall with embrasure"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "reinforced blue concrete wall"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "reinforced green concrete wall"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "reinforced red concrete wall"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "reinforced white concrete wall"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "reinforced purple concrete wall"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "reinforced pink concrete wall"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "reinforced yellow concrete wall"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "reinforced concrete wall"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "half-built reinforced concrete wall"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "magically reinforced concrete wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/terrain.json
msgid "scrrrash!"
msgstr "呲啦咔咔！"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "palisade gate"
msgstr "篱笆大门"

#. ~ Description of terrain "palisade gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A large doorway consisting of long logs cabled together, that could be "
"expanded upon.  Can act as a door if some type of pulley system were rigged "
"on an adjacent palisade wall."
msgstr "一个由长原木紧密连接组成的门板，可以向两侧扩展。如果在相邻的篱笆墙上安装某种类型的滑轮系统，可以当作大门使用。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "open palisade gate"
msgstr "篱笆大门（开）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open palisade gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A hanging palisade gate, hoisted by a nearby pulley system.  Probably "
"shouldn't be underneath when it comes down."
msgstr "一个悬挂的篱笆门，被附近的滑轮系统悬挂起来。当它降下来的时候你可不应该站在下面。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "makeshift portcullis"
msgstr "简易闸门"

#. ~ Description of terrain "makeshift portcullis"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"An immense gateway scrapped together with various bits of steel and metal "
"scraps."
msgstr "一扇由各式各样的钢制和金属碎片拼接而成的巨大闸门。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "locked wire gate"
msgstr "铁丝大门（锁）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "locked wire gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A gate for a chain link fence.  This one has a locked padlock on the latch "
"system.  With the right tools, you could cut the metal fence or pick the "
"lock.  You could also examine the fence to see if it looks climbable."
msgstr "勾花围栏的大门。这扇门的门闩上有一个锁着的挂锁。使用合适的工具，你可以将金属栅栏切割开或尝试开锁。你也可以靠近点检查围栏是否可以攀爬。"

#. ~ Boltcut sound of terrain "locked wire gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "Gachunk!"
msgstr "吭呛！"

#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "locked wire gate"
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "locked retractable gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "With a satisfying click, the lock on the gate opens."
msgstr "随着一声令人满足的咔嗒声，大门的锁被打开了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "closed wire gate"
msgstr "铁丝大门（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wire gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A gate for a chain link fence with a latch system to stay closed."
msgstr "一扇勾花围栏的大门，上面有着一道门闩。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "open wire gate"
msgstr "铁丝大门（开）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open wire gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A gate for a chain link fence with a latch system to stay closed.  The latch"
" is undone, so the gate has swung open."
msgstr "一扇勾花围栏的大门，上面有着一道门闩。门闩被解开了，现在大门敞开。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "locked retractable gate"
msgstr "卷帘门（锁）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "locked retractable gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A retractable security gate.  The latch on this one is locked.  With the "
"right tools, you could cut the metal fence or disable the lock."
msgstr "一扇可伸缩的安全门。这扇门已经被锁上了。使用正确的工具，你可以切断金属栅栏或者开锁。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "closed retractable gate"
msgstr "卷帘门（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed retractable gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A retractable security gate with a latch system to stay closed."
msgstr "一扇可伸缩的安全门，上面有着一道门闩。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "open retractable gate"
msgstr "卷帘门（开）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open retractable gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A retractable security gate with a latch system to stay closed.  The latch "
"is undone, so the gate has retracted up."
msgstr "一扇可伸缩的卷帘门，上面有着一道门闩。门闩被解开了，现在大门敞开。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "closed wooden gate"
msgstr "木制大门（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wooden gate"
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wooden split rail gate"
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wooden privacy gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A commercial quality gate made of wood with a latch system."
msgstr "一扇商用等级的大门，用木头制成，上面有着一道门闩。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "open wooden gate"
msgstr "木制大门（开）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open wooden gate"
#. ~ Description of terrain "open wooden split rail gate"
#. ~ Description of terrain "open wooden privacy gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A commercial quality gate made of wood with a latch system.  The gate is "
"wide open, allowing anything to travel through."
msgstr "一扇商用等级的大门，用木头制成，上面有着一道门闩。这扇大门已经敞开，可以随意进出。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "closed screen door"
msgstr "纱窗门（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed screen door"
#. ~ Description of terrain "open screen door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A simple wooden doorway with screen mesh."
msgstr "装有纱窗的简单木门。"

#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "closed screen door"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "open screen door"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "closed chickenwire gate"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "open chickenwire gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "rattle!"
msgstr "格格作响！"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "open screen door"
msgstr "纱窗门（开）"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "closed chickenwire gate"
msgstr "铁丝网大门（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed chickenwire gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A gate for a chickenwire fence with a simple latch system to stay closed."
msgstr "一种带有简单门闩的铁丝网围栏的门。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "open chickenwire gate"
msgstr "铁丝网大门（开）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open chickenwire gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A gate for a chickenwire fence with a simple latch system to stay closed.  "
"The latch is undone, so the gate has swung open."
msgstr "一扇铁丝网围栏的大门，带有一道简单的门闩。门闩松开了，所以门就打开了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "picket fence"
msgstr "尖桩围栏"

#. ~ Description of terrain "picket fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A barrier made of wood, it's nothing complicated.  Mildly suggests where not"
" to go."
msgstr "一扇木制的栅栏，并不复杂。和善地提醒你此路不通。"

#. ~ Prying message of terrain "picket fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "You pry out the fence post."
msgstr "你撬开了栅栏柱。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "woven wattle fence"
msgstr "枝条围栏"

#. ~ Description of terrain "woven wattle fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A flimsy barrier made of woven sticks.  Suitable for small animals."
msgstr "用编织的枝条做成的脆弱屏障。能挡住小型动物。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "narrow fence posts"
msgstr "窄围栏桩"

#. ~ Description of terrain "narrow fence posts"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A set of narrow wooden posts for a woven wattle fence."
msgstr "一排窄木桩，用于枝条围栏。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "chain link fence"
msgstr "勾花围栏"

#. ~ Description of terrain "chain link fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A tall fence made of woven wires.  It doesn't suggest to stop, it just "
"stops."
msgstr "一扇由铁丝编织而成的高围栏。它不再仅仅是提醒，此路真不通。"

#. ~ Boltcut sound of terrain "chain link fence"
#. ~ Boltcut sound of terrain "wire fence"
#. ~ Boltcut sound of terrain "barbed wire fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "Snick, snick, gachunk!"
msgstr "咔嚓，咔嚓，吭呛！"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "metal post"
msgstr "金属桩"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal post"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "Set of metal posts, that can hold more serious fences."
msgstr "一根金属桩，可以支撑起更复杂的围栏。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "chickenwire fence"
msgstr "铁丝网围栏"

#. ~ Description of terrain "chickenwire fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A rather flimsy tall fence made of 2x4s and woven wire, suitable for "
"containing small livestock like chickens."
msgstr "一种相当脆弱的高围栏，由2x4木板和编织铁丝制成，适合饲养小型牲畜，比如鸡。"

#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "chickenwire fence"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "screen mesh wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "metal rattling!"
msgstr "金属嘎嘎作响！"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "screen mesh wall"
msgstr "纱网墙"

#. ~ Description of terrain "screen mesh wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A rather flimsy tall wall made of 2x4s and screen mesh, suitable for keeping"
" the bugs out."
msgstr "一种相当脆弱的高墙，由2x4木板和纱网制成，可以用来阻挡蚊虫。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "chickenwire fence post"
msgstr "铁丝网围栏桩"

#. ~ Description of terrain "chickenwire fence post"
#. ~ Description of terrain "fence post"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A couple of posts that support the fence.  They look alone without the "
"fence."
msgstr "一根用于支撑栅栏的柱子。没有栅栏时就孤零零的立在那里。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "fence post"
msgstr "围栏桩"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "wire fence"
msgstr "铁丝网"

#. ~ Description of terrain "wire fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A barrier made of wire, it's nothing complicated.  Mildly suggests where not"
" to go."
msgstr "一扇由铁丝制成的网状围栏，并不复杂。和善地提醒你此路不通。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "barbed wire fence"
msgstr "带刺铁丝网"

#. ~ Description of terrain "barbed wire fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A barrier made of sharp barbed wire.  More persuasive brother of wire fence."
msgstr "一扇由锋利的带刺铁丝制成的网状围栏。比它的铁丝网兄弟的说服力要高那么一点。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "rope fence"
msgstr "绳索围栏"

#. ~ Description of terrain "rope fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A barrier made of rope, it's nothing complicated.  Mildly suggests where not"
" to go."
msgstr "一扇绳索编织而成的网状围栏，并不复杂。和善地提醒你此路不通。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "split rail fence"
msgstr "分离式围栏"

#. ~ Description of terrain "split rail fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A rather stout fence made of 2x4s and fence posts, suitable for containing "
"livestock like horses, cows and pigs."
msgstr "一种相当坚固的栅栏，由2x4木板和栅栏柱组成，适合饲养马、牛和猪等牲畜。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "closed wooden split rail gate"
msgstr "木制分离式围栏门（关）"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "open wooden split rail gate"
msgstr "木制分离式围栏门（开）"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "metal fence"
msgstr "金属栅栏"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A simple metal fence."
msgstr "一面简单的金属栅栏。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "closed metal gate"
msgstr "金属门（关）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A closed metal gate."
msgstr "一扇关闭的金属门。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "open metal gate"
msgstr "金属门（开）"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open metal gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "An open metal gate."
msgstr "一扇开启的金属门。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "wooden privacy fence"
msgstr "木制隐私围栏"

#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden privacy fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A rather stout fence made of 2x4s and fence posts, it is tall and prevents "
"people from seeing into your yard."
msgstr "一种相当坚固的栅栏，由2x4木板和栅栏柱组成，它很高，可以防止人们看到你的院子。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "closed wooden privacy gate"
msgstr "木制隐私大门（关）"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "open wooden privacy gate"
msgstr "木制隐私大门（开）"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "railing"
msgstr "栏杆"

#. ~ Description of terrain "railing"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A section of wooden railing."
msgstr "一段木栏杆。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "glass railing"
msgstr "玻璃栏杆"

#. ~ Description of terrain "glass railing"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A section of railing made out of glass."
msgstr "一段玻璃制栏杆。"

#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "glass railing"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "glass braking!"
msgstr "玻璃破裂的声音！"

#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "glass railing"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "cloning vat"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "ker-rash!"
msgstr "咔吱！"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "metal railing"
msgstr "金属栏杆"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal railing"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A section of metal railing."
msgstr "一段金属栏杆。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "concrete railing"
msgstr "混凝土栏杆"

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete railing"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A section of cemented concrete railing."
msgstr "一段接合的混凝土栏杆。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "guard rail"
msgstr "护栏"

#. ~ Description of terrain "guard rail"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A section of metal railing, put in place to prevent people from falling or "
"taking the easy way out."
msgstr "一段金属栏杆，放置在适当的位置，以防止人员坠落或轻易离开。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flesh.json
msgid "overgrown floor"
msgstr "血肉覆盖的地板"

#. ~ Description of terrain "overgrown floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flesh.json
msgid ""
"A bare concrete floor, almost completely covered by twitching filaments of "
"gray flesh."
msgstr "一层裸露的混凝土地板，几乎完全被不断抽搐的细小灰色肉丝所覆盖。"

#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "overgrown floor"
