#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A section of flooring made out of a tough, rubbery material.  Colored a "
"simple white."
msgstr "用坚硬的橡胶材料制成的地板。涂上简单的白色。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "linoleum tile"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "A section of flooring made out of a tough, gray, rubbery material."
msgstr "用坚硬的、灰色的橡胶材料制成的地板。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "painted waxed floor"
msgstr "染色打蜡地板"

#. ~ Description of terrain "painted waxed floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "This section of wax flooring has been painted."
msgstr "这块打蜡地板已经上过漆了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "radiation platform"
msgstr "辐射平台"

#. ~ Description of terrain "radiation platform"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A dual purpose platform that serves as a containment, and as a device that "
"exposes items places on in to the radioactive source, by temporarily "
"hoisting the radioactive material stored within.  Operated from external "
"console."
msgstr "一种双用途平台，用作收容装置，以及通过暂时吊装存放在其中的放射性物质，将物品暴露在放射源中的装置。从外部控制台操作。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "junk metal floor"
msgstr "废旧金属地板"

#. ~ Description of terrain "junk metal floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A simple roof and floor of rusty scrap metal bolted and wire-tied to a "
"makeshift frame.  Very fashionable in post-apocalyptic shantytowns.  Hope "
"you like the sound of rain on corrugated metal."
msgstr ""
"一个由锈迹斑斑的废金属制成的简单的屋顶和地板，被螺栓和铁丝绑在一个简易框架上。在世界末日后的棚户区非常流行。希望你喜欢雨点打在褶皱金属板上的声音。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_groundxeno.json
msgid "dirt"
msgstr "泥土地"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dirt"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"It's dirt.  Looks like some fine soil for tillage.  Could also be dug out "
"for construction projects."
msgstr "泥土地，看来土壤适合耕种。也可以开发建设项目。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "sand"
msgstr "黄沙"

#. ~ Description of terrain "sand"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A large area of fine sand that could be useful in a number of ways, if it "
"was extracted properly."
msgstr "一大片优质细砂，如果开采得当，可以在很多方面发挥作用。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "mud"
msgstr "泥地"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mud"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "An area of wet, slick mud."
msgstr "一块泥泞湿滑的泥地。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "moss"
msgstr "苔藓"

#. ~ Description of terrain "moss"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "Moist spongy moss."
msgstr "潮湿松软的苔藓。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "clay"
msgstr "黏土"

#. ~ Description of terrain "clay"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A field full of malleable clay, suitable for kiln firing if it was extracted"
" properly."
msgstr "一块充满可塑性黏土的场地，如果开采得当，挺适用来烧窑。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "mound of clay"
msgstr "黏土堆"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mound of clay"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "A mound of clay soil."
msgstr "一堆黏土。"

#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "mound of clay"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "mound of clay"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "glacial ice"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "dirt"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "basalt floor"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "snow"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "singing sand"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_groundxeno.json
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/tropical_terrain.json
msgid "splosh!"
msgstr "啪叽！"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "paper floor"
msgstr "纸地板"

#. ~ Description of terrain "paper floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "Floor made of pulpy mass, covered in sticky wasp saliva."
msgstr "一块由纤维物质制成的地板，上面覆盖了粘乎乎的黄蜂唾液。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "hard paper floor"
msgstr "硬纸地板"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hard paper floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"Hardened cardboard floor made of chewed up trees and resin mixed with wasp "
"saliva."
msgstr "一块硬纸板地板，由咀嚼过的树木和树脂混合黄蜂唾液制成。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "paper brood cap"
msgstr "纸巢盖"

#. ~ Description of terrain "paper brood cap"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A thin paper floor, protecting the pupating wasp larva until it's ready to "
"emerge."
msgstr "一块薄薄的纸地板，保护黄蜂幼虫，直到它准备好破蛹而出。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_commercial.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_evac_center.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_hardcoded.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_lab.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_mall.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_recreational.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_residential.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_retirement_community.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_robofachq.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_waste_junk.json
#: data/mods/Graphical_Overmap/go_overmap_terrain_ranch_camp.json
#: data/mods/Graphical_Overmap/go_overmap_terrain_waste_junk.json
#: data/mods/alt_map_key/overmap_terrain.json
msgid "open air"
msgstr "露天"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open air"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "This is open air."
msgstr "这是露天的。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "mound of sand"
msgstr "沙堆"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mound of sand"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "A mound of sand."
msgstr "一堆沙子。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "glassed sand"
msgstr "玻璃化沙岩"

#. ~ Description of terrain "glassed sand"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A patch of sand that has a crust of natural glass atop it, after exposure to"
" intense heat."
msgstr "暴露在高温下的一块沙子，上面形成了一层天然的玻璃。"

#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "glassed sand"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "crunch"
msgstr "嘎吱"

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain.json
msgid "mound of dirt"
msgstr "土堆"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mound of dirt"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"An area of heaped dirt, not easily traversable.  If examined more closely, "
"it's quite favorable for planting seeds and the like."
msgstr "一块开好垄的泥土地，不容易穿行。仔细检查，可以发现它很适合种植。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mound of dirt"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A giant hill of dirt that looks like you could crawl inside for shelter."
msgstr "一个大土丘，看起来可以爬进去当掩蔽。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "odd fault"
msgstr "古怪的裂痕"

#. ~ Description of terrain "odd fault"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"An unnaturally humanoid-shaped hole, it seems oddly familiar.  There's a "
"strange sensation to examine it closer, as if it belongs to you somehow."
msgstr "一个不自然的人形洞，看上去有种奇怪的熟悉感觉。你觉得自己有种想要靠近仔细观察的冲动，仿佛它本来就和你是一体的一般。"

#. ~ Message about the player in an effect
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"This wall is perfectly vertical.  Odd, twisted holes are set in it, leading "
"as far back into the solid rock as you can see.  The holes are humanoid in "
"shape, but with long, twisted, distended limbs."
msgstr ""
"这面墙完美的垂直于地面。\n"
"在坚固的岩石上你能够看到上面有一些扭曲的洞。\n"
"那些洞有人的形状，但又有许多长又扭曲的肿胀肢体。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "grave"
msgstr "墓地"

#. ~ Description of terrain "grave"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A dirt grave, with some grass growing on it.  At least some of the dead do "
"actually rest in peace."
msgstr "一个泥土坟墓，上面长着一些草。至少有些死者确实安息了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "grave"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A fresh grave, covered with stones, either to keep something from digging it"
" out or to keep one inside from digging out of it.  Two planks mark this "
"place of someone's eternal rest."
msgstr "一座新坟，用石头盖着既防止他人挖开又防止里面的东西挖出来。有两块木板标识着某人永恒安息之地。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "rubber mulch"
msgstr "橡胶地板"

#. ~ Description of terrain "rubber mulch"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A large area mulched with shredded rubber.  It's a softer place to land than"
" regular dirt."
msgstr "一大块覆盖着碎橡胶的地板。一块比普通的泥土更柔软的地方。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "pavement"
msgstr "路面"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pavement"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A segment of asphalt, slowly degrading from cracks, frost heaves and lack of"
" maintenance."
msgstr "一段铺了柏油的路面，因为裂缝、冻胀和缺乏维护而逐渐老化。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "yellow pavement"
msgstr "黄线路面"

#. ~ Description of terrain "yellow pavement"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"Streaks of carefully aligned yellow paint mark the road to inform drivers "
"not to cross.  No one is enforcing these rules anymore."
msgstr "禁止司机跨越的双黄线。再也没有人来执行这些规则了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "pedestrian crossing"
msgstr "人行横道"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pedestrian crossing"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"White polymer lines painted on the pavement which indicate places where "
"pedestrians should cross the road."
msgstr "在人行道上漆上白色聚合物线，指示行人应该过马路的地方。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "sidewalk"
msgstr "人行道"

#. ~ Description of terrain "sidewalk"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"An area of common poured concrete, damaged by frost heaves and large cracks "
"due to lack of maintenance."
msgstr "一段现浇混凝土路面。因为缺乏维护而毁于冻胀和大裂缝。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "concrete"
msgid_plural "concrete"
msgstr[0] "混凝土"

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A newer segment of poured concrete with surface finishes for aesthetics and "
"resistance to freeze-thaw cycles."
msgstr "一种新式的水泥浇筑块，表面处理兼顾了美观与抗冻－融循环功能。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A newer segment of poured concrete with surface finishes for aesthetics and "
"resistance to freeze-thaw cycles.  Covered with a streak of yellow paint."
msgstr "一种新式的水泥浇筑块，表面处理兼顾了美观与抗冻－融循环功能。外部涂上一层黄色的油漆。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "wooden floor"
msgstr "木地板"

#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"Wooden floor created from boards, packed tightly together and nailed down.  "
"Common in patios."
msgstr "木质楼板，由扎紧的木板钉牢而成。常见于露台。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "wooden floor gangway"
msgstr "木制舷梯"

#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden floor gangway"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"Wooden gangway bridging a short gap.  Sturdy enough to act as a floor, but "
"not sufficient to support additional flooring."
msgstr "用于连接短距离间隙的木制舷梯。足够坚固，可以用作地板，但不足以支撑额外的地板。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"High-quality and tough checkered flooring to reduce risk of slips and falls."
msgstr "高质量的坚固网纹地板，可以减小滑倒的风险。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "metal floor gangway"
msgstr "金属舷梯"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal floor gangway"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"Metal gangway bridging a short gap.  Sturdy enough to act as a floor, but "
"not sufficient to support additional flooring."
msgstr "用于连接短距离间隙的金属舷梯。足够坚固，可以用作地板，但不足以支撑额外的地板。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dirt floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "Floor consisting of finely mixed earth that has been tamped down."
msgstr "由材质细腻的土壤夯实而成的泥土地板。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "gelatinous ground"
msgstr "凝胶地面"

#. ~ Description of terrain "gelatinous ground"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"An incursion of a large area of otherworldly substrate, it feels like "
"walking on hardened gelatin."
msgstr "一大块异界物质侵入了此处，感觉就像是在硬化凝胶上行走。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "orifice"
msgstr "孔口"

#. ~ Description of terrain "orifice"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A large round orifice with trails of fresh and dried up strange green liquid"
" with a strong acid odor covering its inner sides."
msgstr "一个巨大的圆形孔口，有新鲜及干燥的奇怪绿色液体的痕迹，其中散发出一股浓烈的酸味。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "elevator"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "An elevator section of the flight deck."
msgstr "飞行甲板上的一个电梯。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "deck coating"
msgstr "甲板涂层"

#. ~ Description of terrain "deck coating"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"Thick metal coating of a hull, covered with a military grade epoxy mix.  "
"Used for runways, and can't be melted by jet engine nozzles."
msgstr "船体表面厚厚的金属涂层，覆盖着军用级环氧树脂。用作航母的跑道，不会被喷气发动机高温喷气熔化。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "yellow deck coating"
msgstr "黄色甲板涂层"

#. ~ Description of terrain "yellow deck coating"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"Thick metal covering of a hull, covered with a military grade epoxy mix, and"
" painted in yellow color."
msgstr "船体表面厚厚的金属涂层，覆盖着军用级环氧树脂。被涂成黄色。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "red deck coating"
msgstr "红色甲板涂层"

#. ~ Description of terrain "red deck coating"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"Thick metal covering of a hull, covered with a military grade epoxy mix, and"
" painted in red color."
msgstr "船体表面厚厚的金属涂层，覆盖着军用级环氧树脂。被涂成红色。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "white deck coating"
msgstr "白色甲板涂层"

#. ~ Description of terrain "white deck coating"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"Thick metal covering of a hull, covered with a military grade epoxy mix, and"
" painted in white color."
msgstr "船体表面厚厚的金属涂层，覆盖着军用级环氧树脂。被涂成白色。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "walnut tree"
msgstr "核桃树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "walnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive tree belonging to the 'Juglans' genus.  If you look closely, you "
"can see some unharvested walnuts."
msgstr "一棵巨大的树木，分类学上属于胡桃属。靠近看时可以发现一些还没被摘掉的核桃。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "walnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Juglans' genus."
msgstr "一棵巨大的树木，分类学上属于胡桃属。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "blackjack oak"
msgstr "马利兰德栎树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "blackjack oak"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the genus 'Quercus', with bark cracked into rectangular "
"black plates split by narrow orange fissures.  You could peel off the bark "
"sections if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr "一棵落叶乔木，分类学上属于栎属。树皮开裂出橙色细缝，将其分隔成许多黑色长方块。靠近查看它时，可以把树皮剥下来。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "blackjack oak"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the genus 'Quercus', with bark cracked into rectangular "
"black plates split by narrow orange fissures.  All usable bark has been "
"stripped off."
msgstr "一棵落叶乔木，分类学上属于栎属。树皮开裂出橙色细缝，将其分隔成许多黑色长方块。所有可用的树皮都被剥掉了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "alder tree"
msgstr "桤木"

#. ~ Description of terrain "alder tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous flowering tree with serrate, scalloped, round-obovate leaves, "
"commonly forming dense groves alongside water."
msgstr "一种落叶开花乔木，长着锯齿状扇形纹路的倒卵形叶子，通常在水边形成密林。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "chestnut tree"
msgstr "栗树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "chestnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive tree belonging to the 'Castanea' genus.  If you look closely, you "
"can see some unharvested chestnuts."
msgstr "一棵巨大的树木，分类学上属于栗属。靠近看时可以发现一些还没被摘掉的栗子。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "chestnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Castanea' genus."
msgstr "一棵巨大的树木，分类学上属于栗属。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "beech tree"
msgstr "榉树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "beech tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive tree belonging to the 'Fagus' genus.  If you look closely, you can"
" see some unharvested beech nuts."
msgstr "一棵巨大的树木，分类学上属于山毛榉属。靠近看时可以发现一些还没被摘掉的榉实。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "beech tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Fagus' genus."
msgstr "一棵巨大的树木，分类学上属于山毛榉属。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "hazelnut tree"
msgstr "榛树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hazelnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A stubby tree belonging to the 'Corylus' genus.  If you look closely, you "
"can see some unharvested hazelnuts."
msgstr "一棵粗矮的树木，分类学上属于榛属。靠近看时可以发现一些还没被摘掉的榛子。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hazelnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A stubby tree belonging to the 'Corylus' genus."
msgstr "一棵粗矮的树木，分类学上属于榛属。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "oak tree"
msgstr "橡树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "oak tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive deciduous tree belonging to the 'Quercus' genus, commonly found "
"throughout the New England region.  If you look closely, you can see some "
"acorns the squirrels haven't gotten yet."
msgstr "一棵体型巨大的落叶树，分类学上属于栎属，在新英格兰地区四处可见。靠近看时可以发现一些还没有被松鼠摘取的橡实。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "oak tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive deciduous tree belonging to the 'Quercus' genus, commonly found "
"throughout the New England region."
msgstr "一棵体型巨大的落叶树，分类学上属于栎属，在新英格兰地区四处可见。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "basswood tree"
msgstr "椴树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "basswood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The American linden.  It has pretty and sweet-smelling flowers in the Summer"
" and you might be able to eat its young leaves in Spring."
msgstr "一株美洲椴树。夏天它会开出美丽而芬芳的花朵，而春天你可以吃它的嫩叶。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "basswood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The American linden.  It has pretty and sweet-smelling flowers in the Summer"
" and its young leaves have already been harvested."
msgstr "一株美洲椴树。夏天它会开着美丽而芬芳的花朵，它上面的嫩叶已经被采光了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "cottonwood tree"
msgstr "棉白杨树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "cottonwood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large tree belonging to the 'Populus' genus, commonly found throughout the"
" New England region.  You see some cottonwood tree bolls that can be "
"harvested."
msgstr "一棵体型巨大的树，分类学上属于杨属，在新英格兰地区四处可见。你在上面看到一些可以摘下来的杨絮。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "cottonwood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large tree belonging to the 'Populus' genus, commonly found throughout the"
" New England region.  All the cottonwood tree bolls have been harvested."
msgstr "一棵体型巨大的树，分类学上属于杨属，在新英格兰地区四处可见。上面的杨絮都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "elm tree"
msgstr "榆树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "elm tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large tree belonging to the 'Ulmus' genus, commonly found throughout the "
"New England region."
msgstr "一棵体型巨大的树，分类学上属于榆属，在新英格兰地区四处可见。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "dead tree"
msgstr "枯树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"An indiscernible tree that has withered away, whether by weather, fire or "
"otherworldly."
msgstr "一棵早已枯萎而难以分辨物种的枯树，可能是因受天气、火焰、或是异界的影响。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "warped dead tree"
msgstr "扭曲枯树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "warped dead tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This deciduous tree's branches are warped into a spiral.  This appears to "
"have killed it."
msgstr "这棵落叶树的树枝被某种力量扭曲成螺旋状，而且让它枯萎了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "young tree"
msgstr "小树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "young tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A relatively young sapling of an indeterminate species.  It could take "
"decades before reaching maturity, so there's no use waiting around."
msgstr "一个过于年幼而难以分辨物种的小树。长大成熟可能需要几十年，所以在这里干等着可没用。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "mega fern"
msgstr "巨型蕨叶"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mega fern"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A gigantic fern like nothing you've seen before.  The leaves are a bright "
"scarlet color with a net like structure of green veins.  The multipronged "
"trunks appear to have the consistency of balsa wood."
msgstr "一种你从未见过的巨大蕨类植物。叶子呈明亮的猩红色，有绿色纹理的网状结构。多刺枝干特性似乎和轻木一致。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "apple tree"
msgstr "苹果树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "apple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Malus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as apples.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could probably "
"find a few mature ones in autumn."
msgstr "一棵在秋天能够结出苹果果实的树，分类学上属于苹果属。如果你顺着枝干仔细观察的话，就可以找到几个成熟的苹果。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "apple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Malus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as apples.  There do not appear to be any ripe apples now."
msgstr "一棵在秋天能够结出苹果果实的树，分类学上属于苹果属。看起来上面成熟的苹果都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "pear tree"
msgstr "梨树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pear tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'Pyrus communis', or the common pear tree, which produces viable "
"pears in the fall.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could "
"probably find a few mature ones."
msgstr "一棵在秋天能够结出梨子果实的树，分类学上属于梨属。如果你顺着枝干仔细观察的话，就可以找到几个成熟的梨子。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pear tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'Pyrus communis', or the common pear tree, which produces viable "
"pears in the fall.  Looks like all the ripe pears have been picked."
msgstr "一棵在秋天能够结出梨子果实的树，分类学上属于梨属。看起来上面成熟的梨子都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "coffee tree"
msgstr "咖啡树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "coffee tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'gymnocladus dioicus', or the kentucky coffee tree, which produces "
"roastable coffee pods and brewable leaves in the fall.  If you examined the "
"branches more closely, you could probably find a few mature ones."
msgstr ""
"一棵在秋天能够结出皂荚和叶子的北美皂荚树，俗称肯塔基咖啡树，分类学上属于豆科皂荚属，皂荚可以烘烤成咖啡豆的替代品，而叶子可以酿酒。如果你顺着枝干仔细观察的话，就可以找到成熟的皂荚。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "coffee tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'gymnocladus dioicus', or the kentucky coffee tree, which produces "
"roastable coffee pods and brewable leaves in the fall.  Looks like all the "
"ripe pods have been picked."
msgstr ""
"一棵在秋天能够结出皂荚和叶子的北美皂荚树，俗称肯塔基咖啡树，分类学上属于豆科皂荚属，皂荚可以烘烤成咖啡豆的替代品，而叶子可以酿酒。看起来上面成熟的皂荚都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "cherry tree"
msgstr "樱桃树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "cherry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"cherries in the summer.  If you examined the foliage more closely, you could"
" probably find some viable clusters."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出樱桃果实的树，分类学上属于樱桃属，在新英格兰地区土生土长。如果你顺着枝干仔细观察的话，就可以找到一些成熟的樱桃。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "cherry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"cherries in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe bunches of cherries have "
"been picked."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出樱桃果实的树，分类学上属于樱桃属，在新英格兰地区土生土长。看起来上面成熟的樱桃都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "juniper tree"
msgstr "杜松子树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "juniper tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the species of 'Juniperus' that grows in New England, juniper berries"
" grow over two to three years, first flowering.  On the second year "
"producing a green berry, the last, they produce their more famed blue "
"varieties.  If you examined the foliage more closely, you could probably "
"find some viable clusters."
msgstr ""
"生长在新英格兰的\"刺柏属\"物种之一，杜松子从开花算起需生长两到三年。第二年为绿色浆果，最后，才生出广为人知的蓝色种类。如果你仔细检查树叶，你可能会找到一些可用的果簇。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "juniper tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the species of 'Juniperus' that grows in New England, juniper berries"
" grow over two to three years.  In the first year they flower, in the second"
" year they produce a green berry, the last, they produce their more famed "
"blue varieties.  Looks like all the ripe bunches of berries have been "
"picked."
msgstr ""
"生长在新英格兰的\"刺柏属\"物种之一，杜松子从开花算起需生长两到三年。第二年为绿色浆果，最后，才生出广为人知的蓝色种类。看起来所有成熟的浆果串已经采完了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "peach tree"
msgstr "桃子树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "peach tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"peaches in the summer.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could"
" probably find some mature peaches."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出桃子果实的树，分类学上属于樱桃属，在新英格兰地区土生土长。如果你顺着枝干仔细观察的话，就可以找到一些成熟的桃子。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "peach tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"peaches in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe peaches have been picked."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出桃子果实的树，分类学上属于樱桃属，在新英格兰地区土生土长。看起来上面成熟的桃子都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "apricot tree"
msgstr "杏树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "apricot tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A transplanted species of 'Prunus armeniaca', rarely found in New England.  "
"It produces apricots in the summer.  If you examined the spurs more closely,"
" you could probably find some mature apricots."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出杏子果实的树，分类学上属于樱桃属，移植自其他地区，很难在本地找到。如果你顺着枝干仔细观察的话，就可以找到一些成熟的杏子。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "apricot tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A transplanted species of 'Prunus armeniaca', rarely found in New England.  "
"It produces apricots in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe apricots have "
"been picked."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出杏子果实的树，分类学上属于樱桃属，移植自其他地区，很难在本地找到。看起来上面成熟的杏子都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "plum tree"
msgstr "李子树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "plum tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it "
"produces plums in the summer.  If you examined the spurs more closely, you "
"could probably find some ripe plums."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出李子果实的树，分类学上属于樱桃属，在新英格兰地区土生土长。如果你顺着枝干仔细观察的话，就可以找到一些成熟的李子。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "plum tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it "
"produces plums in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe plums have been "
"picked."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出李子果实的树，分类学上属于樱桃属，在新英格兰地区土生土长。看起来上面成熟的李子都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "mulberry tree"
msgstr "桑树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mulberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Morus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as mulberries.  In the summer, many berries can be picked."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出桑椹果实的树，分类学上属于桑属。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mulberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Morus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as mulberries.  There do not appear to be any ripe mulberries now."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出桑椹果实的树，分类学上属于桑属。看起来上面成熟的桑椹都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "elderberry tree"
msgstr "接骨木"

#. ~ Description of terrain "elderberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Sambucus' genus, producing fruit commonly "
"known as elderberries.  In the summer, many berries can be picked."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出接骨木果果实的树，分类学上属于接骨木属。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "elderberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Sambucus' genus, producing fruit commonly "
"known as elderberries.  There do not appear to be any ripe elderberries now."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出接骨木果果实的树，分类学上属于接骨木属。看起来上面成熟的接骨木果都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "pine tree"
msgstr "松树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A towering coniferous tree that belongs to the 'Pinus' genus, with the New "
"England species varying from 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' and 'P. rigida'.  "
"If you examined the tree more closely, you might find usable sticky whorls, "
"resin clumps and unharvested pinecones."
msgstr ""
"一棵高耸入云的针叶树，分类学上属于松属，在新英格兰地区主要由刚松、北美红松、北美乔松组成。靠近查看它时，可以找到粘稠的松香、树脂和可收获的松塔。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A towering coniferous tree that belongs to the 'Pinus' genus, with the New "
"England species varying from 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' and 'P. rigida'.  "
"Some of the branches and resin clumps have been stripped away and many of "
"the pinecones aren't developed fully yet, but given a season, it could be "
"harvestable again."
msgstr ""
"一棵高耸入云的针叶树，分类学上属于松属，在新英格兰地区主要由刚松、北美红松、北美乔松组成。看起来它的枝干被人折走了许多，成熟的松塔和树脂都被摘光了，不过再过一季就应该能再次收获了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "dead pine tree"
msgstr "枯松树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A towering coniferous tree that belongs to the 'Pinus' genus, with the New "
"England species varying from 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' and 'P. rigida'.  "
"This trees branches are bare, and it appears to be dead."
msgstr "一棵高耸入云的针叶树，分类学上属于松属，在新英格兰地区主要由刚松、北美红松、北美乔松组成。这棵树的枝干都秃了，看起来已经枯萎了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "warped dead pine tree"
msgstr "扭曲枯萎松树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "warped dead pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The branches of this dead pine have been twisted into a shape that remind "
"you of Sierpinski triangles.  It did not survive getting warped like this."
msgstr "这棵枯松树的树枝被扭曲成某种形状，让你想起谢尔宾斯基三角形。它没法被扭曲成这样后继续存活。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "birch tree"
msgstr "桦树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "birch tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Betula' genus, with the characteristic peeling"
" bark.  Species like 'B. alleghaniensis', 'B. papyrifera', and 'B. "
"populifolia' are the most common in the New England region.  You could tear "
"off some strips of bark if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr "一棵高大的落叶树，分类学上属于桦属，在新英格兰地区主要由北美黄桦、北美白桦、北美灰桦组成。靠近查看它时，可以撕下一些树皮。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "birch tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Betula' genus, with the characteristic peeling"
" bark.  Species like 'B. alleghaniensis', 'B. papyrifera', and 'B. "
"populifolia' are the most common in the New England region.  Looks like "
"there isn't enough rhytidome to peel off yet."
msgstr "一棵高大的落叶树，分类学上属于桦属，在新英格兰地区主要由北美黄桦、北美白桦、北美灰桦组成。看起来桦树皮都被撕光了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "willow tree"
msgstr "柳树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "willow tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall, wide deciduous tree of the 'Salix' genus, with long thin leafy "
"branches that hang down like curtains.  You could tear off some bark."
msgstr "一棵又高又壮的落叶树，分类学上属于柳属。叶子长而薄，如窗帘一般垂下。靠近查看它时，可以撕下一些树皮。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "willow tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall, wide deciduous tree of the 'Salix' genus, with long thin leafy "
"branches that hang down like curtains.  Looks like all usable bark has been "
"torn off, and new rhytidomes have not formed yet."
msgstr "一棵又高又壮的落叶树，分类学上属于柳属。叶子长而薄，如窗帘一般垂下。看起来树皮都被撕掉了，还没形成新皮层。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "maple tree"
msgstr "枫树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "maple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large deciduous tree of the 'Acer' genus.  The leaves are distinctively "
"shaped with five prongs.  It could be tapped in order to extract maple "
"syrup."
msgstr "一棵高大的大型落叶树，分类学上属于槭属。长着形似手掌的特别树叶。可以安装插管来收获枫树糖浆。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "maple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large deciduous tree of the 'Acer' genus.  The leaves are distinctively "
"shaped with five prongs.  A spigot is wedged into the trunk, and sweet maple"
" syrup can be extracted."
msgstr "一棵高大的大型落叶树，分类学上属于槭属。长着形似手掌的特别树叶。树干被被楔入一根插管，可以收获甜蜜的枫树糖浆。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "hickory tree"
msgstr "山核桃树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hickory tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  You could look for hickory nuts"
" if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr "一棵高大落叶树，分类学上属于山核桃属。靠近看时可以发现一些还没被摘掉的山核桃。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hickory tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  It looks like the tree has been"
" picked clean of hickory nuts."
msgstr "一棵高大落叶树，分类学上属于山核桃属。看起来上面成熟的山核桃都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "pistachio tree"
msgstr "开心果树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pistachio tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the 'Pistacia' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is"
" not native to this region.  You could look for pistachio nuts if you "
"examined the tree more closely."
msgstr "一棵落叶树，分类学上属于黄连木属。它并非本地原生物种，而是人工栽培的。靠近看时可以发现一些还没被摘掉的开心果。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pistachio tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the 'Pistacia' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is"
" not native to this region.  Unfortunately, it looks like it has been picked"
" clean of pistachio nuts."
msgstr "一棵落叶树，分类学上属于黄连木属。它并非本地原生物种，而是人工栽培的。看起来上面成熟的开心果都被摘完了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "almond tree"
msgstr "扁桃树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "almond tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the 'Prunus' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is "
"not native to this region.  You could look for fresh almonds if you examined"
" the tree more closely."
msgstr "一棵落叶树，分类学上属于李属。它并非本地原生物种，而是人工栽培的。靠近看时可以发现一些还没被摘掉的扁桃仁。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "almond tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the 'Prunus' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is "
"not native to this region.  There are no almonds left to pick on the tree."
msgstr "一棵落叶树，分类学上属于李属。它并非本地原生物种，而是人工栽培的。看起来上面成熟的扁桃仁都被摘完了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "pecan tree"
msgstr "美洲山核桃树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pecan tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  You could look for pecan nuts "
"if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr "一棵高大落叶树，分类学上属于山核桃属。靠近看时可以发现一些还没被摘掉的美洲山核桃。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pecan tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  It doesn't look like there are "
"any pecan nuts left on the tree."
msgstr "一棵高大落叶树，分类学上属于山核桃属。看起来上面成熟的美洲山核桃都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "dead hickory tree"
msgstr "枯山核桃树"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead hickory tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The dead remnants of a tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  Nothing "
"useful can be foraged from this poor, dead tree."
msgstr "一棵枯萎的高大落叶树，分类学上属于山核桃属。从这棵贫瘠的枯萎的树上收获不到任何果实。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "underbrush"
msgid_plural "underbrushes"
msgstr[0] "灌木丛"

#. ~ Description of terrain "underbrush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Small plants and shrubs that decorate the forest.  An observant forager "
"could obtain edible plants, acorns, eggs, and mushrooms from it."
msgstr "四散在森林中的小型植物和灌木。一个有敏锐观察力的采集者能从中找到各种食用植物，橡实，蛋和蘑菇。"

