#. ~ Description of "fridge"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json data/mods/Mythos/items/appliances.json
msgid ""
"A fridge for keeping food cool.  Provides some insulation from outside "
"weather."
msgstr "一台冰箱，用于冷藏食物。能够稍微隔热，减少外界气温的影响。"

#. ~ Description of "freezer"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid ""
"A disconnected freezer.  Can be plugged into a power source to start "
"freezing food."
msgstr "一台未通电的冰柜。可以插入电源开始冷冻食物。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid "disconnected oven"
msgid_plural "disconnected ovens"
msgstr[0] "烤箱（未连接）"

#. ~ Description of "disconnected oven"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid ""
"A disconnected electric convection-based oven, commonly used for heating and"
" cooking food."
msgstr "一台被断开了电源的对流式电烤箱，通常用于加热及烹饪食物。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid "large water purifier"
msgid_plural "large water purifiers"
msgstr[0] "大型净水器"

#. ~ Description of "large water purifier"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid ""
"This device effectively sterilizes water, can be plugged into the wall and "
"used."
msgstr "这台设备能有效地净化污水。可以放置后接入电源使用。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid "disconnected arcade machine"
msgid_plural "disconnected arcade machines"
msgstr[0] "街机（未连接）"

#. ~ Description of "disconnected arcade machine"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid ""
"A bulky upright arcade cabinet, brightly painted and slightly worn with age."
"  Ready to be plugged in and played."
msgstr "一台笨重的立式街机游戏机，色彩鲜艳，因长年使用而略微磨损。可以接入电源后用它玩一会游戏。"

#. ~ Based off JET J-2500 Drill Press
#. ~ Description of "drill press"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid ""
"A powerful drill mounted on a slide that lets it drop precisely down.  "
"Useful in all kinds of projects from industrial fabrication to home "
"woodworking.  Can be placed and plugged into a power source."
msgstr "一台安装在滑轨上的强力钻机，可以用它精确钻孔。可用于从工业制造到家庭木工的各种工作。可以放置后接入电源使用。"

#. ~ Based off Powermatic PM1000 Table Saw
#. ~ Description of "table saw"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid ""
"A rotating sawblade set into a large flat table, for making straight "
"measured cuts, a key tool in any carpenter's arsenal.  Can be placed and "
"plugged into a power source."
msgstr "一台安装在大平台上的旋锯，能够笔直切割出精确的直线，各类木工设备中的关键利器之一。可以放置后接入电源使用。"

#. ~ Based off DEWALT 12-Inch Sliding Compound Miter Saw
#. ~ Description of "mitre saw"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid ""
"A circular sawblade on an arm that can slide and rotate in several "
"directions, this is a staple tool for nearly any carpentry.  Can be placed "
"and plugged into a power source."
msgstr "一台安装在机械臂上的圆锯，可以在多个方向上滑动旋转，是木匠的标配工具。可以放置后接入电源使用。"

#. ~ Based off JET JWBS-18-3 Woodworking Band Saw
#. ~ Description of "band saw"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid ""
"A ribbonlike sawblade runs in a single direction in this tool, allowing "
"precise cuts at almost any angle.  Can be placed and plugged into a power "
"source."
msgstr "一台朝一个方向运行的带型链锯。它可以按任意角度进行精确切割。可以放置后接入电源使用。"

#. ~ Based off Powermatic TS29 Shaper.  TODO: When support for multi-tile
#. appliances is added, this can stretch two tiles
#. ~ Description of "router"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid ""
"This table has an inset router, a rotating motor with an exchangeable blade "
"head for cutting specific profiles and grooves and stuff.  Can be placed and"
" plugged into a power source."
msgstr "这张桌子上安装着一台嵌入式刳刨机、一台旋转电机和一个可更换的刀头，能够切割出特殊轮廓、凹槽和其他形状。可以放置后接入电源使用。"

#. ~ Based off JET JWP-15BHH Woodworking Planer
#. ~ Description of "planer"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid ""
"A hefty tool that will take in a board and cut it smooth and flat to a "
"specific width, particularly great if working with raw lumber stock, but "
"also good just for shaving wood down to size.  Can be placed and plugged "
"into a power source."
msgstr "一台笨重机器，能把木板切割成特定厚度并抛光。特别适合用来处理原木，但也能用来把木块切削加工成合适的尺寸。可以放置后接入电源使用。"

#. ~ Based off Powermatic PJ-882 Jointer.  TODO: When support for multi-tile
#. appliances is added, this can stretch two tiles
#. ~ Description of "jointer"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid ""
"A table-shaped tool with a rotating blade that will cut down, smooth out, "
"and square off a board to make it very smooth and nice indeed.  Can be "
"placed and plugged into a power source."
msgstr "一张安装有旋转刀刃工具的桌子，能把木板切割成形、抛光，使之变得非常光滑、美观。可以放置后接入电源使用。"

#. ~ Based off Daytona DSP20T Hydraulic Shop Press
#. ~ Description of "hydraulic press"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid ""
"If you really want to squash something a lot, this would be exactly the "
"right industrial tool for you.  Can be placed and plugged into a power "
"source."
msgstr "如果你真的很想挤压一些东西，这对你来说就是一个很好的工业工具。可以放置后接入电源使用。"

#. ~ Based off Renegade Industrial 2.2HP 210LPM Air Compressor
#. ~ Description of "air compressor"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid ""
"This durable tank is topped with a motor that will cram as much air into the"
" tank as possible.  Can be placed and plugged into a power source."
msgstr "这个坚固的气罐顶部安装着一台压缩机，能将尽可能多的空气抽进罐中。可以放置后接入电源使用。"

#. ~ Description of "autoclave"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid ""
"This is an autoclave.  It's useful for sterilizing things like CBMs.  It "
"requires a massive amount of power, so it will need to be plugged into a "
"power grid."
msgstr "一台高压灭菌釜，用于对 CBM 之类的物品进行灭菌。启动它需要非常巨大的能量，因此需要接入电网使用。"

#. ~ Description of "power cord"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid ""
"A power cord, like you've seen many times before: it's a short multi-"
"stranded copper cord with power outlet at the end."
msgstr "一根电源线，就像你以前见过的很多一样：它是一根短的多股铜线，末端有电源插头。"

#. ~ Description of "standing lamp"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid ""
"An electrical device containing an electric lamp that provides illumination "
"once plugged into a power outlet."
msgstr "一种包含灯泡的电气设备，一旦插入电源插座即可提供照明。"

#. ~ Description of "standing floodlight"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid ""
"A large and heavy light designed to illuminate wide areas once plugged into "
"a power outlet."
msgstr "又大又重的灯，用来照亮大片半圆形区域。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid "wall wiring"
msgid_plural "wall wirings"
msgstr[0] "墙壁布线"

#. ~ Description of "wall wiring"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid "Electric wires used to run power through walls."
msgstr "安装在在墙上用来供电的电线。"

#. ~ Description of "foot locker recharging station"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid ""
"A universal recharging station integrated into a steel storage compartment."
"  When set up as an appliance and turned on, it will steadily charge all "
"rechargeable batteries (battery cells, lead-acid batteries, etc) placed "
"directly within its storage space."
msgstr "集成了钢制储物柜的通用充电站。当放置为电器并开启后，会对直接放置在其内部存储空间中的任何可充电电池（蓄电池、铅酸电池等）持续充电。"

#. ~ Description of "box battery charger"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid ""
"A small device for recharging batteries integrated into a small wooden "
"storage compartment.  When set up as an appliance and turned on, it will "
"slowly charge all rechargeable batteries (battery cells, lead-acid "
"batteries, etc) placed directly within its storage space."
msgstr ""
"集成了一个小型木制储物箱的小型通用充电器。当放置为电器并开启后，会对直接放置在其内部存储空间中的任何可充电电池（蓄电池、铅酸电池等）持续缓慢地充电。"

#. ~ I don't know how much these were worth pre-Cataclysm but the pu-238 alone
#. is worth about 5-6 million and hundreds of millions were spent on research.
#. After the apocalypse these should basically be valuable beyond compare
#. though.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid "Compact Advanced Stirling Radioisotope Generator"
msgid_plural "Compact Advanced Stirling Radioisotope Generator"
msgstr[0] "紧凑型ASRG发电机"

#. ~ I don't know how much these were worth pre-Cataclysm but the pu-238 alone
#. is worth about 5-6 million and hundreds of millions were spent on research.
#. After the apocalypse these should basically be valuable beyond compare
#. though.
#. ~ Description of "Compact Advanced Stirling Radioisotope Generator"
#: data/json/items/appliances.json
msgid ""
"A really heavy brick of metal housing an ASRG, formerly used by NASA and "
"repurposed by the military.  Will provide about 130w, basically forever as "
"far as you're concerned.  Should be safe due to the large amount of "
"shielding.  Although these were designed for spacecraft, the sheer amount of"
" armor plating and lead means it is much more massive, so you probably "
"shouldn't try to power a vehicle with it."
msgstr ""
"一个非常重的大金属块，里面装有一个ASRG（先进斯特林放射性同位素发电机），以前由NASA使用，后来被军方重新采用。它能提供130W的供电，直到永远（至少对你所需要关心的时间长度来说）。由于它厚重的装甲板，使用起来应该是安全的。尽管这东西是为航天器设计的，但装甲板和铅的数量，意味着它的重量要比你想象的大得多，因此别想着把它装到车上提供动力了。"

