#. ~ Description of "roasted hickory nuts"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/nuts.json
msgid "A handful of roasted nuts from a hickory tree."
msgstr "一把山核桃，已经烤熟了。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/nuts.json
msgid "hickory nut ambrosia"
msgid_plural "hickory nut ambrosias"
msgstr[0] "山核桃酿"

#. ~ Description of "hickory nut ambrosia"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/nuts.json
msgid "Delicious hickory nut ambrosia.  A drink worthy of the gods."
msgstr "美味的山核桃酿。神的饮品。（原文Ambrosia意为神的食物）"

#. ~ Two tablespoons per charge.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/nuts.json
msgid "peanut butter"
msgid_plural "peanut butters"
msgstr[0] "花生酱"

#. ~ Two tablespoons per charge.
#. ~ Description of "peanut butter"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/nuts.json
msgid ""
"A brown goo that tastes very little like its namesake.  It's not bad, but "
"it'll stick to the roof of your mouth."
msgstr "棕色的粘稠物，尝起来没什么花生味。倒不难吃，不过会粘在上牙上。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/nuts.json
msgid "imitation peanutbutter"
msgid_plural "imitation peanutbutters"
msgstr[0] "代花生酱"

#. ~ Description of "imitation peanutbutter"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/nuts.json
msgid ""
"A thick, nutty brown paste so that the peanut-allergic can enjoy PB&Js too."
msgstr "一种浓稠的坚果棕色糊状物，让花生过敏的人也可以享用美味的花生酱果酱三明治。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/nuts.json
msgid "peanut butter spread"
msgid_plural "peanut butter spreads"
msgstr[0] "花生抹面包酱"

#. ~ Description of "peanut butter spread"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/nuts.json
msgid "Processed peanut butter spread."
msgstr "一份工厂出品的抹面包用的加工花生酱。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/nuts.json
msgid "acorns"
msgid_plural "acorns"
msgstr[0] "橡实"

#. ~ Description of "acorns"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/nuts.json
msgid ""
"A handful of acorns, still in their shells.  Squirrels like them, but they "
"taste terribly bitter and can upset your stomach."
msgstr "一把橡子，还带着壳。松鼠的挚爱，当然你不是松鼠，味道非常苦，让你感到恶心。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/nuts.json
msgid "roasted acorns"
msgid_plural "roasted acorns"
msgstr[0] "烤橡实"

#. ~ Description of "roasted acorns"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/nuts.json
msgid "A handful of roasted nuts from an oak tree."
msgstr "一把橡实，已经烤熟了。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/nuts.json
msgid "cooked acorns"
msgid_plural "cooked acorns"
msgstr[0] "熟橡实"

#. ~ Description of "cooked acorns"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/nuts.json
msgid ""
"A serving of acorns that have been hulled, chopped, and boiled in water "
"before being thoroughly toasted until dry.  Filling and nutritious."
msgstr "将橡实去壳，剁碎，煮熟，然后彻底烤干制成。美味又顶饱。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/nuts.json
msgid "blanched acorns"
msgid_plural "blanched acorns"
msgstr[0] "橡实（浸透）"

#. ~ Description of "blanched acorns"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/nuts.json
msgid ""
"A handful of mushy blanched acorns.  No longer bitter, but not pleasant to "
"eat in this state."
msgstr "一把浸透了水的糊状橡实。不再苦涩，但在直接这样吃口感可不太好。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/nuts.json
msgid "blanching acorns"
msgid_plural "blanching acorns"
msgstr[0] "橡实（浸泡中）"

#. ~ Description of "blanching acorns"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/nuts.json
msgid ""
"A mix of water and hulled acorns, slowly leaching the tannins.  It'll take "
"about a week before they're palatable."
msgstr "水和去壳橡实的混合物，正在慢慢浸出单宁。约需一周才能令其变得适口。"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "blanching acorns"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/nuts.json
msgid ""
"After a week of changing water and taste-testing, the acorns are no longer "
"bitter and ready to decant."
msgstr "经过一周的换水和口味测试，橡实不再苦涩，可以滗水了。"

#. ~ "not_ready_msg" action message of item "blanching acorns"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/nuts.json
msgid "The acorns are still bitter."
msgstr "橡实依旧苦涩。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "faux gras"
msgid_plural "faux gras"
msgstr[0] "鹅肝酱"

#. ~ Description of "faux gras"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Though this meal is technically not foie gras, you have a feeling neither "
"the French nor animal rights groups are likely to criticize it now."
msgstr "虽然不是真正字面上的\"鹅\"肝酱，但你感觉，无论是法国人还是动保组织，现在都不太可能以任何方式批评它。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "liver & onions"
msgid_plural "liver & onions"
msgstr[0] "洋葱炒肝"

#. ~ Description of "liver & onions"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "A classic way to serve liver."
msgstr "一道经典的食用肝脏的菜式。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "fried liver"
msgid_plural "fried livers"
msgstr[0] "炸肝"

#. ~ Description of "fried liver"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "Tasty deep-fried liver, a Southern delicacy."
msgstr "美味的炸猪肝，一道南方美食。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "humble pie"
msgid_plural "humble pies"
msgstr[0] "内脏馅饼"

#. ~ Description of "humble pie"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Also known as 'Umble' pie, made with chopped organ meats.  Not half bad, and"
" full of vitamins!"
msgstr "又被称为\"卑微者的馅饼\"，采用切碎的内脏做馅。虽然在以前只有地位低微的人会吃，但尝起来还不赖，甚至还充满了维生素！"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "stewed tripe"
msgid_plural "stewed tripes"
msgstr[0] "炖肚条"

#. ~ Description of "stewed tripe"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Stomach lining, cut up and stewed for an hour in broth.  Better than it "
"sounds."
msgstr "胃，切碎，放进汤里慢慢煨，吃起来比听起来更美味。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "deep-fried tripe"
msgid_plural "deep-fried tripes"
msgstr[0] "油炸肚条"

#. ~ Description of "deep-fried tripe"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Some people don't enjoy the taste or texture of organ meat, so deep-frying "
"is a great way to disguise both."
msgstr "有些人不喜欢内脏肉的味道或质地，所以油炸是解决这种问题的好方法。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "leverpostej"
msgid_plural "leverpostej"
msgstr[0] "丹麦式肉酱"

#. ~ Description of "leverpostej"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid ""
"A traditional Danish pate.  Probably better if you spread it on some bread."
msgstr "一种传统丹麦菜肴，采用绞碎的内脏肉制成的肉酱。最好是抹在面包上吃。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "fried brain"
msgid_plural "fried brains"
msgstr[0] "油炸脑子"

#. ~ Description of "fried brain"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid ""
"I don't know what you were expecting.  It's brain.  It's deep-fried.  Enjoy!"
msgstr "你可别对它抱太大期望了。这依然是个脑子，只是被油炸了一遍，好好享受吧！"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "deviled kidney"
msgid_plural "deviled kidneys"
msgstr[0] "酱制腰子"

#. ~ Description of "deviled kidney"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid ""
"A delicious way to prepare kidneys, originating from Victorian England.  You"
" had to make some substitutions in the devilling sauce, but it still came "
"out damn good."
msgstr "一种烹饪肾脏的美味方法，起源于维多利亚时代的英国。虽然你只能用别的调料来替代“魔鬼酱”，但最后的味道依然很棒。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "grilled sweetbread"
msgid_plural "grilled sweetbreads"
msgstr[0] "煎杂碎"

#. ~ Description of "grilled sweetbread"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "Not sweet like the name would suggest, but delicious all the same!"
msgstr "吃起来一点也不甜，但仍然美味。（注：杂碎英文被称为sweetbread）"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "canned liver"
msgid_plural "canned livers"
msgstr[0] "罐装肝脏"

#. ~ Description of "canned liver"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "Livers preserved in a can.  Chock-full of B vitamins!"
msgstr "在罐子里密封保存的肝脏。富含维生素B！"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "lung provence"
msgid_plural "lung provences"
msgstr[0] "普罗旺斯香草肺片"

#. ~ Description of "lung provence"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid ""
"A French lung dish, made by poaching the lungs before pan-frying them with "
"onion, tomato, seasonings, and a generous amount of wine."
msgstr "一种法式肺脏料理，先将肺煮熟，然后与洋葱、番茄、调味料和大量葡萄酒一起煎。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "töttchen"
msgid_plural "töttchens"
msgstr[0] "明斯特炖杂碎"

#. ~ Description of "töttchen"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid ""
"A German peasant dish that converts many less-desirable meat cuts and organs"
" into a palatable meal with the liberal application of butter, sugar, and "
"wine."
msgstr "一种德国农家菜，将许多不太受欢迎的肉块和器官变为可口的菜肴，主要是靠大量使用黄油、糖和酒。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "scrambled eggs and brain"
msgid_plural "scrambled eggs and brains"
msgstr[0] "脑花炒蛋"

#. ~ Description of "scrambled eggs and brain"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "Brain and eggs, why didn't you ever think to put these together?"
msgstr "脑花加蛋，以前怎么就没想到把它们凑一对儿呢？"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "sausage casing"
msgid_plural "sausage casings"
msgstr[0] "肠衣"

#. ~ Description of "sausage casing"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Sausage casings made from animal intestines.  Ready to be used for forming "
"meat products."
msgstr "用动物的肠子制成的肠衣，可以用来装香肠。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "artificial sausage casing"
msgid_plural "artificial sausage casings"
msgstr[0] "人造肠衣"

#. ~ Description of "artificial sausage casing"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Sausage casings made from plastic bags.  Ready to be used for forming meat "
"products."
msgstr "用塑料制成的肠衣，可以用来装香肠。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/offal_dishes.json
msgid "homemade hot dog"
msgid_plural "homemade hot dogs"
msgstr[0] "自制热狗"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "diet pill"
msgid_plural "diet pills"
msgstr[0] "减肥药"

#. ~ Description of "diet pill"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Not very nutritious.  Warning: contains calories, unsuitable for "
"breatharians."
msgstr ""
"一份没什么营养物质的减肥药。\n"
"警告：含卡路里，呼吸主义者慎用。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "slime glob"
msgid_plural "slime globs"
msgstr[0] "变形怪糊"

#. ~ Description of "slime glob"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A little hunk of glop that fell off a slime monster.  It doesn't seem "
"hostile, but it does wiggle occasionally."
msgstr "一小块从变形怪身上掉下的糊状物，似乎已经没有了敌意，但偶尔会蠕动几下。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "honey comb"
msgid_plural "honey combs"
msgstr[0] "蜂巢块"

#. ~ Description of "honey comb"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A large chunk of wax filled with honey.  Very tasty."
msgstr "一大块涂满了蜂蜜的蜡，超级美味。"

#. ~ Description of "wax"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A large chunk of beeswax.  Not very tasty or nourishing, but okay in an "
"emergency."
msgstr "一大块蜂蜡，既不好吃又不滋补，除非实在没东西吃了。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "royal jelly"
msgid_plural "royal jellies"
msgstr[0] "蜂王浆"

#. ~ Description of "royal jelly"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A translucent hexagonal chunk of wax, filled with dense, milky, bitter and "
"acidic-tasting jelly.  Though some hold it as a panacea, it doesn't have any"
" medical benefit.  Still it is rich with the most beneficial substances the "
"hive can produce."
msgstr ""
"一大块涂满了粘稠 "
"、乳白色液体的半透明蜂窝蜡，尝起来有点苦涩和酸味。虽然有些人认为它是灵丹妙药，但它其实没有任何疗效。不过尽管如此它依然富含蜂群能制造的营养物质。"

#. ~ It takes about 30 portions of honeydew to feed an adult (~2000 kkal).
#. 2000 kkal is about 10 raw chunks of mutant meat, which is 250% toxins.
#. Honeydew probably isn't as toxic as meat, so 30 portions of it would give
#. you 180% of toxins.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "honeydew"
msgid_plural "honeydews"
msgstr[0] "蜜露"

#. ~ It takes about 30 portions of honeydew to feed an adult (~2000 kkal).
#. 2000 kkal is about 10 raw chunks of mutant meat, which is 250% toxins.
#. Honeydew probably isn't as toxic as meat, so 30 portions of it would give
#. you 180% of toxins.
#. ~ Description of "honeydew"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A sugar-rich sticky substance, produced by aphids from plant sap.  Ants and "
"bees love it."
msgstr "一种富含糖的粘性物质，由吸取植物汁液的蚜虫产生。蚂蚁和蜜蜂都喜欢它。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "Marloss seed"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "Marloss berry"
msgid_plural "Marloss berries"
msgstr[0] "马洛斯变异梅"

#. ~ Description of "Marloss berry"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"This looks like a blueberry the size of your fist, but pinkish in color.  It"
" has a strong but delicious aroma, but is clearly either mutated or of alien"
" origin."
msgstr "这看起来像拳头大小的蓝莓，但却有粉红色的颜色。香气浓郁，芬芳扑鼻，但显然经过了变异，或许是外星产物也说不准。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Marloss gelatin"
msgid_plural "Marloss gelatin"
msgstr[0] "马洛斯凝胶"

#. ~ Description of "Marloss gelatin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"This looks like a handful of lemon-colored liquid which has taken a set, "
"much like pre-Cataclysm Jello.  It has a strong but delicious aroma, but is "
"clearly either mutated or of alien origin."
msgstr "这看起来就像凝固住的柠檬色液体，活像末日前的果冻。香气浓郁，芬芳扑鼻，但显然经过了变异，或许是外星产物也说不准。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Mycus fruit"
msgid_plural "Mycus fruits"
msgstr[0] "马卡斯果"

#. ~ Description of "Mycus fruit"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Humans might call this a Gray Delicious apple: large, gray, and smells even "
"better than the Marloss.  If they didn't reject it for its alien origins.  "
"But we know better."
msgstr "人类也许称其为美味灰苹果：大且灰白，香味更甚于马洛斯梅。若那些人类不因其起源于异界而排斥，将会更加美妙。但吾等更清楚。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "yeast"
msgid_plural "yeast"
msgstr[0] "酵母"

#. ~ Description of "yeast"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A powder-like mix of cultured yeast, good for baking and brewing alike."
msgstr "一份人工培育的粉末状酵母，可以用于烘培或者酿造。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "koji"
msgid_plural "koji"
msgstr[0] "清酒酒曲"

#. ~ Description of "koji"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Some ground rice covered with a special kind of mold used for "
"saccharification and fermentation in Japanese cuisine."
msgstr "一些表面覆盖着一种特殊的霉菌的碎米，在日本料理中用于糖化和发酵。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "bone meal"
msgid_plural "bone meal"
msgstr[0] "骨粉"

#. ~ Description of "bone meal"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "This bone meal can be used to craft fertilizer and some other things."
msgstr "一份骨粉，可以用来制造肥料和其他物品。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "powdered gelatin"
msgid_plural "powdered gelatin"
msgstr[0] "明胶粉"

#. ~ Description of "powdered gelatin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Dried and powdered gelatin, used as a gelling agent when mixed with water."
msgstr "经过烘干的粉状明胶，当与水混合后变成凝胶。"

#. ~ Same as the meat it's been made from.  It's additional ingredient
#. compared to smoking, jerking, and dehydrating, so there's no incentive
#. otherwise.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "fresh gelatin"
msgid_plural "fresh gelatin"
msgstr[0] "新鲜明胶"

#. ~ Same as the meat it's been made from.  It's additional ingredient
#. compared to smoking, jerking, and dehydrating, so there's no incentive
#. otherwise.
#. ~ Description of "fresh gelatin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Fresh gelatin.  Not vegan-friendly!"
msgstr "新鲜的明胶。不适合素食主义者！"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "tainted bone meal"
msgid_plural "tainted bone meal"
msgstr[0] "被感染的骨粉"

#. ~ Description of "tainted bone meal"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "This is a grayish bone meal made from rotten bones."
msgstr "腐烂骨头制成的灰色骨粉。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "chitin powder"
msgid_plural "chitin powder"
msgstr[0] "甲壳粉"

#. ~ Description of "chitin powder"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"This chitin powder can be used to craft fertilizer and some other things."
msgstr "一份甲壳粉，可以用来制造肥料和其他物品。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "napkin"
msgid_plural "napkins"
msgstr[0] "纸巾"

#. ~ Description of "napkin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A napkin.  Can be used for fires."
msgstr "一张纸巾。可以用来生火。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "cardboard"
msgid_plural "cardboards"
msgstr[0] "硬纸板"

#. ~ Description of "cardboard"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A piece of cardboard."
msgstr "一片硬纸板。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "canned beans"
msgid_plural "canned beans"
msgstr[0] "罐装豆子"

#. ~ Description of "canned beans"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Canned beans.  A staple among canned goods, these are reputedly good for "
"one's coronary health."
msgstr "罐装豆子。罐头食品的标志性产品，据说有利于冠动脉健康。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "dried beans"
msgid_plural "dried beans"
msgstr[0] "干菜豆"

#. ~ Description of "dried beans"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Dehydrated great northern beans.  Tasty and nutritious when cooked, "
"virtually inedible when dry."
msgstr "脱水的大北豆。煮熟以后美味又营养，但是干燥状态几乎不能食用。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "cooked beans"
msgid_plural "cooked beans"
msgstr[0] "熟菜豆"

#. ~ Description of "cooked beans"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A hearty serving of cooked great northern beans."
msgstr "一份丰盛的水煮大北豆。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "tofu"
msgid_plural "tofu"
msgstr[0] "豆腐"

#. ~ Description of "tofu"
#. ~ Description of "fried tofu"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Tofu, a soy protein crucial to East Asian cuisine.  It absorbs flavors very "
"well and can be used as a meat alternative in many dishes."
msgstr "豆腐，一道在东亚菜系中占据重要地位的菜肴，富含蛋白质。它能很好地吸收风味，在许多菜肴中可作为肉类替代品。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "fried tofu"
msgid_plural "fried tofu"
msgstr[0] "炸豆腐"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "dehydrated tofu"
msgid_plural "dehydrated tofu"
msgstr[0] "脱水豆腐"

#. ~ Description of "dehydrated tofu"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Dehydrated tofu, sealed and still extra firm to last a long time."
msgstr "脱水豆腐，被密封保存。可以保存相当久的时间不腐坏。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "soybeans"
msgid_plural "soybeans"
msgstr[0] "大豆"

#. ~ Description of "soybeans"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Light brown beans, they have many uses, mildly toxic and not recommended, "
"but you could eat them raw."
msgstr "一种淡棕色的豆子，有很多用途，有轻微的毒性。可以生吃，但不推荐。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "raw edamame"
msgid_plural "raw edamames"
msgstr[0] "生毛豆"

#. ~ Description of "raw edamame"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Light green raw edamame still in its pod, you should boil or freeze these, "
"or you could eat them while they are still toxic."
msgstr "淡绿色生毛豆被豆荚包裹着。你应该煮沸或冷冻处理后使用，直接食用可能会中毒。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "dried lentils"
msgid_plural "dried lentils"
msgstr[0] "干扁豆"

#. ~ Description of "dried lentils"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A humble but nutrient-rich legume.  Should be cooked prior to consumption."
msgstr "一种不起眼但富含营养的豆类。食用前应该先煮熟。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "blood rice pudding"
msgid_plural "blood rice pudding"
msgstr[0] "血米布丁"

#. ~ Description of "blood rice pudding"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Blood rice pudding is a pastry made from blood and rice grains.  Best with "
"chopped peanuts, but also good to eat with various seasonings."
msgstr "血米布丁是一种用血和大米做成的糕点。最好搭配花生碎，也可以搭配各种调料食用。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Foodplace's delicious food™"
msgid_plural "Foodplace's delicious food™"
msgstr[0] "美食广场美食™"

#. ~ Description of "Foodplace's delicious food™"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The best-seller from Foodplace, delicious food™, is made with real foodstuff"
" and is guaranteed 100% edible!"
msgstr "美食广场最畅销的产品，美食广场美食™，用真正的食物制成，并保证100%可食用！"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Foodplace's appropriate snack™"
msgid_plural "Foodplace's appropriate snack™"
msgstr[0] "美食广场合适小吃™"

#. ~ Description of "Foodplace's appropriate snack™"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Real foodstuff now in a pocket size format!"
msgstr "真正食品现在被做成能轻松装进你口袋的合适大小！"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "cooked lentils"
msgid_plural "cooked lentils"
msgstr[0] "熟扁豆"

#. ~ Description of "cooked lentils"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Some delicious cooked lentils.  Humble but nutrient-rich."
msgstr "一些美味的煮扁豆，普通但营养丰富。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "coffee powder"
msgid_plural "coffee powder"
msgstr[0] "咖啡粉"

#. ~ Description of "coffee powder"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Ground coffee beans.  You can boil it into a mediocre stimulant, or "
"something better if you had an atomic coffee pot."
msgstr "磨碎的咖啡豆。可以加水煮成普通咖啡当作兴奋剂使用，或者使用原子咖啡机将其制成效果更强的玩意。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Kentucky coffee grounds"
msgid_plural "Kentucky coffee grounds"
msgstr[0] "肯塔基咖啡粉"

#. ~ Description of "Kentucky coffee grounds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Coffee grounds created through washing, cleaning, and roasting the pods from"
" a Kentucky coffeetree.  They can be used to create coffee."
msgstr "通过清洗、清洁和烘烤来自肯塔基州咖啡树的豆荚而形成的咖啡粉。它们可以用来制造类似咖啡的饮品。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "candied honey"
msgid_plural "candied honey"
msgstr[0] "结晶蜂蜜"

#. ~ Description of "candied honey"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Honey, that stuff the bees make.  This variant is \"candied honey\", a "
"variant of very thick consistence.  This honey won't spoil and is good for "
"your digestion."
msgstr "一份由蜜蜂酿造的蜂蜜。这种蜂蜜又被叫做\"结晶蜂蜜\"，是一种浓稠的蜂蜜。它不会腐坏变质，而且能帮助消化。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "canned tomato"
msgid_plural "canned tomatoes"
msgstr[0] "罐装番茄"

#. ~ Description of "canned tomato"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Canned tomato.  A staple in many pantries, and useful for many recipes."
msgstr "罐装番茄。厨房里常见的罐头食品，可以做很多种菜。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "embalmed human brain"
msgid_plural "embalmed human brains"
msgstr[0] "人脑标本"

#. ~ Description of "embalmed human brain"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"This is a human brain soaked in a solution of highly toxic formaldehyde.  "
"Eating this would be a terrible idea."
msgstr "一个浸泡在含有剧毒的福尔马林中的人脑。吃下它会是个十分糟糕的主意。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/items/petfoods.json
msgid "cattle fodder"
msgid_plural "cattle fodder"
msgstr[0] "家畜饲料"

#. ~ Description of "cattle fodder"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"What cattle eat.  Mainly made of grass, silage or legumes.  It's perfect for"
" ruminants."
msgstr "一些喂养家畜用的饲料，主要由草、青贮饲料或豆类等制成，适合奶牛等牲畜食用。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "bird food"
msgid_plural "bird food"
msgstr[0] "鸟食"

#. ~ Description of "bird food"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"What birds eat.  Mainly made of seeds, silage or legumes.  It's perfect for "
"small birds."
msgstr "一些主要由种子、青贮或一些豆类制成的鸟食，小型鸟类非常喜欢吃。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/items/petfoods.json
msgid "wet dog food"
msgid_plural "wet dog food"
msgstr[0] "半湿犬粮"

#. ~ Description of "wet dog food"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"This is wet food for dogs, made from canned fresh meats.  It smells strange,"
" but dogs seem to love it."
msgstr "半湿犬粮，用罐装鲜肉制成。闻起来很奇怪，但是狗狗喜欢。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/items/petfoods.json
msgid "dry dog food"
msgid_plural "dry dog food"
msgstr[0] "干犬粮"

#. ~ Description of "dry dog food"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Dry morsels of dog food with a long shelf life.  Made from dried processed "
"meats and grains, and enriched with vitamins and minerals."
msgstr "有较长保质期的干犬粮。由加工过的肉类和谷物制成，富含维生素和矿物质。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/items/petfoods.json
msgid "wet cat food"
msgid_plural "wet cat food"
msgstr[0] "半湿猫粮"

#. ~ Description of "wet cat food"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"This is wet food for cats, made from canned fresh meats.  It has a pungent "
"aroma that cats seem to love."
msgstr "半湿猫粮，用罐装鲜肉制成。闻起来有点刺鼻，但是猫猫喜欢。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/items/petfoods.json
msgid "dry cat food"
msgid_plural "dry cat food"
msgstr[0] "干猫粮"

#. ~ Description of "dry cat food"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Dry kibbles of cat food with a long shelf life.  Made from dried processed "
"meats and grains, and enriched with vitamins and minerals."
msgstr "有较长保质期的干猫粮。由加工过的肉类和谷物制成，富含维生素和矿物质。"

#. ~ Description of "grass"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Some grass, edible by grazers and ruminants only.  Seeing this item is a "
"bug."
msgstr "一些草，只能被食草动物和反刍动物食用。该物品不应该出现在正常游戏中。"

#. ~ Description of "underbrush"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Some underbrush, edible by ruminants only.  Seeing this item is a bug."
msgstr "一些矮灌木丛，只能被反刍动物食用。该物品不应该出现在正常游戏中。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "nectar"
msgid_plural "nectars"
msgstr[0] "花蜜"

#. ~ Description of "nectar"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Some nectar.  Seeing this item is a bug."
msgstr "一些花蜜。该物品不应该出现在正常游戏中。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "black tea bag"
msgid_plural "black tea bags"
msgstr[0] "红茶包"

#. ~ Description of "black tea bag"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A paper sachet with tea leaves inside.  Put it into boiling water to make a "
"cup of black tea."
msgstr "一个装满了茶叶的小纸袋。把它丢进一杯开水里就能泡出红茶了。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "green tea bag"
msgid_plural "green tea bags"
msgstr[0] "绿茶包"

#. ~ Description of "green tea bag"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A paper sachet with tea leaves inside.  Put it into boiling water to make a "
"cup of green tea."
msgstr "一个装满了茶叶的小纸袋。把它丢进一杯开水里就能泡出绿茶了。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "fruit tea bag"
msgid_plural "fruit tea bags"
msgstr[0] "果茶包"

#. ~ Description of "fruit tea bag"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A paper sachet with leaves and fruit parts inside.  Put it into boiling "
"water to make a cup of fruit tea."
msgstr "一个装满了草叶和干果的小纸袋。把它丢进一杯开水里就能泡出果茶了。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "herbal tea bag"
msgid_plural "herbal tea bags"
msgstr[0] "草药茶包"

#. ~ Description of "herbal tea bag"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A paper sachet with dried wild herbs inside.  Put it into boiling water to "
"make a cup of herbal tea."
msgstr "一个装满了干草药的小纸袋。把它丢进一杯开水里就能泡出草药茶了。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "dandelion tea bag"
msgid_plural "dandelion tea bags"
msgstr[0] "蒲公英茶包"

#. ~ Description of "dandelion tea bag"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A paper sachet with dried dandelion roots inside.  Put it into boiling water"
" to make a cup of dandelion tea."
msgstr "一个装满了干蒲公英根茎的小纸袋。把它丢进一杯开水里就能泡出蒲公英茶了。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "chamomile tea bag"
msgid_plural "chamomile tea bags"
msgstr[0] "甘菊茶包"

#. ~ Description of "chamomile tea bag"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A paper sachet with dried chamomile inside.  Put it into boiling water to "
"make a cup of chamomile tea."
msgstr "一个装满了干洋甘菊的小纸袋。把它丢进一杯开水里就能泡出甘菊茶了。"

