msgstr[0] "水发蔬菜"

#. ~ Description of "rehydrated vegetable"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Reconstituted vegetable flakes, which are much more enjoyable to eat now "
"that they have been rehydrated."
msgstr "一些脱水后再水发的蔬菜片，泡过水再吃更美味了。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "rehydrated corn kernels"
msgid_plural "rehydrated corn kernels"
msgstr[0] "水发玉米粒"

#. ~ Description of "rehydrated corn kernels"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Reconstituted corn kernels, much more enjoyable to eat now that they have "
"been rehydrated."
msgstr "一些脱水后再水发的玉米粒，泡过水再吃更美味了。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "vegetable salad"
msgid_plural "vegetable salads"
msgstr[0] "蔬菜沙拉"

#. ~ Description of "vegetable salad"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "A salad made with all kind of vegetables."
msgstr "一盘什锦蔬菜沙拉，营养丰富。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "dried salad"
msgid_plural "dried salads"
msgstr[0] "方便沙拉"

#. ~ Description of "dried salad"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid ""
"A dried salad packed in a box with mayonnaise and ketchup.  Add water to "
"enjoy."
msgstr "包装在小盒子里的干燥沙拉和蛋黄酱、番茄汁，加入净水就能开始享用了。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "insta-salad"
msgid_plural "insta-salads"
msgstr[0] "即食沙拉"

#. ~ Description of "insta-salad"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid ""
"A dried salad with water added, not very tasty but still a decent "
"substitution for real salad."
msgstr "泡好的方便沙拉，距离真正的沙拉还是有差距的，但是至少能吃。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "baked dahlia root"
msgid_plural "baked dahlia roots"
msgstr[0] "烤大丽花根"

#. ~ Description of "baked dahlia root"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Baking this dahlia root has broken down the starch, making it softer and "
"sweeter."
msgstr "烤过的大丽花根已经分解了其中的部分淀粉，这使它变得更加柔软和香甜。"

#. ~ From Oregon Trail. Be prepared to lose it as soon as your wagon tips
#. over.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "roasted salsify"
msgid_plural "roasted salsifies"
msgstr[0] "烤蒜叶婆罗门参"

#. ~ From Oregon Trail. Be prepared to lose it as soon as your wagon tips
#. over.
#. ~ Description of "roasted salsify"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Now that it's been properly cooked, this salsify tastes vaguely like "
"oysters.  Makes a great side dish."
msgstr "这份已经烤熟的蒜叶婆罗门参，味道有点像牡蛎，是一道很好的配菜。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "sushi rice"
msgid_plural "sushi rice"
msgstr[0] "寿司饭"

#. ~ Description of "sushi rice"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "A serving of sticky vinegared rice, commonly used in sushi."
msgstr "制造寿司时使用的粘醋饭。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "onigiri"
msgid_plural "onigiri"
msgstr[0] "饭团"

#. ~ Description of "onigiri"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid ""
"A triangular block of tasty sushi rice with a healthy green vegetable folded"
" around it."
msgstr "一块三角形的美味饭团，用一些绿色蔬菜包裹着。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "vegetable hosomaki"
msgid_plural "vegetable hosomaki"
msgstr[0] "蔬菜细卷"

#. ~ Description of "vegetable hosomaki"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Delicious chopped vegetables wrapped in tasty sushi rice and rolled up in a "
"healthy green vegetable."
msgstr "将蔬菜切成小条然后用紫菜包起来的寿司卷。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "dehydrated alien fungus chunk"
msgid_plural "dehydrated alien fungus chunks"
msgstr[0] "脱水异界真菌块"

#. ~ Description of "dehydrated alien fungus chunk"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Pieces of alien mushroom that have been dried to prevent them from rotting "
"away.  They will still poison you if you eat them."
msgstr "经过脱水以防止它们腐烂的异界真菌块。依旧有毒不宜食用。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "sauerkraut"
msgid_plural "sauerkraut"
msgstr[0] "德式酸菜"

#. ~ Description of "sauerkraut"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid ""
"This crunchy, sour topping made from lettuce or cabbage is perfect for your "
"hot dogs and hamburgers, or, if you're desperate, straight to your stomach."
msgstr "这种脆脆、酸酸的泡菜由莴苣或是卷心菜制成，配上热狗和汉堡就最完美了。不过紧要关头也可以直接吃下肚。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "nopalito"
msgid_plural "nopalitos"
msgstr[0] "仙人掌嫩茎"

#. ~ Description of "nopalito"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "A less prickly version of cactus pads."
msgstr "少刺的食用仙人掌，吃起来更\"顺滑\"。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "boiled fiddleheads"
msgid_plural "boiled fiddleheads"
msgstr[0] "煮蕨菜"

#. ~ Description of "boiled fiddleheads"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "Boiled fiddleheads.  Not bad, but would be better sauteed in butter."
msgstr "一份煮熟的蕨菜叶。吃起来还不差，但要是用点黄油煎一下就更棒了。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "sauteed fiddleheads"
msgid_plural "sauteed fiddleheads"
msgstr[0] "煎蕨菜"

#. ~ Description of "sauteed fiddleheads"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "Fiddleheads sauteed in fat.  Tender and delicious."
msgstr "用油煎过的蕨菜。软嫩而美味。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "sauteed Jerusalem artichoke"
msgid_plural "sauteed Jerusalem artichokes"
msgstr[0] "炒洋姜"

#. ~ Description of "sauteed Jerusalem artichoke"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Most of this artichoke's inulin has been converted into fructose after "
"cooking, and it now tastes pleasantly sweet."
msgstr "这种洋姜所含的大部分菊糖在烹饪后都转化为果糖，现在尝起来很甜。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "boiled Jerusalem artichoke"
msgid_plural "boiled Jerusalem artichokes"
msgstr[0] "煮洋姜"

#. ~ Description of "boiled Jerusalem artichoke"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Still crunchy but much more palatable than raw, with a slight nutty taste."
msgstr "煮熟的洋姜仍然很脆，但比生的更可口，还有一点坚果味。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "cooked bell pepper"
msgid_plural "cooked bell peppers"
msgstr[0] "炖灯笼椒"

#. ~ Description of "cooked bell pepper"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid ""
"A cored and cooked bell pepper.  It is far more enjoyable now that the seeds"
" are removed."
msgstr "一份去核并煮熟的灯笼椒。去掉籽之后吃起来更美味。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid "prepared ground nuts"
msgid_plural "prepared ground nuts"
msgstr[0] "熟美洲花生"

#. ~ Description of "prepared ground nuts"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Ground nuts that have been peeled and then boiled, to destroy the harmful "
"protease inhibitors.  Safe to eat, but need further cooking to become "
"palatable.  Can be used much like potatoes."
msgstr "去皮然后煮沸的美洲花生，以破坏有害的蛋白酶抑制剂。可以安全食用，但需要进一步烹饪才能变得可口。烹饪方法和土豆差不多。"

#. ~ Description of "boiled ground nuts"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/veggy_dishes.json
msgid ""
"Boiled ground nuts.  They look and taste a little like potatoes, but with a "
"slight nutty taste."
msgstr "煮熟的美洲花生。它们的外观和味道有点像土豆，但带有轻微的坚果味。"

#. ~ Description of "wheat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "Raw wheat, not very tasty."
msgstr "一些生小麦，直接食用不佳。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "boiled grain"
msgid_plural "boiled grain"
msgstr[0] "熟麦"

#. ~ Description of "boiled grain"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"Whole wheat or barley kernels that have been boiled in water.  Very bland on"
" their own, but will do if you can't prepare them in a different way."
msgstr "用水煮熟的全麦或大麦仁。它们本身毫无滋味，但如果你实在想不出其他的吃法，也能吃饱吧。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "raw spaghetti pasta"
msgid_plural "raw spaghetti pasta"
msgstr[0] "生意大利面"

#. ~ Description of "raw spaghetti pasta"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"A type of pasta usually used when preparing spaghetti.  It could be eaten "
"raw if you're desperate, but is much better cooked."
msgstr "一种用来做意大利面的面条。当你饿的不行时，生吃也不是不可以，但是弄熟了之后会好吃得多。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "raw lasagne pasta"
msgid_plural "raw lasagne pasta"
msgstr[0] "生千层面"

#. ~ Description of "raw lasagne pasta"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"A pasta sheet used in making lasagne.  It could be eaten raw if you're "
"desperate, but is much better cooked."
msgstr "一片用来做千层面的生面。当你饿的不行时，生吃也不是不可以，但是弄熟了之后会好吃得多。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "boiled noodles"
msgid_plural "boiled noodles"
msgstr[0] "煮面条"

#. ~ Description of "boiled noodles"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "Fresh wet noodles.  Fairly bland, but fills you up."
msgstr "新鲜的煮面条，虽然乏味，但比啃树根好。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "raw macaroni"
msgid_plural "raw macaroni"
msgstr[0] "生通心粉"

#. ~ Description of "raw macaroni"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "It could be eaten raw if you're desperate, but is much better cooked."
msgstr "当你饿得不行时，生吃也没什么影响，当然，弄熟了再吃最好不过。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "mac & cheese"
msgid_plural "mac & cheese"
msgstr[0] "芝士通心粉"

#. ~ Description of "mac & cheese"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "When the cheese starts flowing, Kraft gets your noodle going."
msgstr "上面覆盖着奶酪的通心粉，好香啊！"

#. ~ 240 ml is equivalent to 1 cup of flour.  10 charges is roughly equivalent
#. to a cup of flour for American recipes.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "flour"
msgid_plural "flour"
msgstr[0] "面粉"

#. ~ 240 ml is equivalent to 1 cup of flour.  10 charges is roughly equivalent
#. to a cup of flour for American recipes.
#. ~ Description of "flour"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "This enriched white flour is useful for baking."
msgstr "这白色的面粉可以用来做成面包。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "bread flour"
msgid_plural "bread flour"
msgstr[0] "高筋面粉"

#. ~ Description of "bread flour"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"This white flour is useful for adding more stretch and chew to bread while "
"baking."
msgstr "这种白面粉有助于在烘烤时增加面包的弹性和咀嚼性。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "oatmeal"
msgid_plural "oatmeal"
msgstr[0] "生麦片"

#. ~ Description of "oatmeal"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"Dry flakes of flattened grain.  Tasty and nutritious when cooked, it also "
"doubles as food for horses while dry."
msgstr "扁平的谷物干片。烹饪后美味和营养并存，干的时候也可以作为马的食物。"

#. ~ Description of "oats"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "Raw oats."
msgstr "生燕麦。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "cooked oatmeal"
msgid_plural "cooked oatmeal"
msgstr[0] "煮麦片"

#. ~ Description of "cooked oatmeal"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"A filling and nutritious New England classic that has sustained pioneers and"
" captains of industry alike."
msgstr "新英格兰经典食物，饱肚子有营养。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "deluxe cooked oatmeal"
msgid_plural "deluxe cooked oatmeal"
msgstr[0] "特级煮麦片"

#. ~ Description of "deluxe cooked oatmeal"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"A filling and nutritious New England classic that has been improved with the"
" addition of extra wholesome ingredients."
msgstr "新英格兰经典食物，饱肚子有营养，更加入了新配方。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "pancake"
msgid_plural "pancakes"
msgstr[0] "薄饼"

#. ~ Description of "pancake"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "Fluffy and delicious pancakes with real maple syrup."
msgstr "用枫糖浆做的松软又美味的煎饼。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "fruit pancake"
msgid_plural "fruit pancakes"
msgstr[0] "水果薄饼"

#. ~ Description of "fruit pancake"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"Fluffy and delicious pancakes with real maple syrup, made sweeter and "
"healthier with the addition of wholesome fruit."
msgstr "用枫糖浆做的松软又美味的煎饼，加了水果之后更加健康和香甜。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "blodplättar"
msgid_plural "blodplättars"
msgstr[0] "血煎饼"

#. ~ Description of "blodplättar"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"Blodplättar is not your average pancake.  It does not taste of blood at all "
"and it tastes like a crispier black pudding."
msgstr "血煎饼不是一般的煎饼。它一点血的味道也没有，尝起来像一个更脆的黑布丁。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "French toast"
msgid_plural "French toasts"
msgstr[0] "法式吐司"

#. ~ Description of "French toast"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "Slices of bread dipped in a milk and egg mixture then fried."
msgstr "切片的面包浸过奶蛋糊之后炸成。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "waffle"
msgid_plural "waffles"
msgstr[0] "华夫饼"

#. ~ Description of "waffle"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"Hey it's waffle time, it's waffle time.  Won't you have some waffles of "
"mine?"
msgstr "嗨，华夫饼时间到了，华夫饼时间到了。你不想来一块我的华夫饼吗？"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "fruit waffle"
msgid_plural "fruit waffles"
msgstr[0] "水果华夫饼"

#. ~ Description of "fruit waffle"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"Crunchy and delicious waffles with real maple syrup, made sweeter and "
"healthier with the addition of wholesome fruit."
msgstr "嘎嘣脆的美味华夫饼浇上枫糖浆，配上水果使它更甜、更健康。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
#: data/mods/My_Sweet_Cataclysm/sweet_monsters.json
msgid "cracker"
msgid_plural "crackers"
msgstr[0] "薄脆饼干"

#. ~ Description of "cracker"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "Dry and salty, these crackers will leave you quite thirsty."
msgstr "一些又咸又干的饼干，味道不错，但吃完会让你口渴。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgctxt "oyster crackers"
msgid "oyster crackers"
msgid_plural "oyster crackers"
msgstr[0] "牡蛎饼干"

#. ~ Description of "oyster crackers"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"These bite-sized crackers go well with soups, but will make you thirsty on "
"their own."
msgstr "这些一口大小的饼干适合用来配汤，但直接吃会让你很口渴。"

#. ~ these vitamins are only for pies that may spawn.  generally they will be
#. inherited from the fruit used.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "fruit pie"
msgid_plural "fruit pies"
msgstr[0] "水果派"

#. ~ these vitamins are only for pies that may spawn.  generally they will be
#. inherited from the fruit used.
#. ~ Description of "fruit pie"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "A delicious baked pie with a sweet fruit filling."
msgstr "一个放满了香甜水果的烤派，非常美味且营养丰富。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "cheese pizza"
msgid_plural "cheese pizzas"
msgstr[0] "奶酪披萨"

#. ~ Description of "cheese pizza"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "A delicious pizza with molten cheese on top."
msgstr "一份铺满融化奶酪的美味披萨。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "granola"
msgid_plural "granola"
msgstr[0] "格兰诺拉燕麦卷"

#. ~ Description of "granola"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"A tasty and nutritious mixture of oats, honey, and other ingredients that "
"has been baked until crisp."
msgstr "一份由燕麦片、蜂蜜和其他原料制成的燕麦卷，烘烤至香脆可口，美味且营养丰富。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "maple pie"
msgid_plural "maple pies"
msgstr[0] "枫糖馅饼"

#. ~ Description of "maple pie"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "A sweet and delicious baked pie with pure maple syrup."
msgstr "一块香甜可口的馅饼派，加了纯净的枫树糖浆烘烤制成。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "fast noodles"
msgid_plural "fast noodles"
msgstr[0] "方便面"

#. ~ Description of "fast noodles"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "So-called ramen noodles.  Can be eaten raw."
msgstr "一份方便面，是种可在短时间之内用热水泡熟食用的面制食物，亦可直接食用。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "cloutie dumpling"
msgid_plural "cloutie dumplings"
msgstr[0] "克罗蒂甜糕"

#. ~ Description of "cloutie dumpling"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid ""
"This traditional Scottish treat is a sweet and filling little boiled cake "
"studded with dried fruit."
msgstr "苏格兰传统美食，嵌入很多果干的水煮小糕点。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "brioche"
msgid_plural "brioches"
msgstr[0] "法式奶油面包卷"

#. ~ Description of "brioche"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "Filling bread buns, taste good with tea on a Sunday morning breakfast."
msgstr ""
"一个介于甜点和面包之间的法式面点，用大量鸡蛋和黄油制成，外皮金黄酥脆，内部超级柔软，口感极佳，入口即化。\n"
"\"吃不起面包，就吃蛋糕呗！——玛丽·安东尼特 皇后\""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "sponge cake"
msgid_plural "sponge cakes"
msgstr[0] "海绵蛋糕"

#. ~ Description of "sponge cake"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "Plain, fluffy cake for the proletariat."
msgstr "为无产阶级准备的普通松软的蛋糕。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "space cake"
msgid_plural "space cakes"
msgstr[0] "太空蛋糕"

#. ~ Description of "space cake"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "This cake's destiny is to take you on a gnarly trip."
msgstr "这块\"叶子\"味的蛋糕会伴随你渡过艰苦的旅途。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "brownie"
msgid_plural "brownies"
msgstr[0] "布朗尼蛋糕"

#. ~ Description of "brownie"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "A rich chocolate brownie, just like how grandma used to bake them."
msgstr ""
"一份包括坚果、霜状白糖、生奶油、巧克力的蛋糕，发源于19世纪末的美国。\n"
"\"这个和外婆做的完全一样。\""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "'special' brownie"
msgid_plural "'special' brownies"
msgstr[0] "特制布朗尼蛋糕"

#. ~ Description of "'special' brownie"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/wheat.json
msgid "This is definitely not how grandma used to bake them."
msgstr ""
"一份包括坚果、霜状白糖、生奶油、巧克力的蛋糕，发源于19世纪末的美国。\n"
"\"这个和外婆做的完全不一样。\""

