"rounds into a shotgun's tube in a much shorter period of time than by hand."
"  It needs to interface with a chute to be used with any speed."
msgstr "一根带滑动手柄的塑料管，能够比手工装填更快地将 6 发霰弹装入霰弹枪中。它需要与枪上的滑槽接口对接，才能快速使用。"

#. ~ Magazine name
#: data/json/items/magazine/shot.json
msgid "shotgun 8-round speedloader"
msgid_plural "shotgun 8-round speedloaders"
msgstr[0] "8发快速装弹器（霰弹）"

#. ~ Description of magazine "shotgun 8-round speedloader"
#: data/json/items/magazine/shot.json
msgid ""
"A plastic tube with a sliding handle that can be used to quickly load 8 "
"rounds into a shotgun's tube in a much shorter period of time than by hand."
"  It needs to interface with a chute to be used with any speed."
msgstr "一根带滑动手柄的塑料管，能够比手工装填更快地将 8 发霰弹装入霰弹枪中。它需要与枪上的滑槽接口对接，才能快速使用。"

#. ~ Magazine name
#: data/json/items/magazine/shot.json
msgid "M26-MASS 3-round magazine"
msgid_plural "M26-MASS 3-round magazines"
msgstr[0] "M26-MASS 3发弹匣"

#. ~ Description of magazine "M26-MASS 3-round magazine"
#: data/json/items/magazine/shot.json
msgid "A small 3-round box magazine for the M26-MASS underbarrel shotgun."
msgstr "一个小型3发盒式弹匣，可用于M26-MASS下挂霰弹枪。"

#. ~ Magazine name
#: data/json/items/magazine/shot.json
msgid "M26-MASS 5-round magazine"
msgid_plural "M26-MASS 5-round magazines"
msgstr[0] "M26-MASS 5发弹匣"

#. ~ Description of magazine "M26-MASS 5-round magazine"
#: data/json/items/magazine/shot.json
msgid "A small 5-round box magazine for the M26-MASS underbarrel shotgun."
msgstr "一个小型5发盒式弹匣，可用于M26-MASS下挂霰弹枪。"

#. ~ Magazine name
#: data/json/items/magazine/weldgas.json
msgid "small welding tank"
msgid_plural "small welding tanks"
msgstr[0] "小型焊接气瓶"

#. ~ Description of magazine "small welding tank"
#: data/json/items/magazine/weldgas.json
msgid ""
"A compact steel cylinder designed for holding pressurized welding gases.  It"
" is marked with several faded and now unreadable symbols."
msgstr "一个紧凑的钢制圆筒，用于保存加压焊接气体。上面有着几个现已褪色无法分辨的标记。"

#. ~ Magazine name
#: data/json/items/magazine/weldgas.json
msgid "welding tank"
msgid_plural "welding tanks"
msgstr[0] "焊接气瓶"

#. ~ Description of magazine "welding tank"
#: data/json/items/magazine/weldgas.json
msgid ""
"A large steel cylinder designed for holding pressurized welding gases.  It "
"is marked with several faded and now unreadable symbols."
msgstr "一个大型钢制圆筒，用于保存加压焊接气体。上面有着几个现已褪色无法分辨的标记。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "war flail"
msgid_plural "war flails"
msgstr[0] "战斗连枷"

#. ~ Description of "war flail"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A stout pole with a large flanged mace head attached to the end with a short"
" chain, a purpose-made combat version of the peasant flail.  It specializes "
"in threshing people in metal armor, rather than grain."
msgstr "一根结实的杆子，末端用一条短链连接着一个带凸缘的大锤矛，是农民连枷的特制战斗版本。它专门用来给穿着金属盔甲的人脱粒，而不是谷物。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "peasant flail"
msgid_plural "peasant flails"
msgstr[0] "农用连枷"

#. ~ Description of "peasant flail"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A stout pole with a wooden club attached to the end with a leather cord.  "
"This farming tool was historically used to thresh wheat and occasionally "
"people when the peasants got angry at their feudal lords."
msgstr "一根结实的杆子，末端用皮绳连接着一根木棒。这种农具在历史上被用来给小麦脱粒，当农民对他们的封建领主感到愤怒时，偶尔也用来打人。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "baseball bat"
msgid_plural "baseball bats"
msgstr[0] "棒球棍"

#. ~ Description of "baseball bat"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A sturdy wooden bat with a plastic handle.  Makes a great melee weapon."
msgstr "一根结实的木制棒球棍，塑料握把，揍起人来既顺手又给力。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "aluminum bat"
msgid_plural "aluminum bats"
msgstr[0] "铝质棒球棍"

#. ~ Description of "aluminum bat"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"An aluminum baseball bat with a plastic handle, lighter than a wooden bat "
"and a little easier to swing as a result."
msgstr "一个铝制棒球棍，塑料握把，比木制棒球棍要轻，因此更易挥舞。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "foam rubber bat"
msgid_plural "foam rubber bats"
msgstr[0] "泡沫橡胶球棒"

#. ~ Description of "foam rubber bat"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A baseball bat made of foam rubber with a plastic handle.  Light and easy to"
" wield, but almost completely ineffective if your goal is to hurt someone."
msgstr "一根用泡沫橡胶制成的棒球棒，带一个塑料手柄。轻巧且趁手，但如果你打算用来打人，这东西完全造成不了什么伤害。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "expandable baton"
msgid_plural "expandable batons"
msgstr[0] "甩棍"

#. ~ Description of "expandable baton"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A telescoping baton that collapses for easy storage.  Right now, it's "
"collapsed.  Activate to expand."
msgstr "一把叠缩式短棍，缩小后更易于携带。现在已经被折叠起来，激活以伸出。"

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "expandable baton"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "collapsed boarding axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/armor/exosuit/exosuit_modules.json
msgid "Expand"
msgstr "展开"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "expandable baton"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "You snap open your baton."
msgstr ""
"\"咻——咔\"\n"
"你甩出你的甩棍。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "expandable baton (extended)"
msgid_plural "expandable batons (extended)"
msgstr[0] "甩棍（展开）"

#. ~ Description of "expandable baton (extended)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A telescoping baton that collapses for easy storage.  Makes a good melee "
"weapon.  Activate to collapse."
msgstr "一把叠缩式短棍，缩小后更易于携带。这是一件不错的的近战武器。激活以收回。"

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "expandable baton (extended)"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "boarding axe"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "C.R.I.T axe"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "The Iron Whip"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/armor/exosuit/exosuit_melee.json
#: data/mods/CRT_EXPANSION/items/crt_tools.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_belts.json
msgid "Collapse"
msgstr "折叠"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "expandable baton (extended)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "You collapse your baton."
msgstr "你折好你的甩棍。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "battle axe"
msgid_plural "battle axes"
msgstr[0] "战斧"

#. ~ Description of "battle axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A huge axe designed for warfare.  Though intended for use as a weapon, it "
"can also be pressed into service as a rather clumsy woodcutting tool."
msgstr "一柄起源于欧洲的战斧，长长的斧柄的一端装有双头斧刃。虽然只建议作为武器使用，但也可以勉强当作一把相当笨拙的伐木工具。"

#. ~ Description of "battle axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A dull, cheaply-made replica of a huge axe designed for warfare."
msgstr "一柄起源于欧洲的战斧，长长的斧柄的一端装有双头斧刃。此款外观、造型和材料与正品有差异，为廉价复制品。"

#. ~ Description of "battle axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A huge axe designed for warfare.  Or it would be, but the axe heads aren't "
"seated properly at all."
msgstr "一柄起源于欧洲的战斧，长长的斧柄的一端装有双头斧刃。这本来应该是一把真正的战斧，但斧头没有被正确安好。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "blackjack"
msgid_plural "blackjacks"
msgstr[0] "皮革短槌"

#. ~ Description of "blackjack"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A short, easily concealed bludgeoning weapon consisting of a weight embedded"
" at the end of a short leather shaft.  Formerly used by law enforcement, "
"this weapon is meant to stun or knock out the subject, although head strikes"
" have a high risk of causing a permanent, disabling brain injury or being "
"fatal."
msgstr ""
"一把便于藏匿的短槌，由皮革制成的手柄加上顶端的配重制成。以前被执法部门使用，主要用于眩晕或击晕目标，但是对头部的攻击仍然有很高的概率造成永久性致残的脑损伤，甚至致命。"

#. ~ Not actually as damaging as a steel katana, by any stretch.  It's a
#. fancy, very well-carved wooden training sword, not a weapon of war.  It's
#. also completely rounded, so any cutting damage wouldn't make sense.  Also,
#. the heaviest bokken I could find were 700g, none were nearly close to a
#. kilogram.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "bokken"
msgid_plural "bokken"
msgstr[0] "日式木刀"

#. ~ Not actually as damaging as a steel katana, by any stretch.  It's a
#. fancy, very well-carved wooden training sword, not a weapon of war.  It's
#. also completely rounded, so any cutting damage wouldn't make sense.  Also,
#. the heaviest bokken I could find were 700g, none were nearly close to a
#. kilogram.
#. ~ Description of "bokken"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A solid wood 'training' katana, exactingly crafted to mimic the weight and "
"balance of the real thing.  Despite its lack of a sharp metal edge, it's "
"still quite capable of inflicting deadly wounds."
msgstr ""
"一柄训练用的木刀，严格模仿真正武士刀的重量和平衡，尽管缺乏一个锋利的刀锋，但它仍然有相当的能力去造成致命的伤害。\n"
"“洞 爷 湖”"

#. ~ Description of "bokken"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A solid wood 'training' katana.  It feels far too light to make an effective"
" weapon."
msgstr "一柄训练用的木刀，但手感太轻了，不是一把好武器。"

#. ~ Description of "bokken"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A solid wood 'training' katana.  It looks to be mass-produced, and not quite"
" as effective as the real deal."
msgstr "一柄训练用的木刀，看上去像是批量生产的便宜货，不如纯手工打造的真品那么好用。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "The 7-10 Split"
msgid_plural "7-10 Splits"
msgstr[0] "7-10分屏锤"

#. ~ Description of "The 7-10 Split"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"An improvised weapon made from a bowling pin with two spikes attached in the"
" shape of a 'T'."
msgstr "一把由保龄球瓶制成的简易武器，上面固定有两根尖刺，呈‘T’字形。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "bowling pin"
msgid_plural "bowling pins"
msgstr[0] "保龄球瓶"

#. ~ Description of "bowling pin"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A standard bowling pin.  Makes a decent melee weapon, if somewhat short."
msgstr "一只标准保龄球瓶。你非要当成武器去砸丧尸也行，就是有点短。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "barbed wire bat"
msgid_plural "barbed wire bats"
msgstr[0] "铁丝棒球棍"

#. ~ Description of "barbed wire bat"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A baseball bat wrapped with barbed wire.  A brutal melee weapon."
msgstr "一根在顶部缠绕了几道带刺铁丝网的棒球棒，野蛮的近战武器。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "walking cane"
msgid_plural "walking canes"
msgstr[0] "步行手杖"

#. ~ Description of "walking cane"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"Handicapped or not, you always walk in style.  Consisting of a metal "
"headpiece and a wooden body, this makes a great bashing weapon in a pinch."
msgstr ""
"甭管腿脚棒不棒，走路一定要时尚，\n"
"金属包头木手杖，关键时刻敲小丧。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "sinister cane"
msgid_plural "sinister canes"
msgstr[0] "邪恶手杖"

#. ~ Description of "sinister cane"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A sinister looking cane made of plastic.  It has a shiny red orb gripped by "
"claws at the handle."
msgstr "一根看起来很邪恶的塑料手杖。它的把手上有个爪子，抓着一颗闪亮的红球。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "cheap wizard cane (off)"
msgid_plural "cheap wizard canes (off)"
msgstr[0] "廉价法师手杖（关）"

#. ~ Description of "cheap wizard cane (off)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"An arcane but cheap-looking cane made of plastic.  It has a white light-up "
"orb on the end.  Using it will turn it on and provide a weak light."
msgstr "一根看起来很神秘但廉价的塑料手杖。它的把手顶部有个白色的发光球体。使用它会打开它，并提供些许微弱的光。"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "cheap wizard cane (off)"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "wizard cane (off)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "You turn the wizard cane on."
msgstr "你打开了法师手杖。"

#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "cheap wizard cane (off)"
#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "wizard cane (off)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "The wizard cane's batteries are dead."
msgstr "法师手杖的电池耗尽了。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "cheap wizard cane (on)"
msgid_plural "cheap wizard canes (on)"
msgstr[0] "廉价法师手杖（开）"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "cheap wizard cane (on)"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "wizard cane (on)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "You turn the wizard cane off."
msgstr "你关闭了法师手杖。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "wizard cane (off)"
msgid_plural "wizard canes (off)"
msgstr[0] "法师手杖（关）"

#. ~ Description of "wizard cane (off)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"An arcane-looking cane made of wood and aluminum.  It has a white light-up "
"orb on the end.  Using it will turn it on and illuminate the area around "
"you."
msgstr "一根看起来很神秘的手杖，用木头和铝合金制成。它的顶部有个白色的发光球体。使用它以打开，并照亮四周。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "wizard cane (on)"
msgid_plural "wizard canes (on)"
msgstr[0] "法师手杖（开）"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "makeshift walking cane"
msgid_plural "makeshift walking canes"
msgstr[0] "简易步行手杖"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift walking cane"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"An improvised cane.  It also works as a basic bashing weapon in a pinch."
msgstr "一根自制的拐杖。在紧要关头时可以用来当作简单的钝击武器。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "wooden club"
msgid_plural "wooden clubs"
msgstr[0] "木棒"

#. ~ Description of "wooden club"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A plank of wood that's been snapped in half, with a crude handle whittled "
"into one end.  It looks like a poorly-made cricket bat."
msgstr "一块被折成两半的木板，一端被削成一个粗糙的握柄，看起来像一个做工粗糙的板球拍。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "large wooden club"
msgid_plural "large wooden clubs"
msgstr[0] "大木棒"

#. ~ Description of "large wooden club"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A long plank of wood with a crude handle whittled into one end.  It's barely"
" an improvement, but at least it is slightly easier to wield than just the "
"plank on its own."
msgstr "一块长长的木板，一端被削成一个粗糙的握柄。和普通的木板相比几乎没什么改进，但至少更容易挥舞。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "crutches"
msgid_plural "pairs of crutches"
msgstr[0] "拐杖"

#. ~ Description of "crutches"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A pair of crutches."
msgstr "一双拐杖。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "makeshift crutches"
msgid_plural "pairs of makeshift crutches"
msgstr[0] "简易拐杖"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift crutches"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A pair of wooden makeshift crutches."
msgstr "一对自制的木头拐杖。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json data/mods/MMA/bludgeons.json
msgid "cudgel"
msgid_plural "cudgels"
msgstr[0] "长棍"

#. ~ Description of "cudgel"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A long, slender wooden rod.  While traditionally intended as a training "
"tool, it still makes a good melee weapon in a pinch."
msgstr "一根细长的木棍。虽然传统上是作为一种训练工具，但在紧要关头，它仍然是把好用的近战武器。"

#. ~ Id retained to avoid breaking anything, same reason as with the makeshift
#. glaive.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "makeshift macuahuitl"
msgid_plural "makeshift macuahuitls"
msgstr[0] "简易双刃剑"

#. ~ Id retained to avoid breaking anything, same reason as with the makeshift
#. glaive.
#. ~ Description of "makeshift macuahuitl"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A flat wooden club with sharpened pieces of stone stuck to both sides."
msgstr "一根扁平的木棍，两边贴有尖锐的石片。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "glass shiv"
msgid_plural "glass shivs"
msgstr[0] "碎玻璃刀"

#. ~ Description of "glass shiv"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A glass shard with wrapping at one end so it can be safely wielded."
msgstr "一片碎玻璃，一端已经被包扎好，可以安全地手持。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/weapons.json
msgid "golf club"
msgid_plural "golf clubs"
msgstr[0] "高尔夫球棍"

#. ~ Description of "golf club"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A long handle with a big metal head, flat on one side, for driving golf "
"balls.  Fore!"
msgstr ""
"一根金属柄，一头是击球金属头，用来驱动高尔夫球。\n"
"\"Fore！（高尔夫球术语）\""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "sledge hammer"
msgid_plural "sledge hammers"
msgstr[0] "大钢锤"

#. ~ Description of "sledge hammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A large, heavy hammer.  A very hard-hitting melee weapon, but it's slow to "
"swing and will probably exhaust you quickly."
msgstr "一把大而重的锤子，非常粗暴的近战武器。但它挥舞起来很慢，而且可能很快让你筋疲力尽。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "short sledge hammer"
msgid_plural "short sledge hammers"
msgstr[0] "短钢锤"

#. ~ Description of "short sledge hammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A sledge hammer with a notably shorter handle.  This makes it worse as a "
"melee weapon, but a more portable tool."
msgstr "一个手柄明显较短的大钢锤，作为近战武器没那么好用，但却是一种更便携的工具。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "engineer's hammer"
msgid_plural "engineer's hammers"
msgstr[0] "工程师锤"

#. ~ Description of "engineer's hammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A stout and hefty hammer, more akin to a sledge than a typical ball-peen.  "
"Useful for portable demolition work, but very unwieldy as a weapon."
msgstr "一把结实而有分量的锤子，相比于一般的圆头锤，更像一把大钢锤。作为一把便携工具，在拆除工作中十分有用，但作为武器用起来十分笨拙。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "heavy sledge hammer"
msgid_plural "heavy sledge hammers"
msgstr[0] "重钢锤"

#. ~ Description of "heavy sledge hammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A large sledge hammer with a massive, heavy head.  This unwieldy tool is "
"meant to break concrete, rock, brick, anything really."
msgstr "一把巨大的钢锤，有着一个同样巨大而沉重的锤头。这个笨重的工具能轻易砸碎混凝土、岩石、砖块，任何东西。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "hockey stick"
msgid_plural "hockey sticks"
msgstr[0] "曲棍球棒"

#. ~ Description of "hockey stick"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A curved wooden stick with a wide and flat end.  Commonly used by hockey "
"players."
msgstr "一端弯曲扁平的木棍，冰球和曲棍球运动员的常用器材。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "homewrecker"
msgid_plural "homewreckers"
msgstr[0] "寡妇制造者"

#. ~ Description of "homewrecker"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A long piece of wood with several chunks of steel firmly tied to it.  The "
"resulting weapon is unwieldy and slow but very heavy hitting."
msgstr "一长条被几块钢铁紧紧包裹的木头。这使得这件武器笨重和缓慢，但可以造成沉重的打击。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "ironshod quarterstaff"
msgid_plural "ironshod quarterstaves"
msgstr[0] "镔铁长棍"

#. ~ Description of "ironshod quarterstaff"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A long wooden staff reinforced with metal bands and caps."
msgstr ""
"一根长木棍，两端箍上金属圈并装上金属包头来加固。\n"
"\"吃俺老孙一棒！\""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "L-stick (off)"
msgid_plural "L-sticks (off)"
msgstr[0] "光棒（关）"

#. ~ Description of "L-stick (off)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"Produced by the Light corporation, this stylish staff functions not just as "
"a light source, but also a lightweight weapon thanks to its superalloy "
"construction.  Due to proprietary efficiency improvements over standard "
"light sources, batteries last longer in the L-stick."
msgstr ""
"这根时尚的手杖由Light公司生产，得益于其超合金结构，它不仅能用作光源，也可以作为轻型武器。原本的标准光源经过专门的能效改进，在维持标准光照强度的同时能耗减半。"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "L-stick (off)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "The L-stick™ lights up."
msgstr "光棒™亮了起来。"

#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "L-stick (off)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "The L-stick's™ batteries are empty."
msgstr "光棒™的电池耗尽了。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "L-stick (on)"
msgid_plural "L-sticks (on)"
msgstr[0] "光棒（开）"

#. ~ Description of "L-stick (on)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"Produced by the Light corporation, this stylish staff functions not just as "
"a light source, but also a lightweight weapon thanks to its superalloy "
"construction.  Due to proprietary efficiency improvements over standard "
"light sources, batteries last longer in the L-stick.  The staff is glowing "
"brightly, which is slowly draining the batteries."
msgstr ""
"这根时尚的手杖由Light公司生产，得益于其超合金结构，它不仅能用作光源，也可以作为轻型武器。原本的标准光源经过专门的能效改进，在维持标准光照强度的同时能耗减半。光棒正在发光，慢慢地消耗着电池。"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "L-stick (on)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "The L-stick's™ light fades away."
msgstr "光棒™失去了光亮。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "lucerne hammer"
msgid_plural "lucerne hammers"
msgstr[0] "琉森锤"

#. ~ Description of "lucerne hammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A versatile polearm with a spiked hammer head, a spike, and a hook attached "
"to a beefy wooden pole."
msgstr ""
"一把多功能的长柄武器，上面有一个钉锤头（又称鸦喙），一个矛头，和一道弯钩。由于其针对各种目标的广泛适应性，在骑兵作战中大放异彩，实用主义派冷兵器的顶尖之作。"

#. ~ Description of "lucerne hammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A cheap piece of crap imitation of a versatile polearm with a spiked hammer "
"head, probably meant to be used for LARPing."
msgstr "一把多功能长柄武器的拙劣仿制品，上面有一个钉锤头，也许只是用来Cosplay的。"

#. ~ Same total damage and slightly higher weight than a morningstar -
#. exchanged.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "mace"
msgid_plural "maces"
msgstr[0] "钉头槌"

#. ~ Same total damage and slightly higher weight than a morningstar -
#. exchanged.
#. ~ Description of "mace"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a wood handle with a heavy metal head.  It "
"is heavy and slow to swing, but its crushing damage is devastating."
msgstr "一柄中世纪武器，木把手顶端有个沉重的金属块，曾作为骑兵突袭的主要武器。虽然非常沉，挥舞起来也很慢，但它的粉碎打击是毁灭性的。"

#. ~ Description of "mace"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A light, cheaply-made replica of a medieval weapon that would normally "
"consist of a wood handle with a heavy metal head."
msgstr "一柄中世纪武器，木把手顶端有个沉重的金属块，曾作为骑兵突袭的主要武器。这把是廉价的复制品。"

#. ~ Description of "mace"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a wood handle with a heavy metal head.  The "
"head feels a bit loose."
msgstr "一柄中世纪武器，木把手顶端有个沉重的金属块，曾作为骑兵突袭的主要武器。这把的锤头有点松了。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "simple mace"
msgid_plural "simple maces"
msgstr[0] "简易狼牙棒"

#. ~ Description of "simple mace"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A stick with a circular lump of metal tied to it in a facsimile of a mace.  "
"You could probably improve it by finding a way to pin the head to the "
"handle."
msgstr "一根木棍，上面套着一块环形金属，像是一把狼牙棒。你也许能找到某种方法，将锤头进一步同握把固定，来提升它的耐用程度。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "trench mace"
msgid_plural "trench maces"
msgstr[0] "战壕狼牙棒"

#. ~ Description of "trench mace"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A mace made from a circular chunk of steel pinned to the end of a stick.  "
"You can feel your inner Trench Raider come alive when you wield it."
msgstr "一根狼牙棒，由钉在棍子末端的圆形钢块构成。当你挥舞它时，你可以感觉到自己体内的战壕奇兵之魂复活了。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "pipe mace"
msgid_plural "pipe maces"
msgstr[0] "钢管狼牙棒"

#. ~ Description of "pipe mace"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A pipe with a handful of pipe fittings screwed onto the end to give it a "
"weighty head for bashing."
msgstr "一根一头拧上了一大堆管道连接件的钢管，使它头部变得很沉，适合用来砸人。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "great pipe mace"
msgid_plural "great pipe maces"
msgstr[0] "钢管狼牙巨棒"

#. ~ Description of "great pipe mace"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"Two pipes fitted end-to-end with more pipe fittings screwed onto the far "
"end.  The result is a large, but awkward bludgeon."
msgstr "两根钢管端对端连接在一起，一头拧上了更多的管道连接件。结果是一根巨大但笨拙的大棒子。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "pipe staff"
msgid_plural "pipe staffs"
msgstr[0] "钢管长棍"

#. ~ Description of "pipe staff"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"Three pipes fitted end-to-end in a monstrously heavy facsimile of a "
"quarterstaff."
msgstr "三根钢管端对端连接在一起，变成了一根笨重得可怕的武术长棍的复制品。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "bronze mace"
msgid_plural "bronze maces"
msgstr[0] "青铜钉头槌"

#. ~ Description of "bronze mace"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"While nothing more than a bronze sphere on a stick, it is still surprisingly"
" effective."
msgstr "虽然只不过是安在棍子上的一个青铜球，但它仍然出人意料地有效。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "makeshift sap"
msgid_plural "makeshift saps"
msgstr[0] "简易皮革短槌"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift sap"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"An improvised sap, also known as a cosh, slapjack and slapper.  A short, "
"flat bludgeoning weapon consisting of a weight embedded between two patches "
"of leather."
msgstr "一根简易皮革短槌，用两片皮革夹住一块配重，制成的扁平钝击武器。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json data/mods/Magiclysm/items/melee.json
msgid "Mjölnir"
msgid_plural "Mjölnirs"
msgstr[0] "Mjölnir，雷神之锤"

#. ~ Description of "Mjölnir"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A large hammer, forged from the heart of a dying star.  It bears the inscription:\n"
"\n"
"Whosoever holds this hammer,\n"
"If he be worthy,\n"
"Shall possess the power to…\n"
"CRUSH!'"
msgstr ""
"一把名为妙尔尼尔的神锤，用白矮星的星核打造。上面有着一道铭文：\n"
"\n"
"执此锤者，\n"
"如其适格，\n"
"当承神威以……\n"
"摧毁！！"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "morningstar"
msgid_plural "morningstars"
msgstr[0] "晨星锤"

#. ~ Description of "morningstar"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a wood handle with a heavy, spiked metal "
"ball on the end.  It deals devastating crushing damage, and the spikes "
"easily puncture soft targets."
msgstr ""
"一柄中世纪的武器，木柄上面附有一个满是尖刺的金属球，步兵对付具甲骑兵的主要武器之一，亦是骑兵间流行的杀敌利器。它能造成毁灭性的钝击伤害，而且尖刺很容易刺穿软体目标。\n"
"“带钉之锤形如晨星，耀眼且致命的诗意。”"

#. ~ Description of "morningstar"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A light, cheaply-made replica of a medieval weapon that would normally "
"consist of a wood handle with a heavy, spiked metal ball on the end."
msgstr "一柄中世纪的武器，木柄上面附有一个满是尖刺的金属球，步兵对付具甲骑兵的主要武器之一。这把是廉价的复制品。"

#. ~ Description of "morningstar"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a wood handle with a heavy, spiked metal "
"ball on the end.  The weight feels off on this one, and the spikes are "
"blunted."
msgstr "一柄中世纪的武器，木柄上面附有一个满是尖刺的铁球，步兵对付具甲骑兵的主要武器之一。这把的重量感觉不对，而且刺也变钝了。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "nail bat"
msgid_plural "nail bats"
msgstr[0] "钉头棒球棍"

#. ~ Description of "nail bat"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A baseball bat with several nails driven through it, an excellent melee "
"weapon."
msgstr "一根棒身插了几根钉子的棒球棒，强力的近战武器。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "nailboard"
msgid_plural "nailboards"
msgstr[0] "钉板"

#. ~ Description of "nailboard"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A plank of wood with several nails through one end; essentially a simple "
"mace.  Makes an acceptable melee weapon."
msgstr "一块木板，上面钉着许多锋利的尖钉，使钝击更能附加若干刺击伤害。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "pool cue"
msgid_plural "pool cues"
msgstr[0] "台球杆"

#. ~ Description of "pool cue"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A hardwood stick designed for hitting colorful balls around a felt table.  "
"Truly, the coolest of sports."
msgstr ""
"一个前细后粗的硬木台球杆，用于在桌面上击打一些五颜六色的台球。\n"
"“酒吧混斗的常规武器。”"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "PR-24 baton (extended)"
msgid_plural "PR-24 batons (extended)"
msgstr[0] "PR-24 甩棍（展开）"

#. ~ Description of "PR-24 baton (extended)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"The Monadnock PR-24 baton is a collapsible, lightweight, side-handle baton "
"used by law enforcement all over the world.  The PR designation is rumored "
"to mean Public Relations.  Activate to retract."
msgstr ""
"一根警棍——麦当客 PR-24甩棍是一种可伸缩的，轻量级，侧柄执法警棍，在全世界范围内被广泛使用。有人谣传说其名字中的PR意为公共关系，激活以收缩。"

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "PR-24 baton (extended)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "Retract"
msgstr "折叠"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "PR-24 baton (extended)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "You collapse your PR-24 baton."
msgstr "你折好你的 PR-24 甩棍。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "PR-24 baton (retracted)"
msgid_plural "PR-24 batons (retracted)"
msgstr[0] "PR-24 甩棍（叠起）"

#. ~ Description of "PR-24 baton (retracted)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"The Monadnock PR-24 baton is a collapsible, lightweight, side-handle baton "
"used by law enforcement all over the world.  The PR designation is rumored "
"to mean Public Relations.  Activate to extend."
msgstr ""
"一根警棍——麦当客 PR-24甩棍是一种可伸缩的，轻量级，侧柄执法警棍，在全世界范围内被广泛使用。有人谣传说其名字中的PR意为公共关系。激活以甩出内棍。"

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "PR-24 baton (retracted)"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "C.R.I.T hatchet"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "Belt of The Iron Whip"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "Biomancer shifting spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
#: data/mods/CRT_EXPANSION/items/crt_tools.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_belts.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_melee.json
msgid "Extend"
msgstr "展开"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "PR-24 baton (retracted)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "You snap open your PR-24 baton."
msgstr ""
"\"咻——咔！\"\n"
"你甩出了你的 PR-24 甩棍。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "quarterstaff"
msgid_plural "quarterstaves"
msgstr[0] "武术长棍"

#. ~ Description of "quarterstaff"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A sturdy staff carved out of wood.  Lightweight and long, it is surprisingly"
" easy to handle."
msgstr "一根用木头制成的结实棍棒。既轻且长，易于操作。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "bō"
msgid_plural "bō"
msgstr[0] "冲绳木棒"

#. ~ Description of "bō"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A wooden staff weapon used in Okinawan martial arts.  Finely sanded and "
"treated with oil for integrity."
msgstr "冲绳传统武术中所使用的木制棍棒。被人精细打磨并上油处理，确保其完好。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "rock in a sock"
msgid_plural "rocks in socks"
msgstr[0] "袜装石锤"

#. ~ Description of "rock in a sock"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A pair of nested socks with a stone tied inside.  A true weapon of "
"desperation."
msgstr "一对套在一起的袜子，里面装了个石头。绝对是绝境下才会使用的武器。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "plastic shank"
msgid_plural "plastic shanks"
msgstr[0] "塑料匕首"

#. ~ Description of "plastic shank"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"An oblong plastic object with the far end ground down into a stabbing point."
msgstr "一片长方形的塑料，一端被磨尖成匕首形状。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "shillelagh"
msgid_plural "shillelaghs"
msgstr[0] "爱尔兰木槌"

#. ~ Description of "shillelagh"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A stout, knotty stick with a large knob at the top that has been left to "
"cure in a chimney.  A traditional Irish weapon, the shillelagh was "
"originally used for settling disputes in a gentlemanly manner."
msgstr "一根短粗木棍，顶端有一个巨大的突起，在烟囱内熏制而成。这是一种传统的爱尔兰武器，最初用于以具有绅士风度的方式解决争端。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "loaded stick"
msgid_plural "loaded sticks"
msgstr[0] "配重木槌"

#. ~ Description of "loaded stick"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A stout knotty stick with a large knob at the top that has been left to cure"
" in a chimney.  A traditional Irish weapon, the shillelagh was originally "
"used for settling disputes in a gentlemanly manner.  The knob has been "
"hollowed and filled with molten heavy metal to pack more of a punch."
msgstr ""
"一根短粗的木棍，顶端有一个巨大的突起，在烟囱内熏制而成。这是一种传统的爱尔兰武器，最初用于以具有绅士风度的方式解决争端。这把木槌的突起被挖空浇铸了金属，具有更强的攻击力。"

#. ~ Description of "shillelagh"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A fake shillelagh massproduced as a souvenir for tourists.  This knotty "
"stick has not been cured in a chimney like a traditional shillelagh, but "
"instead has had fake black soot painted on."
msgstr "一根仿制的爱尔兰木槌，只是量产的纪念品。这根木槌没有像传统爱尔兰木槌一样在烟囱内熏制过，而是在上面涂上了假烟灰。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "powered quarterstaff"
msgid_plural "powered quarterstaves"
msgstr[0] "霹雳长棍"

#. ~ Description of "powered quarterstaff"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"An ironshod quarterstaff that has a high-voltage stun gun built into the "
"handle.  The stun gun is wired to the metal caps at either end of the staff,"
" allowing you to zap a dangerous opponent should beating them senseless with"
" it prove too hazardous."
msgstr ""
"一柄铁头木棒，内置有高压电击枪。电击枪发出的电流能传导至棍棒两端的金属帽上，如果碰到了光是用棍打不太安全的对手，可以不讲武德地把它电晕，再一顿痛殴。\n"
"\"电子兵器，小子。\""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "tactical tonfa (off)"
msgid_plural "tactical tonfas (off)"
msgstr[0] "战术拐（关）"

#. ~ Description of "tactical tonfa (off)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A reinforced plastic tonfa; the core is filled with capacitors and a high-"
"yield rechargeable storage battery.  When a switch on the handle is pressed,"
" a high-voltage current is transmitted to the two electrodes mounted in the "
"end of the tonfa, and by extension to anyone unfortunate enough to be in "
"contact with them.  It also has a nifty flashlight, which is off at the "
"moment."
msgstr ""
"一把强化的塑料警棍，内部装着电容与电池仓。当握把上的开关被按下去时，一股高压电流会被传导至安装在警棍顶端的两个电极上，然后输出给任何接触到电极的倒霉蛋身上。它还有个别致的小手电筒，现在处于关闭的状态。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "tactical tonfa (on)"
msgid_plural "tactical tonfas (on)"
msgstr[0] "战术拐（开）"

#. ~ Description of "tactical tonfa (on)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A reinforced plastic tonfa; the core is filled with capacitors and a high-"
"yield rechargeable storage battery.  When a switch on the handle is pressed,"
" a high-voltage current is transmitted to the two electrodes mounted in the "
"end of the weapon, and by extension to anyone unfortunate enough to be in "
"contact with them.  The integral flashlight is turned on, continually "
"draining power and lighting the surrounding area."
msgstr ""
"一根强化的塑料警棍，内部装着电容与电池仓。当握把上的开关被按下去时，一股高压电流会被传导至安装在警棍顶端的两个电极上，然后输出给任何接触到电极的倒霉蛋身上。它上面的手电筒已经开启，不断耗电来产生光亮。激活它来关闭。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "tonfa"
msgid_plural "tonfas"
msgstr[0] "T型拐"

#. ~ Description of "tonfa"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A hard plastic truncheon commonly employed by police.  Originally an "
"Okinawan weapon, it consists of a stick with a perpendicular handle attached"
" a third of the way down its length."
msgstr "一根通常被警察所使用的硬质塑料警棍。源自冲绳的土著武器，由棍身及垂直连接在主体的三分之一处的握把组成。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "wooden tonfa"
msgid_plural "wooden tonfas"
msgstr[0] "木拐"

#. ~ Description of "wooden tonfa"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A stout wooden truncheon of the sort commonly employed by police.  "
"Originally an Okinawan weapon, it consists of a stick with a perpendicular "
"handle attached a third of the way down its length."
msgstr "一个通常为警用的木头结实短棍。原本是源于冲绳的武器，在棍身三分之一处有着一个垂直的握柄。"

#. ~ Craftable from steel, shouldn't be silver.  A warhammer is essentially
#. one end of a pickaxe with balancing weight on the other and crushes/pierces
#. the armor.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "war hammer"
msgid_plural "war hammers"
msgstr[0] "战锤"

#. ~ Craftable from steel, shouldn't be silver.  A warhammer is essentially
#. one end of a pickaxe with balancing weight on the other and crushes/pierces
#. the armor.
#. ~ Description of "war hammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A medieval hammer with a spike on one end, made for battle.  Its odd shape "
"and balance make it an excellent weapon, but an ineffective tool."
msgstr "一把中世纪风格的战锤，一端有根尖刺。它古怪的外形和平衡使它成为一把优秀的武器，不过敲起钉子来就没有五金店里的锤子好用了。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/fake.json
msgid "bionic claws"
msgid_plural "bionic claws"
msgstr[0] "生化合金爪"

#. ~ Description of "bionic claws"
#: data/json/items/melee/fake.json
msgid "Short, sharp claws made from a high-tech metal."
msgstr "用高科技合金制成的爪子，短而锋利。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/fake.json
msgid "monomolecular blade"
msgid_plural "monomolecular blades"
msgstr[0] "单分子刀刃"

#. ~ Description of "monomolecular blade"
#: data/json/items/melee/fake.json
msgid ""
"A foot-long blade made from high-tech alloy and edged with bonded "
"nanocrystals."
msgstr "使用尖端科技打造的约一尺长的合金刀片，号称只有一个分子宽的纳米晶体组成了它的锋刃。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid "generic kitchen knife"
msgid_plural "generic kitchen knives"
msgstr[0] "通用菜刀"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid "butcher knife"
msgid_plural "butcher knives"
msgstr[0] "屠宰刀"

#. ~ Description of "butcher knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A sharp, heavy knife.  It makes a good melee weapon, and is an ideal item "
"for butchering corpses."
msgstr "一把锋利而厚重的刀子。是把不错的近战武器，也是用于屠宰尸体的理想工具。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid "steak knife"
msgid_plural "steak knives"
msgstr[0] "牛排刀"

#. ~ Description of "steak knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A sharp knife designed for cutting meat.  It makes a poor melee weapon, but "
"is decent at butchering corpses."
msgstr "一把较为尖锐、带有小锯齿的西餐餐具，设计用来在餐桌上切牛排。虽然是把很差劲的近战武器，但用来屠宰尸体还行。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid "paring knife"
msgid_plural "paring knives"
msgstr[0] "削皮刀"

#. ~ Description of "paring knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A short-bladed knife with a sharp blade, made for fine controlled cuts to "
"vegetables without using a cutting board."
msgstr "一把刀口锋利的短刃刀，可以在不使用砧板的情况下对蔬菜进行精细切割。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid "chef knife"
msgid_plural "chef knives"
msgstr[0] "厨刀"

#. ~ Description of "chef knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A long-bladed kitchen knife.  The blade is wider than the handle, giving "
"room for the wielder's knuckles, and it has a characteristic curve for a "
"fast rocking action for chopping vegetables.  It makes an acceptable melee "
"weapon, but the wide blade is unwieldy for butchering."
msgstr ""
"一把长刃菜刀。刀刃比把手宽，为持刀者的指关节提供了空间，刀刃的特殊曲线使它在切菜时可以快速来回摇动。作为近战武器还行，但宽大的刀身在屠宰时不太方便。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid "carving knife"
msgid_plural "carving knives"
msgstr[0] "切肉刀"

#. ~ Description of "carving knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A long-bladed kitchen knife with a thin, slightly curved blade for deftly "
"slicing meat either in flat sheets or around the bone.  It makes a decent "
"melee weapon, and is excellent for butchery."
msgstr "一把长刃菜刀，有一个轻薄、稍微弯曲的刀刃，能够灵巧地将肉切成薄片或剔除骨头。一把不错的近战武器，屠宰时也十分好用。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid "bread knife"
msgid_plural "bread knives"
msgstr[0] "面包刀"

#. ~ Description of "bread knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"This knife has quite a long blade with a scalloped edge for cutting bread.  "
"It's not that sharp, but its length and heft mean it could do a bit of "
"damage and cause some nasty tearing."
msgstr "这把刀有着很长的刀刃，刀刃呈扇形，用来切面包。它并不锋利，但它的长度和重量意味着它能够给敌人造成少许伤害，并导致撕裂伤。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid "vegetable cleaver"
msgid_plural "vegetable cleavers"
msgstr[0] "大菜刀"

#. ~ Description of "vegetable cleaver"
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A menacing-looking knife with a broad, square shaped blade, curved for fast "
"vegetable chopping.  Its heft and sharpness make it a decent weapon as well,"
" although not as good as a meat cleaver."
msgstr "一把看起来很凶险的刀，刀身宽大，呈方形，刀刃弯曲，能够快速切开蔬菜。它的分量和锋利度也使它成为一种不错的武器，虽然不如剁肉刀。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid "meat cleaver"
msgid_plural "meat cleavers"
msgstr[0] "剁肉刀"

#. ~ Description of "meat cleaver"
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A menacing-looking knife with a broad, square-shaped blade.  Its heft and "
"sharpness would make it a very effective melee weapon and an excellent "
"butchering tool."
msgstr "一把看起来很凶险的刀，刀身宽大，呈方形。它的重量和锋利度也使它成为一种非常有效的近战武器，也是一种优秀的屠宰工具。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/misc.json
msgid "bullwhip"
msgid_plural "bullwhips"
msgstr[0] "皮鞭"

#. ~ Description of "bullwhip"
#: data/json/items/melee/misc.json
msgid ""
"A long strip of braided leather with a handle on one end.  Originally "
"developed to settle disagreements with cattle, it's better used now for "
"flaying the rotten flesh off of walking corpses.  Great for when a problem "
"comes along."
msgstr ""
"一端有手柄的狭长皮鞭，本来是用来驱赶不听话的牛羊，但是现在可以防止行尸走肉靠近你。\n"
"\"你可以称之为吸血鬼杀手，但这个世界没有吸血鬼。\""

#. ~ There's no way you can swing this thing without hitting SOMETHING.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/misc.json
msgid "scourge"
msgid_plural "scourges"
msgstr[0] "九尾鞭"

#. ~ There's no way you can swing this thing without hitting SOMETHING.
#. ~ Description of "scourge"
#: data/json/items/melee/misc.json
msgid ""
"The \"cat 'o nine tails\", a handle with nine short leather whips, each "
"sporting a razor-sharp metal tip.  This ancient instrument of torture causes"
" massive bleeding, but by design is inefficient as a weapon."
msgstr ""
"九尾鞭，又被人称为“九尾猫”。一个带着九根短皮鞭的手柄，每根皮鞭的顶端都有锋利的金属尖刺。这种古老的酷刑手段能够导致大量出血，但作为武器使用时并不出色。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/misc.json
#: data/mods/Dark-Skies-Above/overrides/items/weapons.json
msgid "lobotomizer"
msgid_plural "lobotomizers"
msgstr[0] "开瓢器"

#. ~ Description of "lobotomizer"
#: data/json/items/melee/misc.json
msgid ""
"A hand-forged collapsible tool with two axe heads and a sharp shovel-like "
"tip on one end.  It can be used as a shovel, or you could chop some zombies "
"with it instead."
msgstr "一把手工锻造的可折叠工具，有两个斧刃，一头有一个锋利的铲子状尖端。它可以作为铲子使用，或者你也可以用它来给丧尸做脑白质切除手术。"

#. ~ Yes, this is smaller than its magazine well. Go with it.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/misc.json
msgid "stun gun"
msgid_plural "stun guns"
msgstr[0] "电击枪"

#. ~ Yes, this is smaller than its magazine well. Go with it.
#. ~ Description of "stun gun"
#: data/json/items/melee/misc.json
msgid ""
"A high-powered stun gun.  Use this item to attempt to electrocute an "
"adjacent enemy, temporarily paralyzing them."
msgstr "一把高能电击枪。激活以尝试电击身边的敌人，暂时使其瘫痪。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "pitchfork"
msgid_plural "pitchforks"
msgstr[0] "干草叉"

#. ~ Description of "pitchfork"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"An agricultural tool with a long wooden shaft and four spikes.  Normally "
"used to lift hay."
msgstr ""
"一杆农具，多用于农民用来翻干草堆，一杆长柄上有着四根分叉，作为武器时可将敌人缴械，同时格挡敌人的攻击，攻防兼备的近战利器。\n"
"“对某个白发猫眼的猎人有必杀效果。”"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "pointy stick"
msgid_plural "pointy sticks"
msgstr[0] "尖木棍"

#. ~ Description of "pointy stick"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A simple wooden pole with one end sharpened to a point."
msgstr "一根简单的木质长杆，一头被削尖。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "long pointy stick"
msgid_plural "long pointy sticks"
msgstr[0] "长尖木棍"

#. ~ Description of "long pointy stick"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A stout pole with one end sharpened to a point."
msgstr "一根结实的长杆，一头被削尖。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "fire-hardened wooden spear"
msgid_plural "fire-hardened wooden spears"
msgstr[0] "碳化木矛"

#. ~ Description of "fire-hardened wooden spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A stout wooden pole with a fire-hardened point."
msgstr "一根结实的木杆，尖端被火烤过而硬化。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "wooden spear"
msgid_plural "wooden spears"
msgstr[0] "木制长矛"

#. ~ Description of "wooden spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A stout wooden pole with a whittled point."
msgstr "一根结实的木杆，一头被雕刻得十分尖锐。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "sharpened spear shaft"
msgid_plural "sharpened spear shafts"
msgstr[0] "磨尖矛杆"

#. ~ Description of "sharpened spear shaft"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"You've gone through the effort of making a proper spear shaft, but instead "
"of attaching something sharp to the end you just whittled a point into the "
"wood.  The peak of pointy stick technology."
msgstr "你花了很大力气制作一个合适的矛杆，但你没有在末端装上任何尖锐的东西，而只是在木头上刻出了一个尖。不管怎样，这东西都代表了尖木棍技术的顶峰。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "makeshift war scythe"
msgid_plural "makeshift war scythes"
msgstr[0] "简易战斗镰刀"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift war scythe"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"This farming tool has been modified into an improvised weapon by rotating "
"its blade 90 degrees, transforming it into a deadly giant blade on the end "
"of a stick.  It's quite fragile, however."
msgstr "这种农用镰刀的刀刃旋转了90度，被改造成一种简易的武器，巨大而致命，就是不太耐用。"

#. ~ Name changed to simple makeshift glaive, but changing the id would break
#. e.g.  tilesets.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "simple makeshift glaive"
msgid_plural "simple makeshift glaives"
msgstr[0] "简陋长刀"

#. ~ Name changed to simple makeshift glaive, but changing the id would break
#. e.g.  tilesets.
#. ~ Description of "simple makeshift glaive"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A large blade attached to a stout section of tree branch.  It could do a "
"considerable amount of damage, but the blade isn't secured very well and "
"could easily break off."
msgstr "一把大刀安在一段粗壮的树枝上，可以造成相当大的伤害，但刀片不太稳固，可能很容易断掉。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "makeshift glaive"
msgid_plural "makeshift glaives"
msgstr[0] "简易长刀"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift glaive"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A stout tree branch that has been carefully split and reinforced.  At the "
"split point, a sharp blade has been bolted into place and reinforced with "
"layers of sturdy wrapped bindings."
msgstr "一个坚固的粗树枝，在一端劈开并栓接了一把锋利的刀刃，并且用几层结实的材料绑稳。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
#: data/mods/Dark-Skies-Above/overrides/items/weapons.json
msgid "spike on a stick"
msgid_plural "spikes on sticks"
msgstr[0] "铁刺木棍"

#. ~ Description of "spike on a stick"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A flimsy pole made of wood with a basic metal spike tied to it.  It's barely"
" sharp, and crudely constructed, but it will keep the zombies out of arm's "
"reach until you can find something better."
msgstr ""
"一个脆弱的长柄武器，由木棍上面绑上一个金属刺做成。不怎么锋利，制造水平不佳，但是在你找到更好的武器之前可以用来把丧尸拒于手臂的攻击范围之外。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "simple knife spear"
msgid_plural "simple knife spears"
msgstr[0] "简易刺刀长矛"

#. ~ Description of "simple knife spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A flimsy pole made of wood with a knife bound to the end.  It's long enough "
"to slice from a distance, but the knife isn't that well attached.  You could"
" take a bit more time to carefully split the shaft and attach the knife "
"blade more permanently."
msgstr ""
"一个脆弱的长柄武器，由木棍上面绑上一把刀制成。它的长度让你能够从较远距离攻击，但是刀绑得并不是很牢固。要是你多花一些时间，也许可以仔细劈开矛柄，然后更加持久地把刀刃固定到上面。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "makeshift knife spear"
msgid_plural "makeshift knife spears"
msgstr[0] "自制刺刀长矛"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift knife spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A long stick that has been carefully split and reinforced.  At the split "
"point, a sharp blade has been bolted into place and reinforced with layers "
"of sturdy wrapped bindings."
msgstr "一根长木棍，在一端劈开并栓接了一把锋利的刀刃，并且用几层结实的材料绑稳。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "knife spear"
msgid_plural "knife spears"
msgstr[0] "刺刀长矛"

#. ~ Description of "knife spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A stout wooden pole with the blade of a knife bolted into place at the end."
"  The shape of a knife blade isn't ideal for a spear, but it's still very "
"sharp and effective."
msgstr "一根结实的矛杆，末端栓接着一把刀刃。刀刃的形状对于长矛来说并不理想，但依然十分锋利好用。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "homemade halfpike"
msgid_plural "homemade halfpikes"
msgstr[0] "自制短矛"

#. ~ Description of "homemade halfpike"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A short do-it-yourself spear made out of a long stick with a metal spike "
"seated and bound into place at its tip."
msgstr "一根自制的短矛，长木棍的一端安装并固定有金属尖刺。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "crude steel spear"
msgid_plural "crude steel spears"
msgstr[0] "简易钢矛"

#. ~ Description of "crude steel spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A stout wooden pole with a misshapen metal spike seated into the end and "
"bolted into place."
msgstr "一根结实的矛杆，末端有一个奇形怪状的金属矛头，用螺栓固定住。"

#. ~ Block 2 until we re-implement defensive-disarm, I'm afraid.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "forked spear"
msgid_plural "forked spears"
msgstr[0] "木长叉"

#. ~ Block 2 until we re-implement defensive-disarm, I'm afraid.
#. ~ Description of "forked spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A wooden pole with three spikes tied to it.  It's specialized for catching "
"weapons, and not intended for extended use in combat."
msgstr "一根顶端绑上了三根尖刺的木头长棍。主要用于缴械，不能长时间作为近战武器使用。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "copper spear"
msgid_plural "copper spears"
msgstr[0] "铜制长矛"

#. ~ Description of "copper spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A stout wooden pole with a spearhead worked from copper."
msgstr "一根结实的木制长杆，附有锋利的铜制矛头。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "steel spear"
msgid_plural "steel spears"
msgstr[0] "钢矛"

#. ~ Description of "steel spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A stout wooden pole with a hand-forged steel spearhead."
msgstr "一根结实的木棍，配有手工钢质矛头。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "sharpened pipe"
msgid_plural "sharpened pipes"
msgstr[0] "磨尖钢管"

#. ~ Description of "sharpened pipe"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A pipe with one end cut off at an angle."
msgstr "一端被切断磨出尖角的钢管。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "basic pipe spear"
msgid_plural "basic pipe spears"
msgstr[0] "简易钢管长矛"

#. ~ Description of "basic pipe spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "Three pipes tightly fit together with one end cut down to a point."
msgstr "三根钢管被紧紧地固定在一起，其中一端被切断成矛尖。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "pipe spear"
msgid_plural "pipe spears"
msgstr[0] "钢管长矛"

#. ~ Description of "pipe spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"Three pipes tightly fit together with some wrappings for a handle around one"
" end and a sharp tip on the other."
msgstr "三根钢管被紧紧地固定在一起，其中一端有个握柄，另一端被磨尖成矛头。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "pointed rebar"
msgid_plural "pointed rebars"
msgstr[0] "尖钢筋"

#. ~ Description of "pointed rebar"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A rod of rebar that's been crudely hammered into a point."
msgstr "一根被锤子锤得锋利的钢筋。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "sharpened rebar"
msgid_plural "sharpened rebars"
msgstr[0] "磨尖钢筋"

#. ~ Description of "sharpened rebar"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A rod of rebar that's been cut and sharpened to a point."
msgstr "一根被切断并磨尖的钢筋。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "rebar spear"
msgid_plural "rebar spears"
msgstr[0] "钢筋长矛"

#. ~ Description of "rebar spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "Two rods of rebar welded together with a pointed tip."
msgstr "两根被焊接在一起的钢筋，一端十分尖利。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "qiang"
msgid_plural "qiang"
msgstr[0] "长枪"

#. ~ Description of "qiang"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"An ancient Chinese spear, typically with a tassel just below the spearhead "
"and larger than most European spears.  One of the four major weapons in "
"folklore, alongside the dao sabre, jian sword, and gun staff."
msgstr "一把古中国长枪，在枪头之下附有枪缨，比大多数欧洲矛要大。在民间传说中，属刀、剑、枪、棍四大兵器之一。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "halberd"
msgid_plural "halberds"
msgstr[0] "战戟"

#. ~ Description of "halberd"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A versatile polearm with an axe blade, a spike, and other fun things "
"attached to a long, sturdy stick."
msgstr "一把多功能的长柄武器，长粗木棍上固定有一个斧头，一个矛头，以及其他装饰。"

#. ~ Description of "halberd"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A dull, cheaply made replica of a polearm with an axe blade, a spike, and "
"other fun things attached to a thick pole."
msgstr "一把长柄武器的廉价拙劣复制品，粗木棍上固定有一个斧头，一个矛头，以及其他装饰。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "glaive"
msgid_plural "glaives"
msgstr[0] "长柄刀"

#. ~ Description of "glaive"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A sturdy polearm with a sizable single-edged blade on the end."
msgstr "一把结实的长柄武器，末端为一个相当长的单刃刀，形如偃月刀与朴刀，起源于威尔士。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "naginata"
msgid_plural "naginata"
msgstr[0] "薙刀"

#. ~ Description of "naginata"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A sturdy polearm with a curved blade, made in the same manner as the katana "
"and other Japanese blades.  Occasionally used by samurai in early periods, "
"or by their wives in defense of the household."
msgstr ""
"一根坚固耐用的长柄武器，顶部是一个采用和武士刀一样的日式刀具制造方法制成的弯曲利刃。在镰仓时代为步兵与僧侣的主力兵器，在江户时代则成为了武士家女性作为教养的必学项目。"

#. ~ Description of "naginata"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A sturdy polearm with a curved blade, made in the same manner as the katana "
"and other Japanese blades.  This one has a bit of wiggle to its blade and "
"feels a bit shoddily made."
msgstr "一把坚硬的带弯曲刀刃的长柄刀，用与武士刀和其他日本刀刃相同的方式制成。这把刀的刀刃有点晃动，感觉有点粗制滥造。"

#. ~ Description of "naginata"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A dull, slightly floppy replica of a Japanese polearm with a curved blade.  "
"With a little difficulty, you could use it administer a solid slap from a "
"distance."
msgstr "一把无光泽，还有点松动的复制品：带着弯曲刀片的日本薙刀。花点力气，你就可以用它从远处拍出一记结实的耳光。"

#. ~ Description says it can slash. STAB currently doesn't slash, but at least
#. it doesn't give the spear bonus
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "survivor naginata"
msgid_plural "survivor naginata"
msgstr[0] "幸存者薙刀"

#. ~ Description says it can slash. STAB currently doesn't slash, but at least
#. it doesn't give the spear bonus
#. ~ Description of "survivor naginata"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"This sturdy steel shaft with a sword blade at the end is good for both "
"slashing and stabbing."
msgstr "一根坚固的钢制杆身，一端安装了一个带刺刀头，既能斩击又能刺击。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "wooden javelin"
msgid_plural "wooden javelins"
msgstr[0] "木标枪"

#. ~ Description of "wooden javelin"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A fire-hardened wooden spear honed to a sharper point."
msgstr "一个前端磨尖并用火烤硬化的木制长矛。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "iron javelin"
msgid_plural "iron javelins"
msgstr[0] "铁尖标枪"

#. ~ Description of "iron javelin"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "An iron-tipped wooden throwing spear."
msgstr "一支装有铁制矛头的木柄标枪。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgctxt "weapon"
msgid "wooden pike"
msgid_plural "wooden pikes"
msgstr[0] "木制重矛"

#. ~ Description of "wooden pike"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a very long wooden shaft with a fire-"
"hardened point."
msgstr "一把中世纪武器，由一根非常长的木杆，雕刻出矛尖并经过火焰硬化而成。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgctxt "weapon"
msgid "copper pike"
msgid_plural "copper pikes"
msgstr[0] "铜制重矛"

#. ~ Description of "copper pike"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a very long wooden shaft tipped with a "
"copper spearhead."
msgstr "一把中世纪武器，由一根非常长的木杆与铜制矛尖结合而成。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgctxt "weapon"
msgid "pike"
msgid_plural "pikes"
msgstr[0] "重矛"

#. ~ Description of "pike"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a very long wooden shaft tipped with a steel"
" spearhead."
msgstr "一把中世纪武器，由一根非常长的木杆与钢制矛尖结合而成。"

#. ~ Description of "pike"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A dull, cheaply made replica of a medieval weapon consisting of a very long "
"wooden shaft tipped with an iron spearhead."
msgstr "一把中世纪武器，由一根非常长的木杆与铁制矛尖结合而成。这把是廉价且拙劣的复制品。"

#. ~ Description of "pike"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a very long wooden shaft tipped with an iron"
" spearhead.  The head seems to be pretty dull, and the whole thing feels "
"poorly made."
msgstr "一把中世纪武器，由一根非常长的木杆与铁制矛尖结合而成。这把矛尖已经被磨钝了，而且整体感觉做工很差。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "war scythe"
msgid_plural "war scythes"
msgstr[0] "战斗镰刀"

#. ~ Description of "war scythe"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A pole weapon with a curving single-edged blade.  Its blade bears some "
"superficial resemblance to that of an agricultural scythe from which it "
"likely evolved."
msgstr "有弯曲的单侧刀刃的杆状武器。它的刀刃表面有点像农用镰刀，很可能是从农用镰刀演变而来的。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "dory"
msgid_plural "dories"
msgstr[0] "希腊长矛"

#. ~ Description of "dory"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A well-made spear with a bronze head, Greek in origin.  Despite its large "
"size, it was frequently used one-handed."
msgstr "一支制作精良的青铜头长矛，起源于希腊。尽管它的尺寸很大，但通常依然是单手使用。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "bronze spear"
msgid_plural "bronze spears"
msgstr[0] "青铜长矛"

#. ~ Description of "bronze spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A forged spear with a bronze head."
msgstr "一支带有青铜锻造矛头的长矛。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "poleaxe"
msgid_plural "poleaxes"
msgstr[0] "长柄斧"

#. ~ Description of "poleaxe"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A polearm with an axe head, a small hammer on the back, and a short dagger-"
"like spike on top.  It's less heavy than most polearms and has a smaller "
"head, making it slightly quicker."
msgstr "一把带有斧头的长柄武器，另一面有一个小锤子，顶部有一个类似匕首的的短尖。它没有大多数长柄武器那么重，头也更小，挥舞速度更快。"

#. ~ Couldn't find a good way to pluralize the transliteration.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "ji"
msgid_plural "ji"
msgstr[0] "中式戟"

#. ~ Couldn't find a good way to pluralize the transliteration.
#. ~ Description of "ji"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A bronze polearm that originated in the Shang dynasty of China, if not "
"earlier.  It combines a spear head with the perpendicular blade of the "
"earlier ge or dagger-axe."
msgstr "一把起源自中国商朝或是更早时期的青铜长柄武器。它的顶部由矛尖和垂直于矛尖的，被称作戈的刀刃组成。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "stone spear"
msgid_plural "stone spears"
msgstr[0] "石制长矛"

#. ~ Description of "stone spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A stout wooden pole with a sharp stone spearhead."
msgstr "一根结实的木棍，一端配有尖锐的石制矛头。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "simple stone spear"
msgid_plural "simple stone spears"
msgstr[0] "简易石矛"

#. ~ Description of "simple stone spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A long stick with a sharp stone spearhead."
msgstr "一根长木棍，一端配有尖锐的石制矛头。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "2-by-sword"
msgid_plural "2-by-swords"
msgstr[0] "木剑"

#. ~ Description of "2-by-sword"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A plank with a handle and a whittled-down point.  Not much good for "
"slashing, but much better than your bare hands."
msgstr "一块木板，装上护手后削尖了头做成木剑。不太适合拿来挥砍，但总比赤手空拳要好。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "zweitimber"
msgid_plural "zweitimbers"
msgstr[0] "双手木剑"

#. ~ Description of "zweitimber"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A plank with a handle and a whittled-down point, left large enough to "
"require two hands.  Still not much good for slashing, but far better than "
"the plank on its own."
msgstr "一块带有握柄的木板，顶部被削尖，个头不小，需要双手持握。虽然依旧不太适合挥砍，但比木板本身要好得多。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "nord"
msgid_plural "nords"
msgstr[0] "钉齿剑"

#. ~ Description of "nord"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A nail sword, or nord for short.  This wooden sword has a dozen nails "
"sticking out at jagged angles from the edge of the blade, making it much "
"better at chopping than slashing."
msgstr "钉齿剑（nail sword），简称“nord”。这把木剑从剑刃上伸出很多钉子，组成锯齿状，使其相较于挥砍更适合用于切刺。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "scrap sword"
msgid_plural "scrap swords"
msgstr[0] "废料剑"

#. ~ Description of "scrap sword"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"Several bits of thin scrap metal crudely beat into the semblance of an edge "
"over a wooden sword.  The added weight is unbalanced, but the jagged edge "
"offers a good bit of slashing power."
msgstr "一些废铁条被简陋的敲打进一把木剑的边缘。新加上去的重量导致整把武器重心不平衡，不过锯齿的边缘增加了不错的斩击强度。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "scrap greatsword"
msgid_plural "scrap greatswords"
msgstr[0] "废料巨剑"

#. ~ Description of "scrap greatsword"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A large wooden sword with scrap metal hammered over it into something "
"pretending to be an edge.  The extra weight almost completely front-loads "
"the balance, and it hurts your wrists just to wield."
msgstr "一把大木剑，上面有用废金属敲打成的“剑刃”。额外的重量严重破坏了平衡，光是挥舞起来就会伤到手腕。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "welded sword"
msgid_plural "welded swords"
msgstr[0] "焊接剑"

#. ~ Description of "welded sword"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A vicious single-edged sword made out of sheet metal layered twice over "
"itself then welded together.  It's not as robust as a proper forged sword, "
"but the edge is wickedly sharp."
msgstr "一把十分狂野的单刃剑，由金属板折叠后焊接而成。它不像正规的锻造剑那样坚固，但其边缘却非常锋利。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "bolted sword"
msgid_plural "bolted swords"
msgstr[0] "栓接剑"

#. ~ Description of "bolted sword"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A vicious single-edged sword made out of sheet metal layered twice over "
"itself then bolted together.  It's not quite a katana made from steel folded"
" a thousand times over, but it has a certain industrial charm to it."
msgstr "一把十分狂野的单刃剑，由金属板折叠后后用螺栓连接而成。它不是那种千锤百炼而成的武士刀，但却有某种工业的魅力。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "welded greatsword"
msgid_plural "welded greatswords"
msgstr[0] "焊接巨剑"

#. ~ Description of "welded greatsword"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A long-handled single-edged sword made out of sheet metal layered thrice "
"over itself then welded together.  The extra length and weight makes it a "
"tad awkward, but gives it a lot of slashing power."
msgstr "一把长柄单刃剑，由金属板折叠成三层后焊接而成。额外的长度和重量使它有点笨拙，但也带来了更强的劈砍能力。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "bolted greatsword"
msgid_plural "bolted greatswords"
msgstr[0] "栓接巨剑"

#. ~ Description of "bolted greatsword"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A long-handled single-edged sword made out of sheet metal layered thrice "
"over itself then bolted together.  It vaguely resembles a Japanese nagamaki "
"if you squint."
msgstr "一把长柄单刃剑，由金属板折叠成三层后用螺栓连接而成。如果你眯起眼睛，它看起来和一把日式的长卷刀差不多。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "metal sword"
msgid_plural "metal swords"
msgstr[0] "金属剑"

#. ~ Description of "metal sword"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"An imitation of a true sword forged by someone who knows what swords look "
"like, at least.  Made from whatever scrap metal was on hand, it has the "
"general shape of a sword, and it is sharp, but it is a bit heavier than it "
"should be and the balance isn't quite right."
msgstr ""
"一把真剑的仿制品，由某个至少知道剑是什么样子的人锻造而成。它由一些现成的金属废料制作而成，有剑的一般形状，锋利，但比正规剑要沉，平衡性也不太好。"

#. ~ It's not razor-sharp and most of the damage is coming from the heavy
#. weight, hence the high bash-to-cut ratio.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "metal greatsword"
msgid_plural "metal greatswords"
msgstr[0] "金属巨剑"

#. ~ It's not razor-sharp and most of the damage is coming from the heavy
#. weight, hence the high bash-to-cut ratio.
#. ~ Description of "metal greatsword"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A large, crudely-forged blade.  It's too big to be called a sword.  Too "
"massive, too thick, too heavy, and far too rough."
msgstr "一把粗劣锻造制成的大刀，大到不能称之为剑。太大、太厚、太沉，而且太粗糙。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "metal fencing sword"
msgid_plural "metal fencing swords"
msgstr[0] "金属刺剑"

#. ~ Description of "metal fencing sword"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"Calling this a rapier is a stretch.  It's robust and very pointy, but more "
"akin to a long metal spike with a handguard than the elegant swords of the "
"Renaissance."
msgstr "说这是一把刺剑还是太勉强了。它很结实，非常尖，但更像是一把带护手的长金属钉，而不是文艺复兴时期的优雅刺剑。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Variant name of item "switchblade"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "switchblade"
msgid_plural "switchblades"
msgstr[0] "弹簧刀"

#. ~ Description of "switchblade"
#. ~ Description of variant "switchblade" of item "switchblade"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A long, thin knife with a spring-loaded blade that rests inside the handle "
"while not in use."
msgstr "又长又细的弹簧小刀，不用时可以把刀刃收在刀柄里面，使用时自动弹出。"

#. ~ Variant name of item "switchblade"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "balisong"
msgid_plural "balisongs"
msgstr[0] "蝴蝶刀"

#. ~ Description of variant "balisong" of item "switchblade"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A flashy knife with hinged handles that completely conceal the blade while "
"folded.  Popular among movie gangbangers and people who thought fidget "
"spinners were too safe."
msgstr "一把华丽的小刀，带有铰链手柄，折叠时刀片完全隐藏。在认为指尖陀螺太安全了的人，以及那些电影里的黑帮之间很受欢迎。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "folding knife"
msgid_plural "folding knives"
msgstr[0] "折叠刀"

#. ~ Description of "folding knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A small folding knife with a locking blade and a pocket clip.  Not as good a"
" weapon as a solid fixed-blade knife, but better than a penknife."
msgstr "一把小型折叠刀，有着一个可以伸缩的锁口刀片，背面有个口袋夹。和刀身固定的刀具相比，它不适合当作武器使用，但总比一个削笔刀好些。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "combat knife"
msgid_plural "combat knives"
msgstr[0] "战术匕首"

#. ~ Description of "combat knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A military combat knife.  It is light and extremely sharp, and could be "
"deadly in either the right hands or when attached as a bayonet."
msgstr "一把轻而极度锋利的军用战斗匕首，手持或当作刺刀使用同样致命。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "modified combat knife"
msgid_plural "modified combat knives"
msgstr[0] "改装战术匕首"

#. ~ Description of "modified combat knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A military combat knife.  It is light and extremely sharp, and could be "
"deadly in either the right hands or when attached as a bayonet.  This one "
"was modified and customized to mount on pretty much any weapon other than "
"pistols, if you so want."
msgstr "一把轻而极度锋利的军用战斗匕首，手持或当作刺刀使用同样致命。这把匕首经过了改装，可以装在除手枪外的几乎任何武器上。"

#. ~ Highest non-powertool butchering quality.  It's made for skinning and
#. butchering game, which is what you're generally doing.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "hunting knife"
msgid_plural "hunting knives"
msgstr[0] "猎刀"

#. ~ Highest non-powertool butchering quality.  It's made for skinning and
#. butchering game, which is what you're generally doing.
#. ~ Description of "hunting knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"Commonly used by hunters, this single-edged sheath knife is designed for "
"cutting and skinning game rather than combat."
msgstr "猎人常用的刀具，这种单刃带鞘的小刀专用于切削、剥皮等用途，而不是战斗。"

#. ~ This isn't really supposed to be a very good knife, or a very good saw.
#. It's more for looking scary.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "survival knife"
msgid_plural "survival knives"
msgstr[0] "生存刀"

#. ~ This isn't really supposed to be a very good knife, or a very good saw.
#. It's more for looking scary.
#. ~ Description of "survival knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"This massive knife features a hollow handle with a compass built into the "
"pommel and a row of fearsome-looking saw teeth along the back of its blade."
msgstr "一把常见于特种部队、野外求生爱好者所用的大号生存刀。刀身径直，刀背上有着一排锯齿，有着砍、锯、刺等多种用途，握柄底端镶嵌着一个迷你指南针。"

#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "survival knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "A hidden handle compartment.  Unscrew the compass to access ."
msgstr "一个隐藏的把手隔间，拧开指南针就可以打开。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "RM42 fighting knife"
msgid_plural "RM42 fighting knives"
msgstr[0] "RM42 战术匕首"

#. ~ Description of "RM42 fighting knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"This sturdy, matte black Rivtech combat dagger features a long, slim double-"
"edged blade with a spear point and a distinctive slip-resistant grip, which "
"can also be used to affix it to a suitable firearm as a bayonet.  Originally"
" manufactured for the military, it was very popular in films and among "
"collectors due to its fearsome appearance."
msgstr ""
"一把坚固的哑光黑色Rivtech战斗匕首。它有着独特的细长剑形刃和专利防滑握柄，可以在合适的武器上当作刺刀使用。虽说它是为军队设计的，但是因为它吓人的外观，这把匕首在电影和收藏者中非常流行。"

#. ~ The swiss army knife is a bit more of a knife than a toolkit.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "Swiss Army knife"
msgid_plural "Swiss Army knives"
msgstr[0] "瑞士军刀"

#. ~ The swiss army knife is a bit more of a knife than a toolkit.
#. ~ Description of "Swiss Army knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"An iconic pocket knife imported from Europe.  Its red plastic handle "
"conceals many small tools."
msgstr "名字响亮，这个从欧洲进口的折叠刀的红塑料柄里面藏着不少小工具。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "trench knife"
msgid_plural "trench knives"
msgstr[0] "战壕匕首"

#. ~ Description of "trench knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"This stout combat knife features a steel guard to protect the user's "
"knuckles.  The guard can also be used for striking or blocking."
msgstr ""
"一把钢制护手的匕首，用于保护指关节，也可以用来敲击或者格挡。专为第一次世界大战中残酷的肉搏战设计的武器，让士兵们在不足几英尺宽的战壕里互相厮杀，独特的刃形可以令其轻易撬开或凿穿钢盔，对付丧尸也是同样如此。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "makeshift knife"
msgid_plural "makeshift knives"
msgstr[0] "简易小刀"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A knife consisting of a long, somewhat sharpened spike and a tightly-wrapped"
" rag as a handle.  Not as good as a real knife, but it'll do in a pinch."
msgstr "一把小刀，由一根略微锋利的钉刺组成，一边紧紧包裹有破布作为握柄。虽然没有真正的刀子好，但在紧要关头也能用。"

#. ~ literally 75% of a bone.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "bone shiv"
msgid_plural "bone shivs"
msgstr[0] "骨片刀"

#. ~ literally 75% of a bone.
#. ~ Description of "bone shiv"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A femur or other bone, about 20 cm long, which has been broken at one end "
"and sharpened into a cutting tool.  Its jagged edge is wicked but fragile."
msgstr "一根大约20厘米长的股骨或是其他类似的骨头，一端被折断并被磨尖成切割工具。其锯齿状的边缘看上去很危险，但其实很脆弱。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "baselard"
msgid_plural "baselards"
msgstr[0] "贝斯拉德匕首"

#. ~ Description of "baselard"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A medieval dagger forged from rough iron.  It is not the sharpest tool in "
"the shed, but it is certainly one of the largest."
msgstr "一把用粗铁锻造的中世纪匕首。它也许不是工具棚里最锋利的工具，但肯定是最大个之一。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "makeshift machete"
msgid_plural "makeshift machetes"
msgstr[0] "简易砍刀"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift machete"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A large blade with one end wrapped in duct tape to make a crude handle, "
"making it easier to wield as a rough machete."
msgstr "一把大刀，一端用胶带缠住，做成一个粗糙的刀柄，使其更容易作为一把粗糙的砍刀挥舞。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "machete"
msgid_plural "machetes"
msgstr[0] "砍刀"

#. ~ Description of "machete"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"This huge steel knife makes an excellent tool for cutting down large "
"vegetation or other 'obstacles.'"
msgstr "一柄较短、单刃、刀身宽大，以切砍为主要攻击方式的钢制砍刀。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "machete multitool"
msgid_plural "machete multitools"
msgstr[0] "多功能砍刀"

#. ~ Description of "machete multitool"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A thin, wobbly steel blade with sawteeth on one side and a flat chisel tip "
"for digging.  A jack of many trades, and a master of none."
msgstr "细长又摇摇晃晃的的钢刃的一侧有着锯齿，顶部是一个能用来挖掘的凿头。门门精通，样样稀松。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "cavalry saber"
msgid_plural "cavalry sabers"
msgstr[0] "骑兵刀"

#. ~ Description of "cavalry saber"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A curved sword associated with cavalry from the Early Modern period onward."
"  Lightweight, but a deadly slashing weapon."
msgstr "一把骑兵用弯刀，从近代起就成为骑兵的近战武器。轻便，但同时又是致命的斩击武器。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "mild steel cavalry saber"
msgid_plural "mild steel cavalry sabers"
msgstr[0] "骑兵刀（低碳钢）"

#. ~ Description of "mild steel cavalry saber"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"This is a curved sword associated with cavalry from the Early Modern period onwards.  Lightweight, but a deadly slashing weapon.\n"
"\n"
"Made with mild carbon steel and lacking a proper grip, this is better than the sticks you swung around as a kid, but you know you can do better."
msgstr ""
"一把骑兵用弯刀，从近代起就成为骑兵的近战武器。轻便，但同时又是致命的斩击武器。\n"
"\n"
"这把由低碳钢制成，而且缺乏合适的握柄，虽然比你小时候挥舞的棍子好，但你知道你可以做得更好。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "medium steel cavalry saber"
msgid_plural "medium steel cavalry sabers"
msgstr[0] "骑兵刀（中碳钢）"

#. ~ Description of "medium steel cavalry saber"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"This is a curved sword associated with cavalry from the Early Modern period onwards.  Lightweight, but a deadly slashing weapon.\n"
"\n"
"Made with mild carbon steel and with a grip made of leather wrapped in steel wire, this weapon is comfortable in your hand, though the balance isn't perfect and the edge could be sharper."
msgstr ""
"一把骑兵用弯刀，从近代起就成为骑兵的近战武器。轻便，但同时又是致命的斩击武器。\n"
"\n"
"这把由低碳钢制成，带有钢丝包裹着皮革的握柄，拿在手里很舒服，但平衡性并不完美，边缘也可以更锋利。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "high steel cavalry saber"
msgid_plural "high steel cavalry sabers"
msgstr[0] "骑兵刀（高碳钢）"

#. ~ Description of "high steel cavalry saber"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"This is a curved sword associated with cavalry from the Early Modern period onwards.  Lightweight, but a deadly slashing weapon.\n"
"\n"
"Made with high carbon steel and featuring a sturdy grip, this feels like a proper weapon.  The balance feels right and the blade is quite sharp."
msgstr ""
"一把骑兵用弯刀，从近代起就成为骑兵的近战武器。轻便，但同时又是致命的斩击武器。\n"
"\n"
"这把由高碳钢制成，带有坚固的握把，感觉是一把合适的武器。平衡性很好，刀刃也相当锋利。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "hardened cavalry saber"
msgid_plural "hardened cavalry sabers"
msgstr[0] "骑兵刀（表面硬化碳钢）"

#. ~ Description of "hardened cavalry saber"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"This is a curved sword associated with cavalry from the Early Modern period onwards.  Lightweight, but a deadly slashing weapon.\n"
"\n"
"Made of hardened steel and with a molded grip that fits your hand perfectly, this weapon looks as good as any you might find in a museum.  The balance is perfect and the edge is as sharp as a razor."
msgstr ""
"一把骑兵用弯刀，从近代起就成为骑兵的近战武器。轻便，但同时又是致命的斩击武器。\n"
"\n"
"这把由低碳钢经过表面硬化制成，带有一个与你的手完美贴合的模制握把，看起来和能在博物馆里找到的任何武器一样好。平衡性很完美，边缘像剃刀一样锋利。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "tempered cavalry saber"
msgid_plural "tempered cavalry sabers"
msgstr[0] "骑兵刀（回火碳钢）"

#. ~ Description of "tempered cavalry saber"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"This is a curved sword associated with cavalry from the Early Modern period onwards.  Lightweight, but a deadly slashing weapon.\n"
"\n"
"Made of tempered steel, this is a masterpiece.  The grip, the balance, the blade, all perfect.  This is the peak of the swordsmith's craft."
msgstr ""
"一把骑兵用弯刀，从近代起就成为骑兵的近战武器。轻便，但同时又是致命的斩击武器。\n"
"\n"
"这把由中碳钢经过回火处理制成，堪称为杰作：握柄、平衡、剑刃，都无比完美，剑匠工艺的巅峰。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "kris"
msgid_plural "krises"
msgstr[0] "蛇剑"

#. ~ Description of "kris"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"This wavy-bladed dagger is from Southeast Asia.  The design of the blade "
"causes it to make broad, painful wounds."
msgstr "东南亚原产的波纹状刀刃的匕首。刀刃的形状让它善于制造又大又疼的伤口。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#: data/mods/MMA/exemplar_weapons.json
msgid "kukri"
msgid_plural "kukris"
msgstr[0] "库克利弯刀"

#. ~ Description of "kukri"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"This versatile implement is a modern take on a traditional weapon that "
"originated in Nepal.  Featuring a heavy blade with an inwardly-curved edge, "
"it can be used as both a tool and a weapon."
msgstr "这种多功能的传统武器起源于尼泊尔。具有重厚的刀身和向内弯曲的刀刃，可以用来作为一种工具和武器。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "jian"
msgid_plural "jian"
msgstr[0] "剑"

#. ~ Description of "jian"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"An ancient Chinese doubled-edged straight sword, with an ornate guard and a "
"tassel attached to the pommel.  One of the four major weapons in folklore, "
"alongside the dao sabre, qiang spear, and gun staff."
msgstr "一把古中国剑，双刃开锋，剑身长直，护手带有装饰，柄端附有流苏。民间传说中四大武器之一，其余三个是：刀、枪和棍。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "mild steel jian"
msgid_plural "mild steel jian"
msgstr[0] "中式剑（低碳钢）"

#. ~ Description of "mild steel jian"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"This is an ancient Chinese doubled-edged straight sword, with an ornate guard and a tassel attached to the pommel.  One of the four major weapons in folklore, alongside the dao sabre, qiang spear, and gun staff.\n"
"\n"
"Made with mild carbon steel and lacking a proper grip, this is better than the sticks you swung around as a kid, but you know you can do better."
msgstr ""
"一把古中国剑，双刃开锋，剑身长直，护手带有装饰，柄端附有流苏。民间传说中四大武器之一，其余三个是：刀、枪和棍。\n"
"\n"
"这把由低碳钢制成，而且缺乏合适的握柄，虽然比你小时候挥舞的棍子好，但你知道你可以做得更好。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "medium steel jian"
msgid_plural "medium steel jian"
msgstr[0] "中式剑（中碳钢）"

#. ~ Description of "medium steel jian"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"This is an ancient Chinese doubled-edged straight sword, with an ornate guard and a tassel attached to the pommel.  One of the four major weapons in folklore, alongside the dao sabre, qiang spear, and gun staff.\n"
"\n"
"Made with mild carbon steel and with a grip made of leather wrapped in steel wire, this weapon is comfortable in your hand, though the balance isn't perfect and the edge could be sharper."
msgstr ""
"一把古中国剑，双刃开锋，剑身长直，护手带有装饰，柄端附有流苏。民间传说中四大武器之一，其余三个是：刀、枪和棍。\n"
"\n"
"这把由低碳钢制成，带有钢丝包裹着皮革的握柄，拿在手里很舒服，但平衡性并不完美，边缘也可以更锋利。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "high steel jian"
msgid_plural "high steel jian"
msgstr[0] "中式剑（高碳钢）"

#. ~ Description of "high steel jian"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"This is an ancient Chinese doubled-edged straight sword, with an ornate guard and a tassel attached to the pommel.  One of the four major weapons in folklore, alongside the dao sabre, qiang spear, and gun staff.\n"
"\n"
"Made with high carbon steel and featuring a sturdy grip, this feels like a proper weapon.  The balance feels right and the blade is quite sharp."
msgstr ""
"一把古中国剑，双刃开锋，剑身长直，护手带有装饰，柄端附有流苏。民间传说中四大武器之一，其余三个是：刀、枪和棍。\n"
"\n"
"这把由高碳钢制成，带有坚固的握把，感觉是一把合适的武器。平衡性很好，刀刃也相当锋利。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "hardened jian"
msgid_plural "hardened jian"
msgstr[0] "中式剑（表面硬化碳钢）"

#. ~ Description of "hardened jian"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"This is an ancient Chinese doubled-edged straight sword, with an ornate guard and a tassel attached to the pommel.  One of the four major weapons in folklore, alongside the dao sabre, qiang spear, and gun staff.\n"
"\n"
"Made of hardened steel and with a molded grip that fits your hand perfectly, this weapon looks as good as any you might find in a museum.  The balance is perfect and the edge is as sharp as a razor."
msgstr ""
"一把古中国剑，双刃开锋，剑身长直，护手带有装饰，柄端附有流苏。民间传说中四大武器之一，其余三个是：刀、枪和棍。\n"
"\n"
"这把由低碳钢经过表面硬化制成，带有一个与你的手完美贴合的模制握把，看起来和能在博物馆里找到的任何武器一样好。平衡性很完美，边缘像剃刀一样锋利。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "tempered jian"
msgid_plural "tempered jian"
msgstr[0] "中式剑（回火碳钢）"

#. ~ Description of "tempered jian"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"This is an ancient Chinese doubled-edged straight sword, with an ornate guard and a tassel attached to the pommel.  One of the four major weapons in folklore, alongside the dao sabre, qiang spear, and gun staff.\n"
"\n"
"Made of tempered steel, this is a masterpiece.  The grip, the balance, the blade, all perfect.  This is the peak of the swordsmith's craft."
msgstr ""
"一把古中国剑，双刃开锋，剑身长直，护手带有装饰，柄端附有流苏。民间传说中四大武器之一，其余三个是：刀、枪和棍。\n"
"\n"
"这把由中碳钢经过回火处理制成，堪称为杰作：握柄、平衡、剑刃，都无比完美，剑匠工艺的巅峰。"

#. ~ Description of "jian"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"An ancient Chinese doubled-edged straight sword.  The sword is quite worn, "
"and bent at an odd angle."
msgstr "一把古中国剑，双刃开锋，剑身长直——本该如此，实际上它的剑刃磨损严重，还弯出了一个奇怪的角度。"

#. ~ Description of "jian"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A dull, cheaply-made replica of an ancient Chinese doubled-edged straight "
"sword, with an ornate guard."
