#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/whately_generic_dialogue.json
msgid "What's your story?"
msgstr "说说你的故事？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "How are things around here?"
msgstr "这附近的情况怎么样？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Could you tell me about the community?"
msgstr "能和我说说你们这个社区的情况吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid "Want to come with me?"
msgstr "与我同行吧，如何？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
msgid "What do you see in your visions?"
msgstr "你看到了什么？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
msgid ""
"Hi, <name_g>.  Could I pat you on the shoulder?  I wanna be sure you're "
"here."
msgstr "嗨，<name_g>。我能拍拍你的肩膀吗，我想要确认一下你在这里。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
msgid "Are you alright?"
msgstr "你还好吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
msgid "Hey Arturo, how are ya?"
msgstr "嘿，阿图罗，最近怎么样？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
msgid "Nice talking to you, but I gotta go."
msgstr "和你聊天很愉快，但我也该走了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
msgid "Yeah, just that I sometimes see things.  I wanna be sure you're real."
msgstr "我还好，只是有时会看到一些东西。我想确定你是真实存在的。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
msgid "It's alright, just take your time."
msgstr "没事的，你继续忙。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
msgid "Sorry, I gotta go."
msgstr "抱歉，我该走了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
msgid "What's hangin'?"
msgstr "还有别的事吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
msgid ""
"I've had a bad run of things.  I grew up real poor, in a bad part of town, "
"always got my nose where it shouldn't have been.  When I was about eighteen,"
" I started doing coke heavily.  Every two days, I'd get spaced out on the "
"stuff; started robbing gas stations and dumb <swear> things like that for a "
"fix.  I went to jail, and I met the New England Church Community there.  I "
"joined up to find penance for my sins.  Another thing, stay off of that "
"<swear> stuff; I messed up my brain real bad doin' that."
msgstr ""
"我经历了一系列糟糕的事情。我从小就很穷，走遍了城里的每一个糟糕的地方，总喜欢插手各种闲事。当我大约十八岁时，我开始大量吸食可卡因。每两天，我就会因为这些东西而无法思考；开始做出抢劫加油站之类的<swear>蠢事来解决问题。我进了监狱，在那里我遇到了新英格兰教会社区。我加入了为我的罪孽忏悔的行列。而且远离了那些<swear>东西；搞砸了我的大脑真的很糟糕。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
msgid ""
"They're not so hot.  The whole compound is always low on food, there's "
"<swear> <zombies> out on the roads, and Helena's starting to panic a bit.  "
"She thinks I'm a holy visionary, with my episodes…  Sometimes I want to "
"believe her.  I usually take the Thorazine Jane has, but I've been getting "
"it less and less."
msgstr ""
"不太乐观。整个社区的食物总是很匮乏，路上到处都是<swear><zombies>，海伦娜开始有点恐慌了。她认为我是一个神圣的幻想家，因为我之前经历的事情……有时我想相信她。我经常服用简给我的的冬眠灵，但最近越来越少这么做了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
msgid ""
"Well, its an old church group that decided to become doomsday preppers.  I "
"don't know much else, except that they used to do a lot of charity work.  I "
"met them that way."
msgstr "好吧，这是一个决定成为世界末日准备者的古老教会团体。别的我就不知道了，只知道他们曾经做过很多慈善工作。我就是这样认识他们的。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
msgid ""
"Nah.  Not everything's perfect around here, but it's the only thing I've got"
" left."
msgstr "不。虽然这里并非一切都是完美的，但这是我唯一剩下的东西。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
msgid ""
"&Arturo stares blankly for a moment.  \"The man in the mirror comes to me at"
" night, and whispers things in my ear.  Eyes on the walls, watching, "
"watching…  The woman who crawls.\"  I'm sorry about that."
msgstr "阿图罗瞪大了空荡荡的眼睛好一会：“镜子里的男人晚上来到我身边，在我耳边低语。墙上的眼睛，看着，看着……爬行的女人。”啊抱歉。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "What's it like living here?"
msgstr "在这里住着怎么样啊？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid "Is there anything I can help you with?"
msgstr "我能帮你什么忙吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid "How've things been since <the_cataclysm>?"
msgstr "<the_cataclysm>以来这里过得怎么样？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid "Do you knit at all?  I noticed you have sewing needles."
msgstr "你会编织吗？我看到你有缝纫针。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid ""
"Praise the Lord.  It's good to see you're still around, <granny_name_g>."
msgstr "赞美上帝。还能再看到你回来真是太好了，<granny_name_g>。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid "Welcome, <granny_name_g>.  I don't think I recognize you, I'm Theresa."
msgstr "欢迎，<granny_name_g>。我好像没见过你，我是特蕾莎。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid "Nice to meet you, Theresa."
msgstr "很高兴见到你，特蕾莎。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid "Hello, Theresa.  How are you doing?"
msgstr "嗨，特蕾莎。你还好吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
msgid "I'm afraid I can't talk right now."
msgstr "恐怕我现在没空交谈。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid ""
"It is nice to meet you as well.  I reckon you got some questions about our "
"group."
msgstr "我很高兴见到你。我想你对我们这个群体有一些疑问。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
msgid "Actually I'm just heading out."
msgstr "其实，我该走了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid "Just fine.  Nice of you to ask.  How’s it going, <granny_name_g>?"
msgstr "还好。很高兴你这么问。怎么样了，<granny_name_g>？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid ""
"I'm doing as well as can be expected.  How’s everything, <granny_name_g>?"
msgstr "我过得和期待的一样好。你呢，<granny_name_g>？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid "I'm here about the scarf."
msgstr "我来取围巾。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid "I'm here about the blanket."
msgstr "我来取毯子。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid "I'm here about the quilt."
msgstr "我来取被子。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
msgid "Well, it's been nice talking to you, but I need to head out."
msgstr "嗯，和你谈话很愉快，但我该出发了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid ""
"We're doing better than most, to put it mildly.  There's a reason for that, "
"as for everything.  Say, have I told you about my husband?  I'm sorry if I "
"already have, my memory's not what it used to be."
msgstr "委婉地说，我们比大多数人过得更好。这一切都是有原因的。话说，我跟你说过我丈夫的事吗？对不起，如果我已经说了，我的记忆力已经不如从前了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid "Tell me about your husband."
msgstr "和我说说你的丈夫。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid ""
"He was an exceptional man.  Ever since he was a child it was clear that "
"there was something special about him.  My husband had a way with people, "
"and with God too.  But, after all he was as human as you and I.  He was "
"corrupted by addiction.  One day, God appeared to him in a vision that "
"turned his life around, he had other plans for him.  From then on he didn't "
"take his life for granted.  He used his talent and newfound inspiration to "
"better the people around him."
msgstr ""
"他是一个非凡的人。从他还是个孩子的时候起，就很明显有一些特别之处。我丈夫对人有一套，对神也有一套。但是，毕竟他和你我一样是人。他被毒瘾腐蚀了。有一天，上帝出现在他的幻觉中，改变了他的生活，他有了另一套计划。从此，他不再把自己的生命视为理所当然。他利用自己的才华和新发现的灵感来帮助周围的人。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid "So, he founded the community?"
msgstr "所以，他成立了这个社区？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Tell me about his visions."
msgstr "他看到了什么幻觉？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid ""
"That's right.  He wanted something to return for the guidance he received "
"when he was at the lowest point of his life.  He created a charity group "
"which, over the years, became what's now known as the New England Church "
"Community.  He lead them for many decades, until his death a few years "
"before his prophecy was fulfilled.  Now, our niece Helena leads the "
"community."
msgstr ""
"对的。他想要回报他在人生最低谷时得到的指导。他创建了一个慈善团体，多年来，这个团体成为了现在众所周知的新英格兰教会社区。他领导大家几十年，直到他的预言应验，在几年前去世。现在，我们的侄女海伦娜在领导社区。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid ""
"He was a man of many secrets.  It would've been too personal to share, I'm "
"afraid.  On the other hand, there was a prophecy he was quite vocal about.  "
"In a way, he predicted <the_cataclysm> long before the first warning signs "
"appeared.  Thanks to him, we had the foresight to prepare.  Oh what a great "
"man he was…"
msgstr ""
"他是一个神秘的男人。对于分享他的事情，恐怕过于隐私了。另一方面，他有一个一直念叨着的预言。在某种程度上，他早在第一个警告信号出现之前就预测到了<the_cataclysm>。多亏了他，我们才有了准备的先见之明。噢，他是多么伟大的人……"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid ""
"Oh you don't have the time for that, do you now?  It's a long, long tale, "
"thank goodness.  I'm grateful, for I was blessed with a full life."
msgstr "噢，你现在没有时间，是吗？这是一个很长很长的故事，谢天谢地。我总是很感激，因为我被祝福拥有充实的生活。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid ""
"That's very sweet of you <granny_name_g>, but there's nothing I could "
"possibly want from this mortal world.  My life is now complete, I believe."
msgstr "你真是太贴心了，<granny_name_g>，但我对于这个平凡世界没有什么想要的。我相信我的生活现在已经完成了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid ""
"Yes, I knit and sew in my spare time.  Its' helped keep my hands in good "
"shape over the years."
msgstr "是的，我在业余时间编织和缝纫。多年来，我靠它来保持双手状态良好。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid "Could you make something for me?"
msgstr "你能帮我编一些东西吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid ""
"I suppose I could, in exchange for a few icons.  A scarf is five, a blanket "
"ten, a quilt thirty."
msgstr "我想我可以，以一些圣像作为交换。围巾五块，毯子十块，被子三十块。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid "I'll have a scarf."
msgstr "我要一条围巾。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid "I'll have a blanket."
msgstr "我要一条毯子。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid "I'll have a quilt."
msgstr "我要一床被子。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "How long does it take you to make these?"
msgstr "你做这些需要多长时间？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid "I've changed my mind.  How're you feeling?"
msgstr "我改变主意了。你觉得如何？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I've changed my mind, I have to leave."
msgstr "我改变主意了，我得走了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid ""
"I can knit a scarf ready by tomorrow, a blanket in two days, and a quilt in "
"a week."
msgstr "我明天可以织好一条围巾，两天一条毯子，一个星期一条被子。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid ""
"I hope you like it <granny_name_g>.  If you want anything else, just come "
"back."
msgstr "我希望你喜欢它，<granny_name_g>。如果你还想要什么，就回来吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid "Thank you, Theresa.  I'll put it to good use."
msgstr "谢谢你，特蕾莎，我会妥善使用的。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
msgid ""
"I've grown tired, <granny_name_g>.  I haven't left here since we came, and "
"things outside are getting worse each day.  All my old aches and pains have "
"come back too; I can't see too good, and my muscles are always sore.  I "
"don't like where my niece is going either; she's ever more fanatical, and "
"taking my dear husband's prophecy to the extreme.  I'm content with my life,"
" though.  I've lived long and prospered by the grace of the Lord."
msgstr ""
"我已经累了，<granny_name_g>。从我们来到这儿后我就没离开过，而外面的情况一天比一天糟。我所有的陈年病痛都回来了；眼神儿也不好，肌肉老酸痛。我也不喜欢我侄女去的地方；她越来越狂热，把我亲爱丈夫的预言发挥到了极致。不过我对自己的生活挺满意。靠着主的恩典，我活得长久而富足。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard2.json
msgid "Is there anything I can do to help?"
msgstr "有什么我可以帮忙的？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid "Aw hey, it's you again."
msgstr "啊，嗨，又是你。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid "Oh… hi.  I don't know you.  My name's Chloe."
msgstr "哦……嗨。我不认识你。我叫克洛伊。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
msgid "Nice to meet you, kid.  What's up?"
msgstr "很高兴见到你，孩子。怎么了？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid "Hi.  I can't stay and chat right now."
msgstr "嗨。我现在不能留下来闲聊。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid "Do you wanna shoot the breeze?"
msgstr "你要不要聊聊？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/cook.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Just saying hello.  Keep safe."
msgstr "只是过来打个招呼。注意安全。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid "Shoot."
msgstr "中啊。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid "Really, what's your story?"
msgstr "真的，说说你的故事？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid "How'd you and Sonia come to meet?"
msgstr "你和索尼娅是怎么相遇的？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid "How'd you and Sonia come to meet again?"
msgstr "你和索尼娅是怎么重逢的？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid "Aren't you a bit young to be carrying a knife?"
msgstr "你这年纪带把刀子是不是早了点儿？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid "On second though, let's talk about something else."
msgstr "转念一想，咱还是说点别的吧。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid ""
"Things suck right now, but you know that anyway.  I don't even know why you "
"bother asking these stupid questions."
msgstr "现在情况很糟糕，但你应该已经很清楚了。我甚至不知道你为什么要问这些愚蠢的问题。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid ""
"I'm not a baby you know, I don't need a babysitter.  Sonia looks out for me "
"though.  She's not so weird, I guess.  She promised to give me guitar "
"lessons and she even signed me an autograph.  I know she's only nice to me "
"because I saved her, but that's okay; we're equal now."
msgstr ""
"你知道我不是婴儿，我不需要保姆。不过，索尼娅会照顾我。我想她没那么奇怪。她答应给我上吉他课，还给我签了名。我知道她对我好只是因为我救了她，但没关系；我们现在扯平了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid "Yeah, that's enough for me."
msgstr "是，对我而言已经足够了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid ""
"You're creepy.  I'm sorry for your lack of friends but, like, I'm literally "
"a kid.  Everyone on Earth turned into a zombie, we're running out of toilet "
"paper and everything, and my parents are gone.  I know they're still alive "
"and they're looking for me.  I miss them.  Is that enough personal stuff for"
" you?"
msgstr ""
"你真是个怪人。我很抱歉你没有朋友，但我真的是个孩子。地球上的每个人都变成了丧尸，我们的厕纸和所有东西都快用完了，我的父母也不见了。我知道他们还活着，他们在找我。我想念他们。这对你来说够私人了吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid "I'm sorry for your loss.  Mabey we should talk about something else."
msgstr "我为你的损失感到难过。也许我们该谈谈别的事情。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid ""
"Well, I grew up in the city.  My parents were always out of town on some "
"business meeting or another, so I had plenty of time to myself.  They're "
"great people; mom's a wonderful cook, she makes an amazing fish casserole.  "
"Dad's a hot shot for military contracts, he handled business deals for DARPA"
" and whatnot.  He's an ex-marine, and taught me how to defend myself with a "
"knife."
msgstr ""
"嗯，我是在城里长大的。我的父母总是出城参加一些商务会议之类的，所以我有很多时间独处。他们都很好；妈妈是个很棒的厨师，她做的鱼砂锅很棒。爸爸是各种军事合同的热门人选，处理过DARPA的商业交易等等。他也是一名退伍军人，教我如何用刀自卫。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid "Where do you think your parents are now?"
msgstr "你觉得你的父母现在在哪里？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid ""
"I was home alone during the ongoing riots.  My parents chose the worst "
"possible time to reconnect, which sucks, but I'm also kinda happy for them."
"  Anyway, they were part of the NECC people, so they knew about this place "
"and their plans and all.  Thing is, it was, like, really far away.  I kinda "
"didn't want to go alone but I also didn't want the rioters to eat me, so I "
"asked Sonia - my neighbor - to evacuate with me, I guess.  So that was fun; "
"escaping my hometown, walking down the country road, waiting for a horror to"
" ambush us.  Spoiler alert: we were attacked.  So this zombie shambles in "
"front of us and Sonia whacks it real hard with her guitar!  Its brain "
"splatters all over the pavement, I threw up 'cause it was so disgusting.  We"
" got here soon after that.  My parents weren't here, obviously.  Oh man, "
"they must worry about me so much…"
msgstr ""
"在持续的暴动中，我一个人在家。我的父母选择了最坏的时间转移，糟透了，但我也为他们感到高兴。不管怎样，他们是NECC的一员，所以他们知道这个地方，也有他们的计划。那些事情感觉就像过去很久了。我有点不想一个人离开，但我也不希望暴徒吃掉我，所以我请我的邻居索尼娅和我一起撤离，我猜这样会好些。旅途很有趣：逃离家乡，走在乡间小路上，等待恐怖的埋伏忽然跳出来。剧透警告：我们被攻击了。所以有只僵尸在我们面前蹒跚而行，索尼娅用她的吉他狠狠地敲打着它！它的脑浆溅了一地，我吐了，因为实在是太恶心了。在那之后我们很快就到了这里。显然，我的父母不在这里。哦，兄弟，他们一定很担心我……"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid "Thanks for the info.  Let's chat about something else."
msgstr "谢谢你提供的信息。我们谈点别的吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/cook.json
msgid "Thanks for the info."
msgstr "多谢你的消息。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid ""
"I don't know.  They were going to a contract deal before the riots broke "
"out, at one of military bases I think.  I don't know what happened to them "
"from there."
msgstr "我不知道。他们打算在骚乱爆发前签一项合同协议，我想是在一个军事基地里。我不知道他们在那里发生了什么。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid "I'll let you know if anything turns up."
msgstr "如果有任何事情发生，我会通知你。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid "I'll let you know if anything turns up.  See you around."
msgstr "如果有任何事情发生，我会通知你。回头见。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid ""
"Aren't you a bit too old not to realize how dangerous the world is for a kid"
" like me?  I know how to handle one without hurting myself!  My dad taught "
"me everything, he's a real pro."
msgstr ""
"你是不是太老了一点，没有意识到这个世界对我这样的孩子有多危险？我知道如何干掉一个而不伤害自己！我爸爸教会了我一切，他可是一个真正的职业玩家。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid "That makes sense."
msgstr "那就讲得通了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid "They're not dead."
msgstr "他们没有死。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid "I don't wanna talk about it right now."
msgstr "我现在不想谈这件事了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
msgid "Alright, let's change the subject."
msgstr "好，我们换个话题吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/cyrus_whately.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/milly_whately_dialogue.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/sadie.json data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/NC_Yoshimi.json
msgid "How did you get here?"
msgstr "你怎么到这里来的？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "How are things, living here?"
msgstr "住在这里怎么样？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Are the non-joinees treating you fairly?"
msgstr "老教友们对你还公平吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid "Hey there, <name_g>.  Welcome to the losers club."
msgstr "嘿，<name_g>。欢迎来到失败者俱乐部。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I'm just passing through."
msgstr "我只是路过而已。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
msgid "Nice to meet you."
msgstr "很高兴认识你。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid "Hey Corrie, what's up?"
msgstr "嘿，科里，最近咋样？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid "Hey Corrie.  I gotta go."
msgstr "嘿，科里。不过我得走了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid ""
"Well if that's the case, I don't suppose you could help out struggling "
"survivors, do you?"
msgstr "好吧，如果是这样的话，我不认为你是来帮助挣扎中的幸存者的，是吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_gunrunner.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_keycard_seller.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_template_seller.json
msgid "Sorry, not interested."
msgstr "抱歉，没兴趣。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid "Hey, we're on the same boat, aren't we?"
msgstr "嘿，我们在同一条船上，不是吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid "Sure.  I can clear a few minutes of my oh-so hectic schedule."
msgstr "当然。我可以清理一下我忙碌的日程，安排上几分钟。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid "Sorry Corrie, I can't stay to chat."
msgstr "抱歉，科里。我没空留下来聊天。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid ""
"&Corrie blankly stares at the wall for a moment.  \"Me and my friends were "
"in the cities when it hit, I was the only one to make it out.  Some gigantic"
" horror… devoured… everything in its way.  There was a memorial service and "
"all, organized by the church-goers.  By far the nicest thing they've done "
"for me.\""
msgstr ""
"科里呆呆地盯着墙看了一会儿：“当它来袭时，我和我的朋友们都在城市里，我是唯一一个逃出来的人。一些巨大的怪物……吞噬了……路上的一切。后来有一个追悼会，完全由去教堂的人组织。这是他们为我做过最好的事情。”"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid "Sorry for bringing it up.  What were you saying before?"
msgstr "很抱歉提起它。你之前说什么来着？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid "Sorry for bringing it up.  Well, bye."
msgstr "很抱歉提起它。嗯，拜拜。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid "Like second-class citizens, that's how they treat us."
msgstr "就像二等公民，他们就是这样对待我们的。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
msgid "I'd better get going."
msgstr "我得走了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid ""
"I'm just here, really.  I'm the local mechanic around here, I just fiddle "
"with the machinery.  Just about all of it is a <swear> <name_b>, older than "
"dirt and nearly unfixable.  They're running a wood-fire generator for power,"
" the <swear> thing is the noisiest clunker I've ever heard."
msgstr ""
"我还活着，真的仅此而已。我是这附近的当地机械师，只会摆弄机器。几乎所有东西都是个<swear><name_b>，比泥土还古老，几乎没法修。他们用柴火发电机发电，这是我听过<swear>最吵的机器。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid "How have things changed after that deal with Helena?"
msgstr "在和海伦娜做了那笔交易之后，这里有什么变化没？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "No rest for the weary…"
msgstr "快累死了也不让人歇歇……"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid "Not much.  I told you not to go for the icons."
msgstr "不是很多。不过我劝你不要整天围着圣像转。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "Sorry to hear that.  What were you saying before?"
msgstr "真是遗憾。你刚刚还说了什么？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, yeah they have.  I've noticed a change in attitude towards us, the new"
" guys.  Positive ones.  Things might be looking up, a little bit."
msgstr "确实有。我注意到他们对我们这些新人的态度发生了积极的变化。事情可能正在好转，一点点。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid "How about some food as payment?"
msgstr "也许你可以给我点食物，作为报酬。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid "Glad to help.  What were you saying before?"
msgstr "很高兴能帮上忙。你之前说什么来着？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid "Glad to help.  See you around, Corrie."
msgstr "很高兴能帮上忙。下次见，科里。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid "Oh, I completely forget.  Here you are."
msgstr "噢，我完全忘记了。给你。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid ""
"Basic repairs and upkeep, mostly.  The generator in the basement is on its "
"last legs, so I've been thinking about building a solar array for this "
"place.  Helena's against it, but I want to change her mind.  All I need are "
"a few spare parts."
msgstr ""
"主要是基本维修和保养。地下室的发电机快坏掉了，所以我一直在考虑为这个地方建造一个太阳能阵列。海伦娜反对，但我想改变她的想法。我只需要一些零件。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid "I can help you get the items you need."
msgstr "我能帮你搞到需要的东西。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
msgid ""
"Sure, I'll come.  I hate staying here, and you've gone out of your way to "
"help me.  I appreciate that, <name_g>."
msgstr "当然，我会跟你走的。我讨厌呆在这里，而你却来特意帮助我。我很感激，<name_g>。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "About that well…"
msgstr "关于那口井……"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/cyrus_whately.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/milly_whately_dialogue.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/sadie.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/whately_generic_dialogue.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/NC_Yoshimi.json
msgid "How are things here?"
msgstr "这里怎么样？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "Nice farm you have here."
msgstr "你这农场不错啊。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Praise the Lord."
msgstr "赞美主。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/cook.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Welcome back."
msgstr "欢迎回来。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "Nice to see you again, survivor."
msgstr "很高兴再次见到你，幸存者。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "Well I'll be damned, a fellow survivor!  I'm Darryl, nice to meet you."
msgstr "喔，好家伙，一个幸存者老乡！我是达里尔，很高兴认识你。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "Nice to meet you too, Darryl.  Neat farm you have here."
msgstr "我也很高兴认识你，达里尔。你这儿的农场井井有条。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "Hey Darryl.  Got a minute?"
msgstr "嗨，达里尔。有空吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "Hey Darryl.  Care to trade?"
msgstr "嗨，达里尔。想交易吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "How are the chickens?"
msgstr "鸡怎么了？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "I guess I can spare a few minutes.  What is it?"
msgstr "我想我还是能抽出些时间聊聊的，啥事？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
msgid "Can I buy anything?"
msgstr "我能买些什么吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "Do you have any family?"
msgstr "你有家人吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"This uncertainty is eating me inside, to be frank with you.  I'm a simple "
"man: I tend my farm, I scare off vermin, but even I can see somethin' ain't "
"right here.  I've talked to my wife, I had a word with Damien, they told me "
"to have more faith in God.  It's the last sliver of hope I have left, and I "
"was told that's enough."
msgstr ""
"坦白说，这种迷茫正在侵蚀我的内心。我是一个单纯的人：我照料我的农场，驱赶害虫，但即便是我也能看出这里有些不对头。我和我妻子讨论过，也和达米安谈过，他们告诉我要对上帝有更多的信心。这是我仅剩的最后一丝希望，有人告诉我这就够了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"Well, I'd rather not get into my life before all this.  I have a farm to "
"maintain, after all.  Would be nice, sharing our tales while sipping cold "
"brew beer.  Not at a time like this.  Now if you'll excuse me, I'll be back "
"to work."
msgstr ""
"好吧，大前提是我希望别谈论我的生活。毕竟我有一个农场要维护。边喝冷酿啤酒边分享我们的故事也许挺好，但这会儿可不是时候。现在，如果你不介意的话，我要回去工作了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
msgid "Is there anything I can do to help you out?"
msgstr "我能帮你什么忙吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "I'll leave you to it."
msgstr "我就不打扰你了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"Took us three days and four hard-working hands to clear this humble little "
"land.  It's a far-cry from my old garden, it really is.  I heard theories, "
"from Tom of course, that really messed with my head.  You can never know "
"what's in one of them toxic clouds, can ya?  I suspect goo-puker blood.  "
"That putrid oil is a sure way to make any soil infertile, or so that nitwit "
"says.  Here I go again, ramblin' once more.  One of my bad habits."
msgstr ""
"我们花了三天时间和四只勤劳的手来清理这片简陋的小土地。这与我以前的花园相差甚远，真的是这样。我听到了一些理论，当然是从汤姆那里听到的，这些理论真的让我很困惑。你永远不知道那些有毒的云里有什么，是吗？我怀疑是呕吐者的血。那种腐烂的油肯定会使任何土壤变得贫瘠，那个傻瓜是这么说的。我又来了，再一次胡言乱语。我的一个坏习惯。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"Huh, never would have thought you were interested in the fine art of "
"farming.  Sure, I've got seeds I can say goodbye to… if you have the "
"appropriate money of course."
msgstr "唔，想不到你对农艺感兴趣。当然，我有些种子正好想说再见了……当然，如果你有足够的钱的话。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "Let's trade, then."
msgstr "那我们就交易吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "You know what?  Nevermind.  What were you saying before?"
msgstr "你知道吗？算了。你之前在说什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
msgid "Actually, I had better go."
msgstr "转念想想，我该走了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"It's finished, and I've got eggs!  I'd be willing to sell ya some, a dozen "
"for seven icons."
msgstr "它已经完成了，而且我有鸡蛋！我愿意卖给你一些，一打七圣像。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "I'll buy some."
msgstr "我会买点。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "That's a bit rich for my blood.  I'd better go."
msgstr "对我来说太亏了。我该走了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"All right, this is what I've got:  I can give cucumber, barley or blackberry"
" seeds for one icon; carrot, buckwheat or cranberry seeds for two icons; "
"oat, sugar beet or potato seeds for three icons."
msgstr "好吧，这就是我得到的东西。我可以给黄瓜、大麦或黑莓种子一个圣像；胡萝卜、荞麦或蔓越莓种子两个圣像；燕麦、甜菜或土豆种子三个圣像。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "I'll buy cucumber seeds."
msgstr "我要买黄瓜种子。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "I'll buy barley seeds."
msgstr "我要买大麦种子。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "I'll buy blackberry seeds."
msgstr "我要买黑莓种子。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "I'll buy carrot seeds."
msgstr "我要买胡萝卜种子。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "I'll buy buckwheat seeds."
msgstr "我要买荞麦种子。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "I'll buy cranberry seeds."
msgstr "我要买蔓越莓种子。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "I'll buy oat seeds."
msgstr "我要买燕麦种子。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "I'll buy sugar beet seeds."
msgstr "我要买甜菜种子。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "I'll buy potato seeds."
msgstr "我要买土豆种子。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"Can't you just give them to me for free?  You said you didn't need them."
msgstr "你就不能免费把它们给我吗？你说你不需要它们。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "That's a bit rich for my blood.  I had better go."
msgstr "对我来说太亏了。我该走了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"Well, you got me there.  I sure ain't one to block a fellow farmer's right "
"to reclaim this God-given earth."
msgstr "好吧，你问倒我了。我肯定不会阻挠农民朋友收回上帝赐予的这片土地的权利。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "Thank you.  See you around, Darryl."
msgstr "谢谢你。再见，达里尔。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"It really isn't difficult to earn your money here.  Hard labor, like the "
"rest of us."
msgstr "在这里挣钱真的不难。艰苦的劳动，像我们其他人一样。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"I've got a wife, Gemma.  She's a grand lady, should be around here "
"somewhere.  She used to teach biology, and we both love gardenin'; that's "
"how we met, ya see.  She 'aint been herself lately, I'm startin' to worry."
msgstr ""
"我有一个妻子，杰玛。她是一位伟大的女士，应该就在这里的某个地方。她以前是教生物的，我们都喜欢园艺；我们就是这样认识的，你看。她最近不在状态，我开始担心了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "I'll check on her.  I hope everything works out for you."
msgstr "我去看看她。希望对你有帮助。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"Oh, they passed a long time ago.  Wish they could've seen Gemma and I marry…"
msgstr "噢，他们很久以前就去世了。希望他们能看到我和杰玛结婚……"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
msgid "I'm sorry for your loss."
msgstr "听到你的损失我很难过。"

#. ~ Name of effect type id "godco_confessed"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Confessed to Greenwood"
msgstr "向格林伍德坦白"

#. ~ Description of effect type "Confessed to Greenwood"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "You decided to take responsibility for your actions."
msgstr "你决定为自己的行为负责。"

#. ~ Apply message of effect type "Confessed to Greenwood"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "You finally got the weight off your chest."
msgstr "你终于卸下了心中的重担。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid ""
"I'm seeking forgiveness, Father.  I've made mistakes in my life that I can "
"never take back."
msgstr "我正在寻求宽恕，神父。我在生活中犯了一些错误，这些错误我再也无法收回了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "The Lord be with you, brother."
msgstr "主与你同在，兄弟。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Good to see you're still around, brother."
msgstr "很高兴看到你还在，兄弟。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "The Lord be with you, sister."
msgstr "主与你同在，姐妹。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Good to see you're still around, sister."
msgstr "很高兴看到你还在，姐妹。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid ""
"The Lord be with you, brother.  You seem new, nice to meet you.  Welcome, "
"and welcome aboard!"
msgstr "主与你同在，兄弟。你似乎是新来的，很高兴认识你。欢迎，欢迎加入！"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid ""
"The Lord be with you, sister.  You seem new, nice to meet you.  Welcome, and"
" welcome aboard!"
msgstr "主与你同在，姐妹。你似乎是新来的，很高兴认识你。欢迎，欢迎加入！"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Nice to meet you too, Reverend."
msgstr "也很高兴见到你，牧师。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Good to see you again, Reverend.  I wanted to talk."
msgstr "很高兴再次见到你，牧师。我想谈谈。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "I'm looking for work.  Can I do anything for your congregation?"
msgstr "我正在找工作。我能为你们的会众做什么吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Nice meeting you, Reverend.  I'd best get going though."
msgstr "很高兴见到你，牧师。不过我还有要忙的。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "What can I do for you?"
msgstr "我能帮你什么忙吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Where am I?"
msgstr "我在哪？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Actually, I'm just heading out."
msgstr "其实，我该走了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "How may I help you, brother?"
msgstr "我能为你做什么，兄弟？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "How may I help you, sister?"
msgstr "我能为你做什么，姐妹？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Where am I again?"
msgstr "我又是在哪？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Could you tell me a bit about this church?"
msgstr "你能告诉我关于这个教堂的一些情况吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "We all have, brother, we all have."
msgstr "我们都有，兄弟，我们都有。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "We all have, sister, we all have."
msgstr "我们都有，姐妹，我们都有。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Thanks for your time, Reverend."
msgstr "谢谢你的时间，牧师。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid ""
"This is the New England Community Church, the congregation of it.  Praise "
"the Lord that we made it through!"
msgstr "这就是新英格兰社区教会的会众。赞美主，我们熬过去了！"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ Snippet in category "schizo_self_talk"
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#: data/json/snippets/schizophrenia.json
msgid "What are you doing out here?"
msgstr "你到这来做什么？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid ""
"We all came out here when <the_cataclysm> rocked the world.  It's an old "
"retreat Helena bought in the hopes of renovating it, good thing we did."
msgstr "当<the_cataclysm>震撼世界时，我们都来到了这里。这是海伦娜买下的一个古老的度假胜地，希望能对它进行翻新，好在我们做到了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Could I ask you a few more questions?"
msgstr "我可以再问你几个问题吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid ""
"I had a pretty comfortable life growing up.  My parents were florists, owned"
" a shop along the main street of town.  They were always so cheery, as if "
"nothing bad could phase them.  When I was about fifteen, I dreamt that the "
"Lord spoke to me; as if urging me to go and spread his Gospel, so I did.  I "
"took odd jobs at several churches for a while, before I went to seminary.  I"
" went between three different churches, before I found this one.  I've been "
"here since."
msgstr ""
"我有一个相当舒适的成长生活。我的父母是花商，在镇上的主要街道上拥有一家商店。他们总是很开心，好像没有什么坏事能影响他们。在我大约十五岁时，我梦见主对我说话；好像在催促我去传播他的福音，于是我就去了。在上神学院之前，我在几个教会打了一段时间的零工。在找到这个教会之前，我在三个不同的教会之间徘徊。之后我就一直在这里。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid ""
"The full name is the New England Community Church.  Helenas father started "
"it about twenty years ago.  The flock may be small, but we've always helped "
"each other when times were tough; we're like a family now."
msgstr "其全称是新英格兰社区教会。海伦娜的父亲大约在二十年前创办了它。我们这群人可能很小，但我们总是在困难的时候互相帮助；我们现在就像一个家庭。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "What do you think about Helena?"
msgstr "你对海伦娜有什么看法？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid ""
"&Greenwood looks over his their shoulder, briefly glancing around before "
"speaking in a low whisper.  \"Don't tell anyone I said this, but I don't "
"like Helena at all.  Her father was a real nut, he'd rave on and on about an"
" apocalypse he'd prepared for.  He always thought that his church would be "
"the ark to weather the storm, that God would destroy the world by unleashing"
" the armies of Hell; and he wasn't talking about the Second Coming of "
"Christ.  Helena's just as fanatical as he was, and it reflects in her "
"inadequate leadership.  To be honest, I'm highly concerned for some of the "
"people here; they're obsessively zealous with Helena, and harbor a "
"xenophobic hatred of everything.  As in Matthew 15:14, 'They are blind "
"guides.  And if one blind person guides another, they will both fall into a "
"pit'.\""
msgstr ""
"&格林伍德看了看自己的肩膀，在低声说话之前短暂地扫视了一下四周。\"不要告诉任何人我说过这个，但我一点也不喜欢海伦娜。她的父亲是个真正的疯子，他会滔滔不绝地讲述他所准备的启示录。他总是认为他的教堂会成为抵御风暴的方舟，上帝会通过释放地狱的军队来毁灭世界；而且他说的不是基督的第二次降临。海伦娜和他一样狂热，这反映在她不充分的领导上。说实话，我非常担心这里的一些人；他们对海伦娜的狂热，对一切都怀有仇外的仇恨。正如马太福音第十五章第十四节所说：‘他们是瞎子的向导。如果一个瞎子引导另一个瞎子，他们都要掉进坑里'。\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "How's your family?"
msgstr "你的家人怎么样了？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Is there anything I can do for you?"
msgstr "有什么我可以为你做的吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "How's the manuscript coming?"
msgstr "稿子写得怎么样了？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/cook.json
msgid "Lets talk about something else."
msgstr "让我们谈点其他的事情吧。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
msgid "Oh, hi."
msgstr "哦，嗨。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "Hey, good to see you're still around."
msgstr "嗨，很高兴看到你还在。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "Oh, hi there.  My name's Felicity, nice to see a new face."
msgstr "哦，你好。我叫费利西蒂，很高兴看到一张新面孔。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "Felicity?  Nice to meet you.  How are things here?"
msgstr "费利西蒂？很高兴见到你。这里的情况如何？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "Hi Felicity.  Got a minute?"
msgstr "嗨，费利西蒂。有空吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "Hi Felicity.  I'm afraid I can't talk right now."
msgstr "嗨，费利西蒂。恐怕我现在没空交谈。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid ""
"I'm always good for a talk.  It's nice to have company, even if we don't "
"have much else to offer."
msgstr "我一直都很喜欢聊天。有伴的感觉很好，即使我们没有什么其他东西可以提供。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "It's been nice talking to you, but I need to head out."
msgstr "和你谈话很愉快，但我该出发了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "What's on your mind?"
msgstr "你在想什么？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "They're alright.  What can I do for you?"
msgstr "他们都很好。我能为你做什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "It's nice to meet you, but I need to head out."
msgstr "很高兴认识你，但我得出发了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid ""
"I'm actually from New England, Rhode Island specifically.  I grew up in "
"Providence, the state capital.  It was lovely there, I'd always walk to "
"school and stopped in the park on my way home.  Mom was an accountant for "
"various companies, she went to Rivtech back when it was a startup.  Dad was "
"a baker, ran a shop on the corner of Chalkstone and Mt Pleasant.  It smelled"
" so good when you walked by…  I always wanted to be a writer, but I wound up"
" as a proofreader for Stillwater, a publishing firm.  I met Tom at that "
"office, we got married about three years later."
msgstr ""
"我其实来自新英格兰，确切说是罗德岛，在州府普罗维登斯长大。那真是个可爱的地方，我总是步行上学，然后回家的路上在公园逗留。妈妈是多家公司的会计师，她在 "
"Rivtech 刚成立时就进去了。爸爸是个面包师，在 Chalkstone 和 Mt Pleasant "
"的拐角开了家店。当你路过时，闻起来真是香……我一直想成为一名作家，但我最终成为了一家出版公司 Stillwater "
"的校对员。我在那间办公室认识了汤姆，大约三年后我们结婚了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "Why'd you move out here?"
msgstr "你为何搬到这里呢？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Tom and I wanted to get away from the city, so we found a home up here.  We "
"didn't move again until <the_cataclysm>, when we came here."
msgstr "汤姆和我想远离城市，所以我们在这里找到了家。直到<the_cataclysm>后，我们才再次搬家，来到这里。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid ""
"We've been through a lot without much help, it's been difficult to cope.  "
"Still, we put on a happy little face, and some of us pretend everything's "
"all right."
msgstr "我们在没有太多帮助的情况下经历了许多，实在难以应付。尽管如此，我们摆出一副快乐的小脸儿，而一些人装作万事平安。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "I suppose we do."
msgstr "我想我们会的。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "I'd better get going.  Bye, Felicity."
msgstr "我得走了。再见，费莉西蒂。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid ""
"My family's alright.  I have a wonderful daughter, Olwen; she's an "
"electronics nut, had a great job with it too.  My husband Tom is the crazy "
"one, always rambling on about conspiracy theories, secret agents, all that."
msgstr ""
"我的家人挺好。我有个了不起的女儿，奥尔文；她是个电子迷，在这方面也极有成就。我丈夫汤姆是个疯子，总是喋喋不休地谈论阴谋论、秘密特工之类的东西。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "Could you tell me more about Tom?"
msgstr "能和我说说更多关于汤姆的事吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "Could you tell me more about Olwen?"
msgstr "能和我说说更多关于奥尔文的事吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Olwen's a bright girl, always has been.  She studied electricity and "
"computer science when she was in college, found a job with a research and "
"development firm.  My girl's a fiancee now, her and Julian were going to get"
" married in a few months.  She might teach you something, if you ask."
msgstr ""
"奥尔文是个聪明的女孩，一直都是。她大学时学习电子和计算机学科，之后在科研公司找了份工作。我女儿如今是个未婚妻，她和朱利安几个月后就要结婚了。她也许可以教你些东西，如果你请教她的话。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid ""
"He wasn't always like this.  Olwen came not long after we married, he was a "
"great, caring father to her.  A few months before <the_cataclysm> is when he"
" lost it, got in some survivalist circle.  He'd stay up pouring over "
"newspapers and any documents he could find, and wound up quitting his job to"
" study it more.  We didn't see much of him for a while, always in the "
"basement, and took out a chunk of our savings to buy canned goods en masse."
msgstr ""
"他以前不是这样的。我们婚后不久就有了奥尔文，他那时是个伟大的、慈爱的父亲。<the_cataclysm>发生的几个月前，他失去了理智，陷入了一些生存主义者的圈子。他开始熬夜翻阅报纸和他能找到的任何文件，最后还辞掉了工作来进行更多研究。有段时间他老待在地下室里，我们很少见到他，他还拿出了一大笔积蓄购买了许多罐头食品。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "Is there any way to get him out of it?"
msgstr "用过什么办法帮他摆脱困境吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid ""
"I don't know.  I've tried talking to him, tried to convince him to give it "
"up.  I think he's stressed out with everything going on, and snapped because"
" of that.  I just want my husband back…"
msgstr "我不知道。我试着和他谈，试图说服他放弃。我想觉得他对发生的一切深感压抑，并因此而崩溃。我只想要我的丈夫回来……"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "I'll see what I can do.  Bye, Felicity."
msgstr "我看看我能做些什么。再见，费莉西蒂。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid ""
"It's finally finished!  Here, I want you to have a copy of it.  This is my "
"first time writing like this professionally, I hope you enjoy it."
msgstr "终于完成了！来，让你复印一份。这是我第一次像这样专职地写作，希望你喜欢它。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "Thank you, I'm sure it's lovely."
msgstr "谢谢，我肯定会喜欢的。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "I'm still working on it.  I'll have it ready soon."
msgstr "我还在努力，很快就会完成了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/foodguard.json
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/TALK_valhallist_gode.json
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/TALK_valhallist_mechanic.json
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/TALK_valhallist_member.json
msgid "Good luck with that."
msgstr "那祝你好运。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "What does a dorm leader do exactly?"
msgstr "舍监究竟是做什么的？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Can I help you with anything?"
msgstr "我能帮上什么忙？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "I want to join the community."
msgstr "我想加入你们。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "Good to see you're still around, <granny_name_g>."
msgstr "很高兴看到你还在附近，<granny_name_g>。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"Great to see a new face.  I'm Gemma.  Will you be staying here with us?"
msgstr "很高兴看到一张新面孔。我是杰玛。你会和我们一起待在这儿吗？。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "Nice to meet you, Gemma.  I'm just passing through."
msgstr "幸会，杰玛。我只是路过。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "Nice to meet you, Gemma.  I'm seeking asylum."
msgstr "幸会，杰玛。我正在寻找避难所。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "I'm already staying here.  Nice to meet you."
msgstr "我已经住在这里了。很高兴认识你。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "Hi, Gemma.  How're you doing?"
msgstr "嗨，杰玛。最近过的怎样？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "Hello, Gemma.  I'm afraid I can't talk right now."
msgstr "你好，杰玛。恐怕我现在没空交谈。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"It's nice to meet you too, survivor.  It's a tragedy what's become of the "
"New England Church Community, perhaps it'll flourish again someday."
msgstr "我也很高兴认识你，幸存者。新英格兰教会社区已成悲剧，然而终有一天它将再次兴旺。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "I'd better get going.  Nice meeting you."
msgstr "我得走了。很高兴遇到你。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"I heard what it's like out there.  You must be weary from exploring this "
"unforgiving wasteland.  I'm sorry that you're leaving us this soon."
msgstr "我听说过那里的情况。探索这片无情的荒地想必已经令你厌倦了。很遗憾你这么快就离开了我们。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"We are all under God's protection here.  Our community, like all moral "
"civilizations, has a set of rules.  Obey the Decalogue, have respect for "
"your neighbors and we'll get along just fine, okay?"
msgstr "在这里，我们皆在上帝保护之下。与所有道德的文明一样，我们社区也有一套规则。遵守十诫，尊重你的邻居，我们将相处融洽，可以吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Got it."
msgstr "知道了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "What is the Decalouge?"
msgstr "什么是十诫？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"Its also called the Ten Commandments, if you've heard it by that.  A long "
"time ago, Moses lead the Isrealites out of slavery in Egypt, towards the "
"Promised Land.  They broke their Covenant with God, and were cursed to "
"wander the desert for forty years, as opposed to the nineteen days it would "
"normally take.  On the way there, Moses went atop Mount Sinai to speak with "
"God.  He saw a burning bush, and heard the voice of the Lord; who engraved "
"the Decalouge on two tablets of stone."
msgstr ""
"如果你听说过的话，它也被称为十条诫命。很久以前，摩西带领以色列人摆脱埃及的奴役，前往应许之地。他们违背了与上帝的盟约，被诅咒要在仅十九天路程的沙漠中游荡四十年。在去那里的路上，摩西登上西奈山顶与上帝交谈。他看见燃烧的荆棘，又听见耶和华的声音；是祂将十诫刻在两块石板上。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"&Gemma is in deep, silent thought for a moment, before clearing her throat."
"  \"They read: 'I am the Lord your God, who brought you out of Egypt, out of"
" the land of slavery.  You shall have no other gods before me.  You shall "
"not make for yourself a carved image, or any likeness of anything that is in"
" heaven above, or that is in the earth beneath, or that is in the water "
"under the earth.  You shall not take the name of the Lord your God in vain."
"  Remember the Sabbath day, and keep it holy.  Honor your father and your "
"mother.  You shall not murder.  You shall not commit adultery.  You shall "
"not steal.  You shall not bear false witness against your neighbor.  You "
"shall not covet your neighbors house.\"  They're written in Exodus 20:1-17, "
"for future reference."
msgstr ""
"&杰玛沉思片刻，然后清了清嗓子。“他们读到：‘我是主你的神，曾将你从埃及为奴之地领出来。除我以外，你不可有别的神。不可为自己雕刻偶像，也不可做什么形像仿佛上天、下地，和地底下、水中的百物。当记念安息日，守为圣日。当孝敬父母。不可杀人。不可奸淫。不可偷盗。不可作假见证陷害邻人。不可贪恋邻人的房屋。”它们写在出埃及记"
" 20:1-17 中，供将来参考。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"You are most welcome here.  In the good old days we would've held a ceremony"
" for you.  Oh well, times have changed.  Accept this blanket, you may choose"
" either bed by the window.  If you're hungry, you can go see Simon for a "
"meal, up to one per day."
msgstr ""
"这里非常欢迎你。在过往的美好时光里，我们能为你举办一场仪式。哦，好吧，时代变了。收下这条毯子，你可以选靠窗的任一张床。饿了可以去找西蒙吃顿饭，一天最多一顿。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "Thank you.  See you around, Gemma."
msgstr "谢谢你。回见，杰玛。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "My story?  It's been told a thousand times."
msgstr "我的故事？那已经说过上千遍了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "What was it you said earlier?"
msgstr "你刚才说什么？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"I always have things on the go: tidying, organizing, cleaning, but I don't "
"complain.  I never complain."
msgstr "我总有事情要忙：收拾整理、组织活动、打扫卫生，但我不抱怨。从不抱怨。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "There sure is.  Well, bye."
msgstr "肯定的。那再见啦。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"I'm feeling great!  Even if the world's over, I always have myself and God "
"above."
msgstr "我感觉棒极了！即使世界终结，我总是与至高的神同在。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "I'm feeling alright, just working away."
msgstr "我感觉挺好，就是在工作。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "I'm happy to hear that, Gemma.  I'd best be going."
msgstr "杰玛，我很高兴听到这个。我得走了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/foodguard.json
msgid "I'll see you around."
msgstr "咱们回头见。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid ""
"My flowers look a bit dehydrated, I'd appreciate it if you watered them for "
"me.  These indoor plants are the most calming reminders of life before "
"<the_cataclysm>."
msgstr "我的花看起来有点脱水，如果你能帮我浇水，我将不胜感激。这些室内植物是<the_cataclysm>前生活最安详的回忆。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "I meant \"Are there any jobs you know of?\""
msgstr "我的意思是“你知道有什么工作吗？”"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "Sure.  Well, bye."
msgstr "确实。那再见啦。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Blessings to you."
msgstr "祝福你。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Stranger, what brings you to our holy home?"
msgstr "陌生人，是什么带你来到我们神圣的家园？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid "Good to see you again."
msgstr "很高兴再次见到你。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I can't talk right now."
msgstr "我现在没空交谈。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I'm Helena, the caretaker of this flock.  Who might you be, wanderer?"
msgstr "我是海伦娜，这羊群的牧守者。汝是何人，流浪者？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I'm not doing much wandering, I'm staying here."
msgstr "我并未长久流浪，我如今留在这里。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I'm just passing through.  I'll see you around."
msgstr "我只是路过。我们回头见。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Just like all the sinners, roaming through Hell."
msgstr "就像所有的罪人一般，在地狱中游荡。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "It certainly seems like it."
msgstr "看起来确实如此。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "See ya later, crazy lady."
msgstr "回头见，疯狂的女士。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I'm glad you could make it here.  May the Lord have mercy on you."
msgstr "很高兴你能来这里。愿主怜悯你。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Thank you, I hope he shares that sentiment."
msgstr "谢谢，我希望他感同身受。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Thank you.  I'll see you around."
msgstr "谢谢。我们回头见。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
msgid "What do you need?"
msgstr "你想要什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Corrie and I have finished that solar cart."
msgstr "科里和我已经完成了那辆太阳能车。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Olwen's finished the radio transmitter she was working on."
msgstr "奥尔文完成了她正在研究的无线电发射器。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"I am a prophet, like my uncle before me.  He saw <the_cataclysm>, the "
"righteous judgement of God and set about preparing an ark to save us.  He "
"passed before his visions could be fulfilled, and now I carry his righteous "
"banner."
msgstr ""
"我是个先知，就像我之前的叔叔一样。他看到了<the_cataclysm>，神公义的审判，并且着手准备方舟来拯救我们。他在他的愿景实现之前就过世了，现在由我高举他的正义旗帜。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"He had many visions, and he had many secrets.  I don't know all of them, but"
" there was one he was highly vocal about, regarding <the_cataclysm>, that "
"according to him \"The spawn of Satan shall descend upon the Earth, and all "
"will be consumed in death and destruction\".  He never said much else about "
"it, and always had a mortified face whenever someone brought it up."
msgstr ""
"他看到了很多东西，他还有很多秘密。我对这些毫不知情，但有一个他直言不讳，是和<the_cataclysm>有关的。根据他的说法，“撒旦的产物将降临地球，所有的一切都将在死亡和毁灭中被吞噬”。他从未提起更多细节，每当有人说起这件事时，他总是一副羞愧的表情。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"Thanks to my uncle's forethought, we've been blessed by God.  We have plenty"
" of food for ourselves, safety from the hordes of Hell, and the continued "
"protection of the Lord our God."
msgstr "感谢我叔叔的先见之明，我们得到了上帝的祝福。我们有足够的食物供自己享用，免受地狱大军的伤害，并得到我们的主——上帝的持续保护。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"They denied us, they labeled us as a doomsday cult, threw sticks and stones "
"at us, and yet, we were standing resiliently.  Why?  Because we knew God was"
" on our side."
msgstr "他们否认我们，他们给我们贴上末日邪教的标签，向我们扔棍棒和石头，然而，我们却坚强地站了起来。为什么？因为我们知道上帝站在我们这边。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"We are all under God's protection here.  Our community, like all moral "
"civilizations, has a set of rules.  Obey the Decalogue, have respect for "
"your neighbors and we'll get along just fine.  Go see Gemma or Julian for a "
"bed, if one's available.  We do have limited space on our Ark, though."
msgstr ""
"在这里，我们皆在上帝保护之下。与所有道德的文明一样，我们社区也有一套规则。遵守十诫，尊重你的邻居，我们将相处融洽。如果还有空位，你可以去找杰玛或朱利安申请张床位。不过，我们方舟上的空间确实有限。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Okay, I'll see about that later."
msgstr "好的，我稍后去看看。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Okay, I'll see about that.  Goodbye."
msgstr "好，我会考虑的。拜拜。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"&Helena flips through her Bible before stopping.  \"They read: 'I am the "
"Lord your God, who brought you out of Egypt, out of the land of slavery.  "
"You shall have no other gods before me.  You shall not make for yourself a "
"carved image, or any likeness of anything that is in heaven above, or that "
"is in the earth beneath, or that is in the water under the earth.  You shall"
" not take the name of the Lord your God in vain.  Remember the Sabbath day, "
"and keep it holy.  Honor your father and your mother.  You shall not murder."
"  You shall not commit adultery.  You shall not steal.  You shall not bear "
"false witness against your neighbor.  You shall not covet your neighbors "
"house.\"  They're written in Exodus 20:1-17, for future reference."
msgstr ""
"&海伦娜翻了几页她的圣经，然后停了下来。“他们读到：‘我是主你的神，曾将你从埃及为奴之地领出来。除我以外，你不可有别的神。不可为自己雕刻偶像，也不可做什么形像仿佛上天、下地，和地底下、水中的百物。当记念安息日，守为圣日。当孝敬父母。不可杀人。不可奸淫。不可偷盗。不可作假见证陷害邻人。不可贪恋邻人的房屋。”它们写在出埃及记"
" 20:1-17 中，供将来参考。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"I like what you and Corrie's put together.  I did promise payment for a "
"proof-of-concept, what'll it be?"
msgstr "我可喜欢你和科里一起造出来的那玩意了。之前我说过会给原型机付报酬的，你想要点什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I'll have some icons."
msgstr "我要些圣像。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I want Corrie to have some extra rations."
msgstr "我想让科里多领点口粮。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Let's negotiate some other time."
msgstr "我们下次再谈这件事吧。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Here's your money.  Don't spend it all in one place."
msgstr "这是你的报酬。可别一股脑花光了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"A generous soul, are we?  That's not what I was expecting, but I'll see to "
"it."
msgstr "一个慷慨的灵魂，可不是么？这可真出乎我的意料了，但我保证会做到的。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"Yes, I was just informed of that.  I also heard that she found a large group"
" of people living out in an old evacuation center, who consider themselves "
"merchants.  That would be a good place to resume our spread of the Truth, "
"perhaps we could find others who were faithful before <the_cataclysm>."
msgstr ""
"是的，我刚刚听说这件事了。我还听说她找到了一大群住在破旧的难民中心的人，自称是什么商会的。这将是一处让我们重新传播福音的好地方，也许我们能找到些在<the_cataclysm>前的虔诚信徒。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I presume you want me to pay a visit?"
msgstr "我猜你是不是想让我过去拜访一下？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Oh, I've met them before!"
msgstr "哦，我以前见过他们！"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid ""
"Yes, you seem like a good fit for the job.  I'll pay you a small sum for "
"getting some information about them."
msgstr "是的，你看起来很适合这项任务。我会付给你些报酬，换取些关于他们的情报。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Alright, I'll go and see what's up."
msgstr "好的，我去看看是怎么一回事。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Really?  I'd pay a small sum for information about them."
msgstr "真的吗？我愿意花笔小钱来换取关于他们的情报。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Well, they're…"
msgstr "好吧，他们是……"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Need any help?"
msgstr "需要帮忙么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Could you provide any medical services?"
msgstr "你能帮我看看病吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"I might have some medicine for the community.  Anything you're missing?"
msgstr "我这里为教会备了一些药。你缺点什么吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Are you taking care of Arturo?"
msgstr "你在照顾阿图罗吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Do you want to come with me?"
msgstr "想要和我同行吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
msgid "How can I help you?"
msgstr "我能帮你什么忙吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"Oh, I don't think we've met before.  My name's Jane, I'm the local doctor."
msgstr "哦，我想我们以前没见过面。我叫简，我是这里的医生。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Nice to meet you too, Jane."
msgstr "很高兴见到你，简。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Hi, Jane.  Got a minute?"
msgstr "嗨，简。有空吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Always nice to meet a fellow outsider.  How can I help you?"
msgstr "能见到个外乡人总是那么美好。我能帮你什么忙吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Sure, I don't see why not.  I've gotta keep my mind off stuff anyway."
msgstr "当然，没什么不行的。反正我现在也得找些能消耗精力的事干。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"I'm doing somewhat well, thanks to my occupation.  The other joinees, well, "
"they're barely scraping by.  It's been tense, and I'm not seeing it change "
"for the better."
msgstr "由于我的职业，我过的还算可以。其他教友，额，他们只是勉强糊口而已。气氛一直很紧张，而我也看不出情况有好转的迹象。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"I was a physician, one of the more unfortunate people who didn't call in "
"sick during the riots.  I remember it all so clearly, the cuts, bruises, "
"deep bites, then those oily black eyes, caustic yellow blood, spastic fungal"
" growths… it was <swear> gnarly.  Then things descended into all-new levels "
"of fucked up, and some of my coworkers were preparing to just get the hell "
"out.  I followed them."
msgstr ""
"我曾经是一名医生，属于是暴乱期间没能请上病假的倒霉蛋中的一员。我记得很清楚，伤口、瘀伤、深深的咬伤，然后是那些油乎乎的黑眼睛、腐蚀性的黄血、痉挛的真菌生长……太<swear>可怕了。然后事情进展到了一种全新的混乱水平，我的一些同事已经做好了赶紧开溜的准备，我也跟着他们一起溜了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Were you evaced'?"
msgstr "你们被疏散了？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "No, not by the government."
msgstr "不，不关政府的事。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"No, not really.  I came here after I was split from my friends by a horde of"
" <zombies>.  They let me in after I gave away some food I found.  The church"
" distrusts my profession; I get by helping Kostas."
msgstr ""
"不，算不上好。我是在一群<zombies>把我和朋友分开后才来到这里的。在我捐出了一些我找到的食物后，我得以进来。教会不信任我的职业；我是靠帮科斯塔斯打下手才勉强活下来的。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"I really don't, actually.  Even my help is thankless here.  Bandaging cuts, "
"setting bones, disinfecting wounds; who needs all that when they can pray "
"anything away?"
msgstr "实话说，我真不需要。即使在这里我干的也是吃力不讨好的活。包扎伤口、固定骨骼、消毒伤口；当他们可以祈祷解决一切问题的时候，谁还需要这些呢？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Do you have any work available?"
msgstr "你这里有什么需要我做的吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Would you like to buy any supplies?"
msgstr "你想买些医疗用品吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"I do what I can, but he's mostly beyond my skillset.  Coke's a <swear> "
"<name_b>, really messes a person up.  Arturo was on it for several years "
"before he tried to get help, now he has auditory hallucinations; hears "
"voices from nowhere.  Traumatic experiences have a harsher effect on "
"recovering addicts, but <the_cataclysm> is worse than anything we've gone "
"through before."
msgstr ""
"我尽我所能，但他已经远远超出了我的能力范围。快克是一种<swear><name_b>，真的能毁掉一个人。阿图罗在求医之前，已经吸了好几年，现在甚至出现了幻听；凭空听见各种声音。创伤经历对脱瘾者的影响更严重，而<the_cataclysm>比我们之前经历的任何事情都要糟糕。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"Thorazine would go us a long way, but Arturo's having trouble getting it.  "
"They think he's the key and that my help would obstruct him.  Regardless, "
"there's just so much anti-medical sentiment here that I've given up on "
"prescribing anything."
msgstr ""
"冬眠灵可以管上一阵子，但阿图罗很难找到这种药。他们认为他是关键人物，而我的治疗会阻碍他。无论如何，这里有太多的反医情绪，以至于我已经不敢开处方了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "What about Kostas?  The Church seems to trust him."
msgstr "科斯塔斯呢？教会似乎很信任他。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"He's an alright physician, but the Church massively overrates him.  They "
"think his 'natural medicine' can cure anything, like he's a magic medicine "
"man.  God created everything, so what on Earth isn't natural?!"
msgstr ""
"他是个不错的医生，但教会对他评价过高了。他们认为他的“纯天然药物”可以治愈任何东西，仿佛他是个魔法药师一样。既然上帝创造了一切，那么地球上有什么不是天然的呢？！"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "How do you feel about him personally?"
msgstr "你觉得他这个人怎么样？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"Personally, I like him.  We've worked together for a few cases, but most "
"people refuse to let me work; they only want to see him."
msgstr "就我个人而言，我喜欢他。我们一起工作过几次，但大多数人拒绝让我看病；他们只想见他。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"Sure, I've got some supplies on hand, just give me a minute and you'll be "
"right as rain.  It'll cost three icons."
msgstr "当然，我手头正好有一些药，给我一分钟，你会没事的。只要三个圣像。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "I can pay for quality work.  Here it is."
msgstr "我付得起好的医疗服务。给你。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I've changed my mind.  Let's talk about something else."
msgstr "我改变主意了，我们谈点别的吧。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"I'm up for it, Arturo's got enough medicine for two-and-half months.  It's "
"thankless work around here, so let's blow this joint."
msgstr "我准备好了，阿图罗的药够吃上两个半月了。在这算是吃力不讨好的活，所以让我们赶紧离开这里吧。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"I'd like to leave, but I've got to take care of Arturo.  He's always low or "
"nearly out of antipsychotics, so I do what I can."
msgstr "我想离开，但我得照顾阿图罗。他用的抗精神病药剩不多了，要么就是几乎没有，所以我得尽我所能。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Alright.  Wanna chat?"
msgstr "好吧，能聊聊不？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid ""
"I could always use more bandages, disinfectant, and the like.  What do you "
"have?"
msgstr "我总是需要更多的绷带、消毒液之类的。你有些什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "I don't have anything right now.  Lets talk about something else."
msgstr "我现在什么都没有，我们谈点别的吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "I don't have anything right now.  I'll come back with something later."
msgstr "我现在什么都没有。我以后再带些来。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/TALK_valhallist_shopkeeper.json
msgid "I have <topic_item>."
msgstr "我有<topic_item>。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
msgid "What's your take on the situation here?"
msgstr "你对这里的情况还有什么看法？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "What are your parents like?"
msgstr "你的父母怎么样了？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "What are your plans after <the_cataclysm>?"
msgstr "你在<the_cataclysm>之后有什么打算吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Were could I find work around here?"
msgstr "我能在这里找到活干吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Hey, look who's back."
msgstr "嗨，看看谁回来了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
msgid "Hey again."
msgstr "嘿，又来了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
msgid "Oh, hey, it's you again."
msgstr "哦，嗨，又是你。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Oh, uh… you look new.  Didn't think we'd see new people here.  Hey."
msgstr "哦，呃……你看起来是个新人。没想到我们能在这里看到新面孔。嘿。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "I'm just a traveler, kid.  I won't be staying here for long."
msgstr "我只是个路人，孩子。我不会在这里呆太久。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "I'm not exactly new here, kid."
msgstr "我算不上新人了，孩子。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Hey, Jerry.  What's up?"
msgstr "嗨，杰里。怎么了？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Hey, kid.  I can't stay to talk."
msgstr "嗨，孩子。我不能留下来聊天。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I have a name, you know.  It's Jeremiah, but people just call me Jerry."
msgstr "我有名字的，知道吗。我叫耶利米，但大伙都叫我杰里。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Sorry, Jerry.  What's up?"
msgstr "抱歉，杰里。怎么了？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Sorry, Jeremiah.  I'll be on my way."
msgstr "抱歉，耶利米。我该走了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I thought asking about each other's emotions went out of style after "
"<the_cataclysm>.  Uhm, okay then.  I'm fine, I guess."
msgstr "我本认为见面询问对方的情绪在<the_cataclysm>之后就已经过时了。嗯，好吧。我想我还行吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "I noticed you're holding a D&D handbook.  Do you play much?"
msgstr "我注意到你随身带着一本D&D手册。你经常玩吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "I've convinced Kostas to take you on."
msgstr "我已经说服科斯塔斯教你了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"My take?  You already know how things are.  People are dead, my friends are "
"dead, so yeah.  At least there's no school, the adults just love reminding "
"me that.  You know what?  I kinda miss school."
msgstr "我的看法？你已经知道情况如何了。人们都死了，我的朋友也死了，就是这样。至少没有学校了，大人们总喜欢提醒我这一点。但其实我有点怀念校园了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I was in high school, like anyone else my age.  Then out of nowhere, my mom "
"pulled me out of school to \"save me\".  I got packed into a bus with my "
"parents and their old-timey friends.  We've been stuck here ever since.  "
"Actually, it's not all that bad.  I'm studying to be a herbalist like "
"Kostas, which is cool I guess."
msgstr ""
"我是个高中生，和其他同龄人一样。然后，我妈妈突然把我从学校拖出来“救我”。我和父母以及他们的老朋友一同挤进了一辆大巴。从那以后，我们就一直被困在这里。实话说，情况也没那么糟。我正在学习成为像科斯塔斯这样的草药师，我想这很酷。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Tell me about your parents."
msgstr "跟我说说你的父母吧。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, I play.  I ran a campaign for a while with some of my friends, we'd "
"play after school.  I don't know where they are now, though.  Do you wanna "
"play some?"
msgstr "是的，我玩。我以前一直和我的一些朋友跑团，在我们放学后。不过我不知道他们现在在哪里。你也想玩一局吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Sure, I'm up for it."
msgstr "当然，我准备好了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "No thanks, I'd better get going."
msgstr "不，谢谢。我得走了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"&Jeremiah leans his head towards your ear, speaking in a low whisper.  \"To "
"be honest with you, I don't like my mom at all.  She's like a <swear> "
"helicopter, always telling me what to do, where to go, who I can be with.  "
"She never thinks of me as an individual, only some idea of who she thinks I "
"am.  My dad's alright, he's the chef around here.\""
msgstr ""
"&耶利米把头靠在你的耳边，悄悄说道：“老实说，我一点都不喜欢我妈。她就像一架<swear>直升机，总是告诉我该做什么，去哪里，可以和谁在一起。她从不把我当成一个独立的人，只是她想要的样子。我爸还好，他是这的厨师。”"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "I'll be on my way."
msgstr "我这就出发。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I don't know, exactly.  I think I'll stay here and do what I can for the "
"community."
msgstr "确切地说我也不知道。但我想我会留在这里，为社区尽一份力。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I'd like to study herbology with Kostas, it seems like a useful skill these "
"days.  I do feel bad for Jane though, she's a skilled doctor and nobody here"
" cares, they all just think any illness can be prayed away."
msgstr ""
"我想和科斯塔斯一起学习草药学，这似乎是一项有用的技能。不过，我确实为简感到难过，她是一名资深医生，但这里没有人关心，他们都认为任何疾病都可以通过祈祷来消除。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "When do you plan on starting that apprenticeship?"
msgstr "你打算什么时候开始当学徒？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"Well…  Kostas is a bit unsure about teaching me, for some reason.  If you "
"could change his mind, I'd pay you some \"icons\", what we've started using "
"for money around here."
msgstr "嗯……科斯塔斯有点不太想教我。如果你能改变他的想法，我会付给你一些“圣像”，我们已经开始用它当货币了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "No thanks.  Let's talk about something else."
msgstr "不，谢谢。我们谈点其他的事情吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "I'll see what I can do for you."
msgstr "我看看我能为你做些什么。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "That's great!  Thanks <name_g>, here's the money."
msgstr "干得不错！谢谢<name_g>，这是给你的钱。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "You're welcome."
msgstr "不客气。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"Darryl should have something for you to do if you like gardening, Jane could"
" use some medical supplies, too.  If you like to be bossed around, Helena "
"probably has a few things that need doing.  I'd just ask around, really."
msgstr "如果你喜欢园艺，达里尔可以给点事你做，简也需要一些医疗用品。如果你喜欢被人摆布，海伦娜可能有一些事情需要做。我只是四处听说到的，真的。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Is there anything you need?"
msgstr "你还需要什么吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "What are the advantages of being a dorm leader?"
msgstr "当个舍监有什么好处？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Why did you join the Church?"
msgstr "你为什么加入教会？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hey, <name_g>."
msgstr "嘿，<name_g>。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid ""
"Hey, a new face.  I'm Julian, the guy in charge of this room.  You're "
"planning on sticking around or somethin'?"
msgstr "嘿，一张新面孔。我叫朱利安，目前管着这个房间。你是打算留下还是怎么的？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Nice to meet you, Julian.  I'm just passing through."
msgstr "很高兴见到你，朱利安。我只是路过。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Nice to meet you, Julian.  I'm seeking asylum."
msgstr "很高兴见到你，朱利安。我正在寻找避难所。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "I'm a joinee actually.  Nice to meet you."
msgstr "其实我已经是教友了。很高兴认识你。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hey, good to see you again."
msgstr "嘿，很高兴又见到你了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Hello, Julian.  I can't stay to talk."
msgstr "嗨，朱利安。我不能留下来聊天。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "If you have complaints, please don't tell anyone."
msgstr "如果你有抱怨，请不要告诉任何人。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "You're still staying here, joinee?"
msgstr "你怎么还在这里，教友？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Need anything, joinee?"
msgstr "需要什么吗，教友？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Need anything?"
msgstr "需要什么吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "Go on…"
msgstr "继续……"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid ""
"You sure?  I mean, you've been traveling for a long time, haven't you?  "
"Alright, it's your decision.  Let me know when you changed your mind."
msgstr "你确定吗？我是说，你已经旅行了很长时间了，不是吗？好吧，这是你的决定。当你改变主意时告诉我。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid ""
"Aight, here are the rules: don't commit sins, don't litter, and try not to "
"die.  Have some mutual respect, capiche?"
msgstr "好吧，这里有份守则：别犯罪，别扔垃圾，尽量别死。相互尊重点，行不？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid ""
"Your name is now on the books.  Here's your blanket, joinee.  Those two beds"
" next to the window, you can choose one of them.  It's safe, don't worry.  "
"I'm armed.  By the way, if you're hungry you can go bug Simon for a meal, up"
" to one in a day."
msgstr ""
"你的名字现在列在名册里了。这是你的毯子，教友。窗户旁边的那两张床，你可以选一张。这里很安全，不用担心。我有武器。顺便说一下，如果你饿了，你可以去找西蒙吃顿饭，一天最多吃一顿。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Thank you.  See you around, Julian."
msgstr "谢谢你。回见，朱利安。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid ""
"&Julian suddenly appears disturbed, and looks away from you for a moment.  "
"\"It's a long story, and not an interesting one at that.  I was a cop "
"before.  You must've heard about those riots and all that.  I'm glad we all "
"managed to make it out alive.\""
msgstr ""
"&朱利安突然显得很不安，眼神避开你了一小会儿：“那是个很长的故事，一点也不有趣。我以前是一名警察。你一定听说过那场暴乱和之后的事情。我很高兴我们都成功地活了下来。”"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "How did you make it out?"
msgstr "你怎么活下来的？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid ""
"Well, I might as well be honest with you.  I ran mostly, ran like the devil "
"was chasin' me.  I was at one of the police stations in town, when we were "
"called out to handle a violent mob on the loose.  When we got there, the "
"people were crazy, smashing and killing everything in their way.  They had "
"these bloodshot eyes and a weird goo in their mouths.  We pulled out all the"
" stops to handle them.  When tear gas wouldn't work, the chief told us to "
"draw guns and kill them all.  We did…  There was so much blood…  That "
"maneuver killed a lot of them, but not all.  One snuck up behind a lady who "
"worked with us, tore a whole section of her spine out.  She never even had "
"time to scream, just slumped over the cruiser door…  So I jumped post and "
"ran, never looked back.  God, I can still hear the cries…"
msgstr ""
"好吧，我想和你实话实说也无妨。我大多数时间都在逃跑，就像魔鬼在追着我一样。当时我在镇上的一个警察局，我们接到通知去管控一群暴民。当我们到达那里时，人们都疯了，用各种方式粉碎和杀害一切。他们双眼布满血丝，嘴里有种奇怪的粘液。我们用尽一切办法来对付他们。当催泪瓦斯不起作用时，警长告诉我们拔枪，把他们全部杀死。我们做到了……留了太多的血……那次行动杀死了很多人，但不是所有人。有一只偷偷溜到一位和我们一起工作的女士身后，把她的脊柱撕了一大截下来。她甚至连尖叫的时间都没有，就那样瘫倒在警车门上……所以我跳船逃走了，再也没回过头。天啊，我仿佛还能听到那种惨叫声……"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "I'm sorry for your loss.  Maybe we should change the subject."
msgstr "我为你的损失感到难过。也许我们该换个话题。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "I'm sorry for your loss.  I gotta go."
msgstr "请节哀。我得走了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Advantages?  All I do is work!"
msgstr "好处？我手头只有做不完的活！"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Anything I can do to help you out?"
msgstr "我能帮你什么忙吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Yeah, it must be exhausting.  Well, bye."
msgstr "是的，一定很累。好吧，再见。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid ""
"It's been a struggle, trying to keep this bunch together.  Oh things could "
"be better here, of course.  It could always be, but sometimes we don't even "
"realize how good we have it here."
msgstr "这是份吃力不讨好的活，试图让这群人团结在一起。当然，情况本可以更好。人总是这样，但有时我们甚至没有意识到现状有多好。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid ""
"When I was younger, I used to go to church with my family.  When I started "
"growing up, I saw all this evil around me, people hating and persecuting "
"others, despite the teachings of Jesus; I just stopped going one day, "
"decided to make my own way.  I joined the NECC a few years back to rekindle "
"my relationship with God, get back to who I was."
msgstr ""
"当我年轻的时候，我经常和家人一起去教堂。当我开始长大的时候，我看到了我周围的一切邪恶，人们憎恨和迫害他人，无视耶稣的教导；我只是在某一天停了下来，决定走自己的路。几年前，我加入了新英格兰教会，重新唤醒了我与主的联结，寻回自我。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "I'd rather not talk about it."
msgstr "我不想谈这件事情。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Yeah, I can understand.  See ya later."
msgstr "是的，我能理解。再见。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Can you tell me about Arturo?"
msgstr "能和我说说关于阿图罗的事情吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Can you tell me about Corrie?"
msgstr "能和我说说关于科里的事情吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Can you tell me about Jane?"
msgstr "能和我说说关于简的事情吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Can you tell me about Sonia?"
msgstr "能和我说说关于索尼娅的事情吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Can you tell me about Zachary?"
msgstr "能和我说说关于扎卡里的事情吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Can you tell me about Simon?"
msgstr "能和我说说关于西蒙的事情吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Can you tell me about Jeremiah?"
msgstr "能和我说说关于耶利米的事情吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/valhallist_leader_backstory.json
msgid "What did you do before <the_cataclysm>?"
msgstr "你在<the_cataclysm>之前是做什么的？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "You don't seem to like the joinees very much.  Why is that?"
msgstr "你似乎不太喜欢新入会者。为什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Do you know where I could find some work?"
msgstr "你知道我在哪能找到活干吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Oh well, yet another survivor.  Welcome to our group, I'm Katherine."
msgstr "哦，好吧，又是一个幸存者。欢迎来到我们这个小团体，我叫凯瑟琳。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Hi, Katherine.  How's it going?"
msgstr "嗨，凯瑟琳。近况如何？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Nice to meet you, Katherine."
msgstr "很高兴见到你，凯瑟琳。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "It's always a pleasure.  How may I help you?"
msgstr "总是很高兴见到新人。我能为你做什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
msgid "I just had some questions."
msgstr "我只是有些问题。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "We have many things to pray for, I'm afraid."
msgstr "恐怕我们有很多事要祈祷。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I understand.  I don't have the answers you are looking for, I'm afraid."
msgstr "我理解。恐怕我没有你想要的答案。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "I'll be on my way then."
msgstr "那我还是走吧。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"Our prayers were heard.  We knew the day was coming, so we prepared.  Our "
"community stockpiled months' worth of canned goods, well enough until the "
"chaos ends.  With the food we have left, we could live peacefully, but we "
"foolishly didn't take extra people into consideration.  With so much at "
"risk, I don't think we can afford more people.  Though I'm not the one who "
"makes the decisions here, and it's probably for the better."
msgstr ""
"我们的祈祷受了回应。我们知道末日即将到来，所以我们做好了准备。我们社区囤积了几个月的罐头食品，直到混乱结束。有了剩下的食物，我们本可以平静地生活，但我们愚蠢地没有考虑到额外增加的人口。现在处境已经很危险，我觉得我们负担不起更多的人。虽然我不是在这里能做主的人，但这种决定可能会更好。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Can you can take in joinees once there's a vacancy?"
msgstr "一旦出现了空缺，你能接受新教友加入吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I worked for the Church, organized charities and filed paperwork.  That's "
"how I met the Founder.  I did so much for everyone, yet they never noticed…"
msgstr "我为教会工作，组织慈善机构并负责文书。我就是这样认识创始人的。我为每个人做了很多，但他们从来没有注意到……"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"You're right, I don't.  They should've come when they had the chance.  Now "
"that our Ark has sailed, they want to jump aboard.  Such is the way of "
"sinners, I suppose."
msgstr "你说得对，我不太喜欢。他们本就应该一有机会就加入。而现在我们的方舟已经启航，他们却想跳上船。我想这就是罪人的行为。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"If there's a vacancy.  Even then, there's the decision of which joinee to "
"include.  Those people don't share or respect the same values as we do.  "
"None of them are promising candidates."
msgstr "只在有空缺的情况下。即使如此，也要决定哪一个入会者能加入。这些人没有分享或尊重与我们一样的价值观，他们都算不上有希望的候选人。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Jesus warned us about false prophets."
msgstr "耶稣警告我们要提防假先知。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"She knows this and that about electronics.  The generator we have here was "
"made by her.  Nice to have one here, even though there's not much use for it"
" yet."
msgstr "她对电子产品了如指掌。我们这里的发电机是她造的。能弄一台在这里肯定不错，虽然它目前还没有多大用处。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I hear she knows this and that about electronics.    She keeps herself "
"occupied by doing menial tasks around the camp, looking for payment."
msgstr "我听说她对电子产品了如指掌。她一直忙着在营地四周做些杂活，寻找报酬。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"There's not an illness God can't cure.  Yet, by fate, we were given a "
"doctor.  She's now taking care of Arturo, that poor thing.  Oh well, who am "
"I to question God's ways?"
msgstr "没有上帝无法治愈的疾病。然而，命运却给我们送来了一个医生。她现在在照顾阿图罗，那个可怜的家伙。哦，我又怎敢质疑上帝的意志？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"She occasionally plays her guitar in the hall, and she's quite good at it.  "
"Unsurprisingly, she doesn't know any hymns.  Wouldn't let her near my son."
msgstr "她偶尔会在大厅里弹吉他，而且弹得很好。毫不意外，她不会唱赞美诗。不会让她靠近我儿子的。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"My dear, sweet husband.  He worked as a cook for one of the homeless "
"shelters, that's how we met.  He's always liked to try new things.  He "
"should be in the dining hall, if you want to see him."
msgstr "我亲爱的，亲爱的丈夫。他之前在一家流浪者收容所当厨师，我们就是这样认识的。他总是喜欢尝试新事物。如果你想见他，他应该在餐厅。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"He's my son, such a wonderful boy.  He's always been the light in my life, "
"and I've tried to teach him well.  We've been a bit distant as of late, but "
"I'm sure he'll come around."
msgstr "他是我儿子，真是个好孩子。他一直是我生命中的光，我一直在努力教他。我们最近有点疏远，但我相信他会回心转意的。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"He can keep his distance with his smug nothingness.  At least he's a bit "
"more useful than some of the others.  He helped Corrie make that generator."
msgstr "他可以保持与他那自以为是的虚无的距离。至少他比其他人有用一点。他帮助科里造了那台发电机。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I'm not planning to communicate with him, that's for certain.  He can keep "
"his distance with his smug nothingness.  At least he knows how to cut "
"lumber."
msgstr "我不打算和他交流，这是肯定的。他可以保持与他那自以为是的虚无的距离。至少他知道如何伐木。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"If you're here for an exciting story, you're talking with the wrong person."
"  Ever since I was born I've lived very modestly.  Did I regret it?  No, it "
"will all be worth it in the end…"
msgstr "如果你来这里是为了一个激动人心的故事，那你可找错人了。自从我出生以来，我就过着朴实无华的生活。我后悔了吗？不，这一切最终都是值得的……"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Tell me about the community."
msgstr "和我说说这个社区吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
msgid "Tell me about your family."
msgstr "和我说说你的家庭情况。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I've been a member of the New England Church Community for a quarter of a "
"century, took part in each and every sermon and gathering they held even "
"while I was carrying my boy Jeremiah.  Not to mention the countless times we"
" visited those filthy homeless shelters and prisons filled with sinners.  I "
"even met the Founder himself.  I can confidently say I'm more worthy to be "
"here than those impostors who leech on us at this camp."
msgstr ""
"我成为新英格兰教会社区的一员的时间已经接近四分之一个世纪了，参加了他们举行的每一场布道和聚会，甚至在我怀着我的儿子耶利米的时候。更不用说我们无数次参观那些肮脏的流浪者收容所和充满罪人的监狱了。我甚至见过创始人本人。我可以自信地说，我比那些在这个营地里依赖我们的冒名顶替者更有资格呆在这里。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "The Founder?"
msgstr "创始人？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"I'm sure you've met my husband, Simon.  He was also a volunteer at a "
"homeless shelter, working as a cook.  We were brought together by the hands "
"of fate as some would say.  We have a son together, Jeremiah, the light in "
"my life.  Such a creative and well-behaved boy, I just wish we could find an"
" appropriate woman for him."
msgstr ""
"我肯定你已经见过我丈夫西蒙了。他也是流浪者收容所的志愿者，当厨师。正如有些人所说，是命运之手让我们相会的。我们有一个儿子，耶利米，我生命中的光。那么一个富有创造力又举止得体的男孩，我真希望我们能为他找到一位合适的女士。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid ""
"He was quite reserved when I met him, seemed distant in his thoughts.  "
"Theresa has the answers you are looking for."
msgstr "我第一次见到他时，他还很矜持，沉浸在自己的思索之中。特蕾莎有你想要的答案。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "I'll talk to her then."
msgstr "好吧，我会去跟她谈谈。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "I have the pine needles you asked me for."
msgstr "我找到了你要的松针。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard3.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
msgid "What do you do around here?"
msgstr "你在这里干什么？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"You must be new here, nice to meet you.  They call me Kostas, I'm the local "
"herbalist."
msgstr "你一定是新来的，很高兴认识你。他们叫我科斯塔斯，我是本地的草药师。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Nice to meet you too, Kostas."
msgstr "很高兴见到你，科斯塔斯。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "I heard Jeremiah wanted to learn a few things from you."
msgstr "我听说耶利米想向你学些东西。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Hi, Kostas.  Care to trade?"
msgstr "嗨，科斯塔斯。想交易吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Hey, Kostas.  I can't stay to talk."
msgstr "嗨，科斯塔斯。我不能留下来聊天。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "What can I do for you, <name_g>?"
msgstr "我能帮你什么忙吗，<name_g>？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Are there any jobs I could do?"
msgstr "有什么我可以帮忙的？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"My story?  I'm afraid it's not as gripping as the other tales around here.  "
"My father was an herbalist, my grandfather was an herbalist and - as "
"ancestral pressure would have it - I also became an herbalist.  I studied "
"from the best teachers and, through the years, a generation's knowledge "
"passed on to me.  I've spent a good portion of my life warning others of the"
" fakery that is plastic medicine and helping them rediscover the forgotten "
"beauty that lies in our surroundings.  I joined the New England Church "
"Community to express my gratitude towards the benevolence of nature.  This "
"is where it brought me."
msgstr ""
"我的故事？恐怕它不像这里的其他故事那样扣人心弦。我父亲是一名草药师，我爷爷是一名草药师，而我也成为了一名草药师。我师从最好的老师，经年累月，传授给我一代人的知识。我花了大部分时间来警告其他人当心那些塑料做的假药，并帮助他们重新发现周围被遗忘的美好事物。我加入了新英格兰教会社区，以感谢大自然的仁慈。而这它把我带到了这里。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"It's been quiet and peaceful.  Nature is recovering, and so are we.  There's"
" something bittersweet about <the_cataclysm>, isn't there?  Our species was "
"on the path of destruction, but Mother Nature spared us.  A sign of mercy "
"for a creature that did not deserve it."
msgstr ""
"这里安宁而平静。大自然正在复苏，我们也是。<the_cataclysm>有点苦乐参半，不是吗？我们这个物种正走在毁灭的道路上，但大自然宽恕了我们。这是对一个不配拥有它宽恕的生物的怜悯。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"You must be new to herbalism, no?  In short, I scavenge the land for herbs "
"to supply our humble community with medicine.  And that's just one part of "
"my job.  Say, are you interested in buying campsite gear?  I came across an "
"abandoned camp while foraging.  One can only wonder what happened to its "
"poor inhabitants…"
msgstr ""
"你对草药一定很陌生吧？简而言之，我在这片土地上寻找草药，为我们这个小社区提供药品。这只是我工作的一部分。比如说，你有兴趣购买露营装备吗？我在外出采集时发现了一个废弃营地。只能猜测它里面的可怜住户发生过些什么……"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Care to share your knowledge about herbalism?"
msgstr "能教教我你的草药知识吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"Foraging is about recognising the abundance that is around us all the time, "
"not seeking out rare species."
msgstr "采集重点要识别我们周围丰富的野生植物，而不是寻求稀有物种。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"You'll need a good book to confidently identify edible and poisonous wild "
"foods.  I'd recommend the book 'Autobiography of a Mountain Man' for "
"detailed descriptions."
msgstr "你需要一本好书才能有效识别可食用和有毒的野生植物。我推荐《山人自传》这本书，里面有详细描述。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"Never eat any wild food without first being sure of its identity.  It only "
"takes one mistake."
msgstr "在没有完全辨别之前，切勿食用任何野生植物。只需一个错误就会酿成大祸。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"The huge diversity of wild plants and fungi can be very daunting to the "
"novice forager.  Don’t be too ambitious.  Try to enjoy the learning process "
"without getting frustrated or taking risks around uncertain identifications."
msgstr "野生植物和真菌繁杂的多样性可能会让采集新手望而却步。步子不要太大。尽量享受学习过程，不要感到沮丧，也不要在辨别不明时冒险。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"I can tell you this: pine needles make the best tea.  Perhaps I'll make you "
"one someday."
msgstr "我可以告诉你：松针是最好的茶。也许有一天我会给你泡一壶。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Can I try your pine needle tea?"
msgstr "我可以尝尝你的松针茶吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Sure.  Bring me a dozen pine boughs and I'll boil you some."
msgstr "当然可以。给我一打松枝，我给你煮一些。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
msgid "I'll be back soon."
msgstr "我很快就会回来。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"This recipe is a gemstone of my family heritage.  Lucky for us that the most"
" common evergreen tree in the U.S. is non-toxic.  Start by rinsing the "
"needles, and separating any woody parts from them.  Then, cut the pine "
"needles in half.  Add one bough's worth of chopped needles to a cup or mug "
"and fill it with boiling water.  Let the needles steep for ten minutes, "
"until they turn brownish and sink down to the bottom.  As a final step, you "
"can strain the needles, but then you'd be wasting precious calories.  A "
"drink like this is perfect for mid-winter colds."
msgstr ""
"这份配方是我家学传承的一颗宝石。幸运的是，北美最常见的常青树都是无毒的。首先漂洗松针，并剔除残留的木质部分。然后，把松针切成两半。在杯子或马克杯中加入一整根松枝的碎松针，并将其灌满沸水。让松针浸泡十分钟，直到它们变成褐色并沉入底部。最后一步，你可以滤掉松针，但这样你就浪费了宝贵的卡路里。像这样的热饮非常适合治疗冬季感冒。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Thank you.  See you around, Kostas."
msgstr "谢谢你。回见，科斯塔斯。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, yeah…  I don't think he'd be a good fit for an herbalist.  He has a "
"bad habit of wandering off someplace, could get him killed one of these "
"days."
msgstr "是的，是的……我认为他不适合做草药师。他有个坏习惯，总是爱四处闲逛，这在目前的情况下总有一天会害死他自己。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"Jeremiah's a bright kid.  I'll just tell him to not wander as a stipulation."
msgstr "耶利米是个聪明的孩子。我会把这个当作约定，让他不得四处闲逛。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "I know him pretty well, I'm sure he'll learn as he goes along."
msgstr "我很了解他，我相信他会随着时间的推移学会的。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"If you don't take him under your wings, I'll rip them off for you.  Capiche?"
msgstr "如果你不把他收进你羽翼下，我会把它们都撕碎的。听明白了没？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid ""
"Alright, you've convinced me.  I'll take Jeremiah on and show him the ropes."
msgstr "好吧，你说服了我。我会教耶利米的，指点他一下。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "No, I'm still certain about this.  Jeremiah just isn't a good fit."
msgstr "不，我还是很确定。耶利米就是不太适合。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Alright.  See you around, Kostas."
msgstr "好的。回见，科斯塔斯。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "Is everyone treating you fairly?"
msgstr "大家对你还公平吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Hey <name_g>!  Nice to see you again!"
msgstr "嗨，<name_g>！很高兴再次见到你！"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"I don't think I've met you before, have I?  I'm Maria Serrano, it's nice to "
"see an new face."
msgstr "我想我以前没见过你，是吗？我是玛丽亚·塞拉诺，很高兴看到一张新面孔。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "It's a pleasure to meet you, Maria."
msgstr "很高兴认识你，玛丽亚。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Hey Maria.  What's up?"
msgstr "嗨，玛丽亚。怎么了？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Hey Maria.  I can't stay to talk right now."
msgstr "嗨，玛丽亚。我不能留下来聊天。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Could you sew something for me?"
msgstr "你能帮我缝一些东西吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "How's my order going?"
msgstr "我的订单怎么样了？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"I arrived a bit later than everyone else, I was at my studio when "
"<the_cataclysm> came.  Had to dodge a big horde of <zombies> on my way out "
"of town, totaled ny car, and hiked the rest of the way."
msgstr ""
"我比其他人晚到了些，<the_cataclysm>到来的时候我正在我的工作室里。在我出城的路上，我不得不躲开一大群<zombies>，撞坏了我的车，剩下的路都是徒步过来的。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"I always wanted to be a fashion designer when I was young.  I used to have a"
" set of dolls, and I'd make dresses for them out of spare cloth I could "
"find.  I took up sewing in high school, and I was trying to get a job with "
"Fashion Nova before <the_cataclysm> screwed that up."
msgstr ""
"我小时候一直想成为一名时装设计师。我以前有一套洋娃娃，我会用我能找到的多余布料为它们做衣服。我在高中时就开始学习缝纫，在<the_cataclysm>搞砸一切之前，我还想在Fashion"
" Nova里找份工作。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"Things are alright, could be better.  I've been mending clothes and sheets "
"ever since I arrived, fixing this and that.  Theresa's been a big help in "
"those regards, we've traded quilt patterns and designs quite a bit."
msgstr ""
"一切都很好，也许能更好。自从我来了以后，我就一直在补衣服和床单，补补这个，补补那个。特蕾莎在这方面帮了我大忙，我们互相交流了各种缝纫图样和款式。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Could you tell me about Theresa?"
msgstr "能和我说说关于特蕾莎的事情吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"She's a kind old lady, does a lot of knitting.  She could probably make you "
"something if you asked nicely."
msgstr "她是一位善良的老太太，会编织很多东西。如果你好好问问，她可能会给你做点什么。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Yeah, they are.  I just wish my work was more appreciated."
msgstr "是的，大家都很好。我只是希望我的工作能得到更多人的赞赏。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "What'll ya have?"
msgstr "你想要什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I'll have a t-shirt."
msgstr "我要一件T恤衫。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I'll have a pair of pants."
msgstr "我要一条长裤。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I'll have a jacket."
msgstr "我要一件夹克。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I'll have a dress."
msgstr "我要一件连衣裙。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I'll have a duster."
msgstr "我要一件防尘风衣。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I'll have a trench coat."
msgstr "我要一件风衣。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I'll have a backpack."
msgstr "我要一个背包。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I'll have a gambeson."
msgstr "我要一件软铠。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "What can you sew?"
msgstr "你都会缝些什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "What's the price?"
msgstr "价钱是多少？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I've been busy lately, what did you ask for again?"
msgstr "我最近很忙，你之前订什么来着？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I ordered a t-shirt."
msgstr "我订了一件T恤衫。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I ordered a pair of pants."
msgstr "我订了一条长裤。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I ordered a jacket."
msgstr "我订了一件夹克。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I ordered a dress."
msgstr "我订了一件连衣裙。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I ordered a duster."
msgstr "我订了一件防尘风衣。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I ordered a trench coat."
msgstr "我订了一件风衣。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I ordered a backpack."
msgstr "我订了一个背包。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "I ordered a gambeson."
msgstr "我订了一件软铠。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Nevermind.  Let's talk about something else."
msgstr "算了，我们谈点其他事情吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Nevermind, I have to leave."
msgstr "算了，我该走了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"I sure can!  For now, I can make t-shirts, pants, dresses, dusters, trench "
"coats, backpacks, jackets, and a gambeson; if that's your thing."
msgstr "我当然会！现在，我可以缝T恤、长裤、连衣裙、防尘风衣、风衣、背包、夹克和软铠；如果你喜欢的话。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Let's get to it."
msgstr "开始动手做吧。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"T-shirts, pants, jackets, and dresses are four icons.  Dusters, trench "
"coats, and backpacks are six icons.  A gambeson is fifteen."
msgstr "T恤、长裤、夹克和连衣裙是四个圣像。防尘风衣、风衣和背包是六个圣像。软铠要十五个。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"T-shirts, pants, jackets, and dresses take me two days.  Dusters, trench "
"coats, and backpacks take four days, while a gambeson takes six days."
msgstr "T恤、长裤、夹克和连衣裙得花两天。防尘风衣、风衣和背包得花四天。软铠得六天。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Alright, I'll get to it."
msgstr "好吧，我会开始做的。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid ""
"Here it is, I hope you enjoy it.  If you want something else, just come to "
"me."
msgstr "给你，我希望你喜欢。如果你还想要别的，来找我就行。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "I heard you were handy with computers."
msgstr "我听说你很会用电脑。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "You don't look too shabby."
msgstr "你看起来挺有范啊。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "I definitely haven't met you yet.  Nice to meet you, I'm Olwen."
msgstr "我肯定还没见过你。很高兴认识你，我是奥尔文。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "I'm just a traveler.  I won't be staying here for long."
msgstr "我只是个路人。我不会在这里呆太久。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "Hi, Olwen.  What's up?"
msgstr "嗨，奥尔文。怎么了？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "Hey, Olwen.  I can't stay to talk."
msgstr "嗨，奥尔文。我不能留下来聊天。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "You look somewhat interesting.  So, what's your story?"
msgstr "你看起来是个有意思的人。那么，你的故事是什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "I'm just a curious traveler."
msgstr "我只是一个好奇的旅行者。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "I'm seeking asylum here."
msgstr "我来这里寻求庇护。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "I'd rather not say, I gotta go."
msgstr "我不想说话，我得走了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Not many travelers come through here these days.  There's not much left to "
"wander too, besides a horde of <zombies>"
msgstr "这些天来这里的旅行者并不多。除了<zombies>尸潮，剩下会到处游荡的也不多了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "Any old port in a storm, I guess."
msgstr "我想暴风雨中，任何港口都是避难所。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid ""
"I suppose a lot of us are these days, with all the nasty things wandering "
"around.  I hope you like it here, might not be the most comfortable, but "
"it'll do for me."
msgstr "我想现在我们很多人都是这样，到处都是四处游荡的怪物。我希望你喜欢这里，也许不够舒适，但对我够用了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/TALK_valhallist_member.json
msgid "What's up?"
msgstr "怎么了？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid ""
"They're alright, I suppose.  Helena's an asshole as usual, we're low on "
"supplies, and all scared to go twenty feet outside the gate."
msgstr "我想还算可以吧。海伦娜像往常一样是个混蛋，我们的补给不足，所有人都害怕走出大门外二十英尺。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Not much too it, really.  I came here on that bus with everyone else when "
"<the_cataclysm> happened to stroll by.  I've been servicing everyone's "
"electronics since then."
msgstr "真的没什么可以说的。我和其他人一起坐公交车来到这里，<the_cataclysm>碰巧发生。从那时起，我就一直在为大伙提供电子设备服务。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "Could you tell me about your past?"
msgstr "你能告诉我你的过去吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Why not?  Oversharing is kind of my thing anyway.  Got any more interview "
"questions?"
msgstr "为什么不呢？反正过度分享算是我的弱点。还有什么面试问题吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid ""
"My dad's having a hard time letting go of the past.  Got any more interview "
"questions?"
msgstr "我爸爸对过去发生的事情还是难以忘怀。还有什么面试问题吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, I got a master's in computer science from the University of Rhode "
"Island.  Everyone around here comes to me when they want to keep their "
"computers running.  Corrie works more with the hardware portion of these "
"things; I'd recommend visiting her."
msgstr "是的，我在罗德岛大学获得了计算机科学硕士学位。这里任何想要保持电脑正常运行的人都会来找我。科里更多负责硬件相关的部分；我建议你去找找她。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "Could you teach me anything?"
msgstr "你能教我点东西吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Let's talk about getting you those trophies."
msgstr "我们谈谈那些狩猎战利品的事。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Why don't you hunt these trophies yourself?"
msgstr "你为什么不亲自去狩猎这些战利品？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Why didn't you hunt these trophies yourself?"
msgstr "你为什么不亲自去狩猎这些战利品？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Do you really need these trophies?"
msgstr "你真的需要这些狩猎战利品吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Praise the Lord, <name_g>."
msgstr "感谢上帝，<name_g>。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Greetings, <name_g><punc>  You okay?"
msgstr "你好，<name_g><punc>你还好吧？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"Huh, so it was you over there.  It's always great to see a new face.  Name's"
" Russell, Russell Connelly."
msgstr "唔，原来是你在那边。看到一张新面孔总是很棒的。我叫拉塞尔，拉塞尔·康纳利。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Russell, hey?  Nice to meet you."
msgstr "拉塞尔，是吗？很高兴见到你。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Hi, Russell.  Got a minute?"
msgstr "嗨，拉塞尔。有空吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Hey, Russell.  I can't stay to talk."
msgstr "嗨，拉塞尔。我不能留下来聊天。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"It's not often that we see new folks around the remnants of the New England "
"Community Church.  So, got any tales to share from the outside world?"
msgstr "这个新英格兰社区教会的残存周围很少有新面孔。那么，有什么外面的故事可以和我们分享吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "I'm just a curious traveler.  What's up with you?"
msgstr "只是一个好奇的旅行者。你们情况如何？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "I'm seeking asylum here.  What's up with you?"
msgstr "我来这里寻求庇护。你们情况如何？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"Who cares what's up with me?  You're the new one here.  Let me put it "
"another way: what have you seen out there?  I'm talking about the monsters "
"that lurk deep in the woods.  Have you witnessed them with your very own "
"eyes?"
msgstr "谁在乎我们怎么样了？你是新来的。让我换个说法：你在外面看到了什么？我说的是潜伏在森林深处的怪物。你亲眼目睹过吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "I wouldn't be here if I saw one.  Why do you ask?"
msgstr "要是我看到过，我就不会在这里了。你为什么这么问？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "I've seen too many things out there.  Why do you ask?"
msgstr "我在外面见过太多东西了。你为什么这么问？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"I won't let you leave just yet.  You're the new one here, I have so much to "
"ask.  Let me put it another way: what have you seen out there?  I'm talking "
"about the monsters that lurk deep in the woods.  Have you witnessed them "
"with your very own eyes?"
msgstr "我现在还不会让你离开。你是新来的，我有很多事要问。让我换个说法：你在外面看到了什么？我说的是潜伏在森林深处的怪物。你亲眼目睹过吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "I've seen too much out there.  Why do you ask?"
msgstr "我在外面见过太多东西了。你为什么这么问？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"Well, let's just say I'm interested in rare game.  I've heard stories, "
"rumors and some tall tales about otherworldly beings out there in the "
"wasteland.  That's where you come in.  I want to see the evidence, something"
" physical I can collect as a trophy collection.  You seem to have "
"experience, I was hoping you could help me."
msgstr ""
"好吧，不如说我对稀有的猎物感兴趣吧。我听过一些关于荒原上异界怪物的传说、谣言和一些荒诞的故事。而这也是你来的地方。我想看看证据，一些我可以收集作为战利品的实物。你似乎很有经验，我希望你能帮我。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Go and hunt them yourself.  You have a gun after all."
msgstr "你可以自己去狩猎它们。毕竟你有枪。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"I've got other things to deal with.  Do you really need these trophies?"
msgstr "我还有其他事情要处理。你真的需要这些狩猎战利品吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "I can help.  Anyway, how are things?"
msgstr "我可以帮忙。话说回来，这里情况如何？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
msgid "Find somebody else, dude."
msgstr "去找别人吧，兄弟。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"I've been better.  Having a hellish time keeping up with strange wildlife "
"that suddenly want us dead… hey, let's forget the world while we're talking."
"  How's life treatin' ya?"
msgstr ""
"我已经好多了。之前度过一段地狱般的时间，与那些突然想要杀死我们的奇怪野生动物近距离接触……嘿，我们在交谈时先忘了这个世界吧。你的生活怎么样？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"Look, I'm just a regular God-fearing fella like you.  You gotta have "
"something to keep your mind off stuff.  You'd get mad otherwise.  My passion"
" happens to be collecting trophies.  I appreciate your help, by the way."
msgstr ""
"听着，我只是一个和你一样的虔诚信徒。你得找些东西让自己稍稍远离这些琐事。否则你会疯掉的。而我的爱好恰好是收集战利品。顺便说一下，我很感谢你的帮助。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"Look, I'm just a regular God-fearing fella like you.  You gotta have "
"something to keep your mind off stuff.  You'd get mad otherwise.  My passion"
" happens to be collecting trophies."
msgstr "听着，我只是一个和你一样的虔诚信徒。你得找些东西让自己稍稍远离这些琐事。否则你会疯掉的。而我的爱好恰好是收集战利品。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Your life, your escape mechanism…"
msgstr "你的生活，你的逃避机制……"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"Oh it's nothing new to me.  Livin' off the land, far from everyone - it's "
"just what I'm adjusted to.  I've kept in touch with the church folks, and "
"that was enough.  I had a loyal companion back home, Betsey, my rottweiler."
"  Things have been very different since she passed away, though."
msgstr ""
"噢，这对我来说并不是什么新鲜事。生活在远离人群的地方，这正是我早就适应了的。我一直与教会的人保持联系，这就够了。我曾经在家里有一个忠实的同伴，贝西，我的罗威纳犬。不过，自从她去世后，情况就大不相同了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "What do you do now?"
msgstr "你现在做什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Could you tell me more about Betsey?"
msgstr "能和我说说更多关于贝西的事吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"I hunt with most of my time these days.  Whatever game I spot, I bag and "
"donate.  Thing is, it's getting harder and harder.  Have you also noticed "
"how corruption is slowly overtaking the natural wildlife in this God-given "
"planet?  They think the flesh is just rotten.  No, it's mutated, become "
"something else."
msgstr ""
"这些天我大部分时间都在打猎。无论我发现什么猎物，我都会干掉它，献给教会。然而情况却越来越难了。你是否也注意到，在这个上帝赐予的星球上，腐败正在慢慢征服野生动物？他们认为肉只是腐烂了。不，它变异了，变成了别的东西。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"&Russel's expression becomes somber, and he briefly stares at the wall.  "
"\"She was my dog, had her for seventeen years.  We used to go duck-hunting, "
"she'd swim out and get anything I shot.  She helped me track many a deer "
"through the woods…   When <the_cataclysm> hit, she saved me from some "
"<zombies> when we were skippin' town, but she died…  Then she came back, "
"wasn't herself…  I had to put her down.\""
msgstr ""
"&拉塞尔的表情变得阴沉，他盯着墙看了一会：“她是我的狗，养了她十七年。我们过去常去猎鸭子，她会游出去，把我射杀的猎物叼回来。她帮我在树林里追踪过无数头鹿……当<the_cataclysm>到来时，我们在小镇上滑雪，她从一群<zombies>手中救下了我，但她也死了……然后她又复活了，不再是她自己……我不得不亲手杀了她。”"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "I'm sorry for your loss.  Let's change the subject."
msgstr "我为你的损失感到难过。我们换个话题吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid "I'm sorry for your loss.  I'd better get going."
msgstr "请节哀。我得走了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"I may be more skilled or better equipped but you, my friend, have something "
"I don't: experience.  A good hunter never leaves his hunting ground.  I sure"
" ain't gonna leave it!  Now you <name_g>, you know what it's REALLY like out"
" there!"
msgstr ""
"我可能更熟练或装备更好，但我的朋友，你有我没有的东西：经验。一个好猎人从不离开他的猎场。我肯定不会离开的！而现在你，<name_g>，你知道外面变成什么样子了！"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"I hate to break it to you, but I came here because I don't want to see the "
"world."
msgstr "我不得不打破你的幻想，但我来这里是因为我不再想看到这个世界。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "I'm humbled by your words.  Well, bye."
msgstr "您谬赞了。好吧，再见。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "And I hate to break it to you, but my point still stands."
msgstr "我不得不打破你的幻想，但我的观点仍然成立。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "I'm humbled by your words.  See ya later."
msgstr "您谬赞了。好吧，回头见。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"We're all desperately holding on to our stockpiles, but I can find something"
" for you.  I have some spare hides and pelts, if you're interested in "
"buying."
msgstr "我们都在拼命维持仅剩的库存，但我可以为你找到一些东西。如果你有兴趣的话，我有一些多余的兽皮和毛皮。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Since I helped you out with your trophies, can I get a discount?"
msgstr "既然我帮你带来了这些战利品，能给我打个折吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Let's make a deal."
msgstr "让我们做个交易吧。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid ""
"I can't give a discount, but here's some meat instead.  Made by yours truly."
msgstr "我没法打折，但这里还有一些肉。由你亲爱的朋友制造。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Thank you.  What were you saying before?"
msgstr "谢谢你。你刚才说什么来着？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
msgid "Thank you.  I'll see you around, Russell."
msgstr "谢谢你。回见，拉塞尔。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid "That's a nice guitar you have."
msgstr "你这把吉他很不错。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid "Well now, good to see you again, friend."
msgstr "好了，很高兴再次见到你，朋友。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid ""
"Good to see people like you in the world.  I'm Sonia, Sonia Greene.  I "
"entertain the people."
msgstr "很高兴在世界上看到像你这样的人。我叫索尼娅，索尼娅·格林。我让大伙开心些。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid "Sonia?  Nice to meet you.  How are things here?"
msgstr "索尼娅？很高兴见到你。这里情况如何？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid "Hey Sonia.  What's up?"
msgstr "嗨，索尼娅。最近咋样？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid "Hey Sonia.  I can't stay to talk right now."
msgstr "嗨，索尼娅。我现在不能留下来聊天。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid ""
"Just playing some good ol' tunes.  There's so much negativity around here, "
"someone's gotta cheer people up, ya know?"
msgstr "只是弹一些过去的好曲子。这里有太多的负能量，总得有人让大家伙们振作起来，你知道吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid ""
"You're <swear> right.  I like its scars, makes it look like it has a "
"history, you know?  We've been through a lot.  Those pesky <zombies> forced "
"me to harm my sweet, sweet guitar, but I retaliated and bashed their heads "
"in!  I lost a part of me that day, but the guitar's alright.  Just a bit "
"rusted from all that blood and gore, that's all."
msgstr ""
"你<swear>是对的。我喜欢它的伤疤，这让它看起来像是有段历史，你知道吗？我们一起经历过很多。那些讨厌的<zombies>迫使我弄伤了我亲爱的吉他，但我报仇了，狠狠地砸碎了它们的头！那天我失去了自己的一部分，是的，但吉他没事。那些血迹让它有些锈了，只是这样。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid ""
"Now that's a wild story.  I owe my life to this kid Chloe, really.  I'll let"
" her tell the tale."
msgstr "那可真是一个疯狂的故事。我的生命真的要归功于克洛伊，这个孩子，真的。我会让她讲完这个故事。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid ""
"I was in an underground band - Taurists was our name - before all this.  "
"Performing gigs at local venues and jamming with my friends; that's all my "
"life was about.  Now, I'm a badass soloist with a war-torn guitar, a singer "
"of the old-world preserving the wonders of music and the Taurist legacy for "
"generations to come.  That's also a synonym for not having all that much "
"going on in my life."
msgstr ""
"在这一切发生之前，我是一个地下乐队的成员——金牛座是我们乐队的名字。在周边的场子演出，和朋友们一起表演；而那是我生命的全部。现在，我是一个带着饱受摧残吉他的恶棍独奏家，一个旧世界的歌手，为后世保存下音乐的奇迹和金牛座的遗产。这也是我生活中没有那么多事情发生的同义词。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid ""
"Oh, just fine.  A bit malnourished and all, but I can't really complain if "
"that's the worst of it, right?  My guitar makes our twisted little world a "
"bit more tolerable, though.  Takes my mind off stuff and muffles the screams"
" of the boogeyman, you know?"
msgstr ""
"哦，还行吧。有点营养不良，但如果只有这件事能称得上糟糕，我真的没什么好抱怨的，对吧？不过，我的吉他让这个扭曲的小世界变得更容易忍受。让把我的注意力从其他事情上移开，压制住怪兽们的尖叫，你知道吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
msgid ""
"Fairly?  There's no such thing as fairness in the world.  The NECC wouldn't "
"give a damn if I starved to death on this very bench.  At least I have "
"friends here, ones that appreciate what I do.  I make music and that's all I"
" have left, it means everything to me."
msgstr ""
"公平？这世界上从来就没有公平这回事。如果我在这张板凳上饿死，新英格兰教会也根本不在乎。至少我在这里有个朋友，能欣赏我干的活。我做音乐，这就是我仅剩的活计，它对我来说意味着一切。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Let's talk about your goals."
msgstr "我们来谈谈你的目标。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
msgid "Tell me about yourself."
msgstr "跟我说说你的情况吧。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Hey, it's you again!  Any news from the outside world?"
msgstr "嘿，又是你！有外界的消息吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Ah, another survivor!  I hope you come in peace.  I'm Tom, nice to meet you."
msgstr "啊，又一个幸存者！我希望你能平安归来。我是汤姆，很高兴认识你。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Nice to meet you, Tom."
msgstr "很高兴见到你，汤姆。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Hi Tom, got a minute?"
msgstr "嗨，汤姆。有空吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Hey, Tom.  I can't stay to talk."
msgstr "嗨，汤姆。我不能留下来聊天。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Was it difficult to find us?  We haven't seen a single soul out there for so"
" long, I'm starting to lose my hope.  So, tell me about yourself."
msgstr "找到我们非常困难吗？我们已经很久没有见到一个活人了，我都快失去希望了。所以，和我说说你自己吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "I'm just a curious traveler.  What about you, how are you doing?"
msgstr "只是一个好奇的旅行者。你呢，过得怎么样？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "I'm seeking asylum here.  What about you, how are you doing?"
msgstr "我来这里寻求庇护。你呢，过得怎么样？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Hey, that's nice of you to ask.  The people here are barely holding on.  "
"Malnutrition, sleepless nights, odd sounds from the woods, everyone turns a "
"little mad in these circumstances.  It's not their fault, I know, but they "
"did get what they wanted."
msgstr ""
"嘿，你能问我真是太好了。这里的人几乎快撑不下去了。营养不良，失眠长夜，树林发出奇怪的声音，在这种情况下，每个人都会变得有点疯狂。我知道这不是他们的错，但他们确实得到了他们想要的。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Please continue."
msgstr "请继续说。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "No rest for the weary.  See you around, Tom."
msgstr "疲惫者不能休息。回头见，汤姆。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"The sky has broken!  They received a rather passive-aggressive sign from "
"God!  The wait is finally over.  Well, not for me.  So much is left "
"unanswered, and I know for a fact the answer's out there."
msgstr "天塌了！他们从上帝那里得到了某种消极反抗的信号！等待终于结束了。好吧，对我来说不是。还有很多问题没有答案，我知道答案就在那里。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Perhaps it's not worth finding out."
msgstr "也许这不值得一探究竟。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Try not to get stuck in the past.  See you around, Tom."
msgstr "尽量不要陷入过去。回头见，汤姆。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Perhaps.  You don't wanna think about the stuff I'm thinking about, it would"
" spiral a newbie independent thinker into madness.  I don't blame you for "
"saying that."
msgstr "也许吧。你可别去想我所在想的事情，这会让一个刚刚学会独立思考的新人陷入疯狂。你会这么说我一点都不奇怪。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"I'm currently in the middle of solving a pointless mystery for my own "
"entertainment.  Of course I have time!"
msgstr "我目前正在自娱自乐尝试解决一个毫无意义的谜团。我当然有时间！"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Sorry Tom, I can't stay to chat."
msgstr "抱歉，汤姆。我没空留下来聊天。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"I haven't got a story.  I'm an independent thinker.  Living out here, away "
"from the Man."
msgstr "我没有故事。我是一个独立思考的思想家。住在这里，远离人类。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"I was nobody but an ordinary office drone.  Lived the average suburban life,"
" prepping for the inevitable.  Had the bright idea of purchasing a Last Man "
"On Earth shelter, but I decided to settle for less when I found out it cost "
"five times my annual salary.  That's how I ended up in a religious "
"campground with my family and a survival kit."
msgstr ""
"我只是一个普通的办公室工蜂。过着普通的郊区生活，为不可避免之事做准备。我曾经有过购买“地球上最后一个人”庇护所的好主意，但当我发现它的花费是我年薪的五倍时，我决定花费更少的钱。这就是我和我的家人以及全套生存装备一起来到这个宗教露营地的原因。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"All of us are here; me, Felicity, and Olwen.  We're so <swear> lucky, I feel"
" like crying tears of joy every time I see them."
msgstr "我们都在这里；我、费利西蒂和奥尔文。我们太<swear>幸运了，每次看到他们，我都想高兴地流泪。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Could you tell me about Felicity?"
msgstr "能和我说说关于费利西蒂的事情吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Could you tell me about Olwen?"
msgstr "能和我说说关于奥尔文的事情吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"She's my wife, we've been married for a while now.  We used to live in Rhode"
" Island, worked at a publishing firm, Stillwater.  She's always wanted to be"
" a writer, that's why we moved away.  We've been a bit distant as of late, I"
" don't think she's taking the \"whole end-of-the-world\" thing too well."
msgstr ""
"她是我的妻子，我们结婚有一段时间了。我们过去住在罗德岛，在一家出版公司 Stillwater "
"工作。她一直想成为一名作家，这就是我们搬走的原因。我们最近有点疏远了，我不认为她对“世界末日”有足够的理解。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Olwen's a bright girl; she's fiddled with electronics and computers since "
"she was in high school.  She got a master's in it from the University of "
"Rhode Island.  Felicity's been a good mother for her, always been there for "
"us.  Olwen might be able to teach you a few things, she should be around "
"here somewhere."
msgstr ""
"奥尔文是个聪明的女孩；她从高中起就喜欢摆弄电子设备和电脑。她获得了罗德岛大学的硕士学位。费利西蒂一直是她的好母亲，一直在我们身边。奥尔文也许能教你一些东西，她应该在这里的某个地方。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"New England Church Community is what they're called.  My wife was the first "
"in the family to come in contact with 'em.  She joined because of their "
"charity work and as for myself, well… you know why I was there.  Let me tell"
" you, being surrounded by like-minded folks was like a breath of fresh air."
"  Even if the only belief we shared was paranoia, but you get what I'm "
"saying.  I tried everything to prep my family for the inevitable, I really "
"did, but in the end it wasn't me who saved us all."
msgstr ""
"新英格兰教会社区，他们就是这么称呼自己的。我妻子是家里第一个和他们接触的人。她加入是因为他们的慈善工作，至于我，嗯……你知道我为什么在这里。让我告诉你，被志同道合的人包围就像呼吸新鲜空气。即使我们唯一的共同信念是偏执，但你明白我的意思。我想尽一切办法让我的家人为不可避免之事做好准备，我真的做到了，但最终救下了我们全家人的并不是我。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"I want to find out the truth and preserve the past for the following "
"generation, so that they'll know some of what <swear> happened."
msgstr "我想找出真相，为下一代人保留过去，这样他们就会知道<swear>发生了什么。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Any progress?"
msgstr "有什么进展吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Sounds like an ambitious project.  Is there anything I can do to help you "
"out?"
msgstr "听起来像是一个雄心勃勃的大工程。我能帮你什么忙吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Good luck with that.  See you around, Tom."
msgstr "祝你好运。回头见，汤姆。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"So far?  Not so great.  Now that the Internet is down, I don't know.  Such "
"abundant hidden information - all gone!"
msgstr "目前为止，不太妙。现在互联网已经瘫痪了，我也不知道怎么办。如此丰富的隐藏信息——全都没了！"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "Try not to glorify the past.  See you around, Tom."
msgstr "尽量不要美化过去。回头见，汤姆。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"Of course!  Just put all your literary findings on that chair over there.  "
"Remember, you're not only doing a favor for me, but for all of humanity as "
"well.  World heritage is what we're talking about!  I managed to get my "
"hands on a book called 'Zombie Survial Guide' while, uh… dumpster diving.  "
"Imagine how much this book alone reveals about our pre-Cataclysm culture!  "
"Oh boy, how wrong we were about everything."
msgstr ""
"当然了！把你所有的文学发现放在那边的椅子上。记住，你不仅是在帮我的忙，也是在帮全人类的忙。我们谈论的是世界遗产！我设法弄到了一本叫做《丧尸生存指南》的书，在我呃……打扫垃圾桶的时候。想象一下，单是这本书就能揭示了我们大灾变前的文化！天啊，我们把一切事情都想错了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid "I mean, can I help with the research?"
msgstr "我的意思是，我可以帮助研究吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
msgid ""
"No no no no no!  Thinking is one of the only thing I have left and you can't"
" take that away from me.  But, If you *really* want to make yourself useful,"
" relevant newspapers would help me piece out the puzzle."
msgstr "不不不不！思考是我仅存的东西之一，你不能把它从我身上抢走。但是，如果你*真心*想让自己变得有用，相关的报纸会帮我解开这个谜题。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/TALK_FORGE_MERCHANT.json
msgid "Delivering <topic_item>."
msgstr "提供<topic_item>。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "Why don't you blow this joint and come with me?"
msgstr "你为什么不抽了这根大烟和我一起飞？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "I got my rights to be here, chum.  Squatter's rights!"
msgstr "我有权在这里，朋友。擅自占有权！"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "Don't worry, I'm not going to hurt you."
msgstr "别担心，我不打算伤害你。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid ""
"I got here first, therefore this place belongs to me.  Them's the rules in "
"the <the_cataclysm>."
msgstr "我先到的，所以这个地方属于我。这就是<the_cataclysm>的规则。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "Now that's an archaic belief.  I'll see you around."
msgstr "这可真是一个过时的信仰。回头见。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid ""
"I ain't leaving, bruv.  Not until that eldritch screechin' nightmare is dead"
" 'n buried."
msgstr "我不会离开的，兄弟。直到那个恶魔尖叫的梦魇被埋葬。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "What nightmare?"
msgstr "什么梦魇？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "I'll see you around then."
msgstr "那我们回头见了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid ""
"That ain't the point here, chum.  Don'tcha get it?  This was MY territory, "
"but they took it away from me.  Now they think of us as nothin' but a "
"<swear> nuisance."
msgstr "这不是重点，哥们。你不明白吗？这是我的地盘，但他们把它夺走了。现在他们认为我们只是个<swear>讨厌鬼。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid ""
"Who I was is gone, dead… died when I put down the monsters wearing the face "
"of my friends.  Ever since then, I've felt nothing but disgust for myself.  "
"Let's not <swear> reminisce."
msgstr "曾经的那个我已经没了，死了……当我干掉戴着我朋友脸的怪物时就已经死了。从那以后，我只对自己感到厌恶。别<swear>回忆了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid ""
"They are nice people, lettin' us stay here 'n all.  I got friends here, and "
"while we may not be members we belong here.  We'll fight together if they "
"ever try to kick us out."
msgstr "他们都是好人，让我们呆在这里。我在这里有朋友，虽然我们还不是教会成员，但我们属于这里。如果他们想把我们踢出去，我们会团结起来和他们打一架。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid ""
"It ain't so bad.  I got shelter, heat, and people to defend me if any "
"<zombie> shuffles its way in here.  If I want to eat then I'll be doin' "
"construction work all day."
msgstr "没那么糟。我有庇护所，有暖气，如果有那个<zombie>敢来这里的话，也有人保护我。如果我想混口饭吃，我可以从早到晚当建筑工。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid ""
"Food is just the thing a starving man needs.  Thanks for the help, <name_g>."
msgstr "食物正是饥饿的人所需要的。谢谢你的帮助，<name_g>。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid ""
"Ha ha ha!  Think before you speak, chum.  Eight icons for an honest day's "
"work, I say the system's broken!"
msgstr "哈哈哈！说话前先想一想，老兄。八个圣像能换一整天诚实的工作，想想可不可能吧！"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid ""
"Ain't you heard it?  It's been screeching out in the forest during the night"
" for a while now, keeps me up sometimes.  I'm too scared to go out and see "
"what that thing is.  If you'd kill it, I'd be in your debt forever."
msgstr "你没听到吗？夜里总有东西在森林里发出尖叫，有时让我睡不着。我太害怕了，不敢出去看看那是什么东西。如果你杀了它，我会永远记住你的恩情。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_shopkeep.json
msgid "I'll see what I can do."
msgstr "我看看能做些什么。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid ""
"I'm sorry to hear that <name_g>, but I don't feel like facing it either."
msgstr "听到这个消息我很抱歉，<name_g>，但我也不想面对它。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid ""
"After what you did for me, I'll follow you to the ends of the Earth!  No one"
" around here's stood up for me like that, I owe ya one."
msgstr "在你为我做了这一切之后，我会跟随你到天涯海角！这里没有人这样支持我，我欠你一个人情。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid ""
"No chance!  Its not you, its the world out there I'm worried about.  All "
"those <swear> monsters really give me the creeps, and as far as I know this "
"church is the last bastion of humanity in the <the_cataclysm>."
msgstr ""
"门都没有！我担心的不是你，而是外面的世界。所有这些<swear>怪物真的让我毛骨悚然，据我所知，这座教堂是<the_cataclysm>世界上人类的最后堡垒。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/godco/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
msgid "That's understandable."
msgstr "可以理解。"

#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/godco/classes.json
msgid "Leader"
msgstr "领袖"

#. ~ Job description of "Leader" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/godco/classes.json
msgid "I am the leader of the New England Church Community."
msgstr "我是新英格兰教会社区的领袖。"

